iyalur District.\n...Petitioner/Appellant/\nAccused\nVs\nThe State Rep. by,\nThe Inspector of Police,\nAriyalur Police Station,\nAriyalur District.\nCrime No.2 of 2025.\n...Respondent/\nComplainant\nPrayer : Criminal Miscellaneous Petition filed under Section 430(1) of\nBNSS, 2023 praying to suspend the sentence imposed in Judgement\npassed by the Learned Additional District and Sessions Court, Ariyalur in\nSC.No.73 of 2025 dated 31.07.2026 and enlarge the Petitioner on bail\npending disposal of the above appeal.\n__________\n\nCRL MP No.16662 of 2026\nin\nCrl.A.No.1101 of 2026\nFor Petitioner : Mr.P.Muthamizhselvakumar\nFor Respondent : Ms.Sharada Vivek\nAdditional Public Prosecutor\nORDER\nThe Criminal Appeal challenges the Judgment passed in S.C.No.73\nof 2025 by the learned Additional District and Sessions Judge, Ariyalur,\nholding the petitioner guilty of the offences under Sections 115(2) of\nBNS and 4 of TNPHW Act 2022 (3 counts) and sentencing him to\nundergo one year of SI for the offence under Section 115(2) of BNS and\nto undergo two years of RI (each) and to pay a fine of Rs.10,000/- i/d to\nundergo three months of SI (each) for the offence under Section 4 of\nTNPHW Act 2022 (3 counts) .\n2. Aggrieved by the same, the petitioner has preferred\nCrl.A.No.1101 of 2026 before this Court along with the instant criminal\nmiscellaneous petition.\n3. The learned counsel for the petitioner would submit that a fixed\nsentence of imprisonment has been imposed on the petitioner; that the\npetitioner has raised substantial grounds in the appeal; and that the\npetitioner has prayed for suspension of sentence pending disposal of the\nappeal.\n__________\n\nCRL MP No.16662 of 2026\nin\nCrl.A.No.1101 of 2026\n4. Heard the learned Additional Public Prosecutor and perused the\nmaterials available on record.\n5. The trial Court had suspended the sentence for a period of one\nmonth. Considering the fact that the petitioner/appellant has raised\nsubstantial grounds in the appeal and the appeal is not likely to be taken\nup in the near future, this Court is inclined to grant the relief of\nsuspension of sentence to the petitioner.\n6. Accordingly, this criminal miscellaneous petition stands\nallowed, and the sentence imposed on the petitioner is suspended till the\ndisposal of the above criminal appeal, and the petitioner is ordered to be\nreleased on bail on the following conditions:\n(a).The petitioner shall execute a bond for a sum\nof Rs.10,000/- (Rupees Ten Thousand only), with two\nsureties, each for a like sum to the satisfaction of the\nlearned Additional District and Sessions Judge,\nAriyalur;\n(b).The petitioner and the sureties shall affix their\nphotographs and Left Thumb Impression in the surety\nbond and the Trial Court may obtain a copy of their\nAadhar card or Bank pass Book and mobile numbers to\nensure their identity;\n__________\n\nCRL MP No.16662 of 2026\nin\nCrl.A.No.1101 of 2026\n(c).The petitioner shall appear before the\nrespondent police once in fifteen days and before the\nTrial Court on the first working day of every month at\n10.30 a.m. until the disposal of the appeal and if he is\nnot able to appear before the Trial Court on any day, he\nshall make arrangements to file an application under\nSection 317 Cr.P.C. and shall appear before the Trial\nCourt on any other day in lieu of the date of his\nabsence, as directed by the Trial Court.\n09-10-2026\nIndex: Yes/No\nSpeaking/Non-speaking order\nNeutral Citation: Yes/No\nIssue Order Copy Today.\ndk\nTo\n1. The Additional District and Sessions Judge,\nAriyalur.\n2. The Inspector of Police\nAriyalur Police Station,\nAriyalur District.\n3. The Public Prosecutor,\nHigh Court, Madras.\n__________\n\nCRL MP No.16662 of 2026\nin\nCrl.A.No.1101 of 2026\nSUNDER MOHAN J.\ndk\nCRL MP No. 16662 of 2026\nin\nCRL A No. 1101 of 2026\n09-10-2026\n__________	5	t	HCMA010011012026	Criminal Appeal	2026-10-09	Single Bench	Pannu Marimuthu	The State Rep. by, The Inspector of Police, Ariyalur Police Station, Ariyalur District.	Mr.P.Muthamizhselvakumar	Ms.Sharada Vivek Additional Public Prosecutor	Civil Law	In this judgment under Civil Law, the Court ruled on the dispute between 24 Crl-Mp-16662-2026 and the Respondent.	0	2026 LexGuard (Judg) 0249F2	{"court": "Madras High Court (Principal Seat, Chennai)", "title": "Marimuthu @ Pannu Marimuthu v. State Rep. by Inspector of Police, Ariyalur", "case_id": "0249f2b0-2623-4794-ab39-7fa38f653e0f", "case_no": "Crl.A.No.1101 of 2026", "parties": "Marimuthu @ Pannu Marimuthu v. State Rep. by Inspector of Police, Ariyalur", "category": "BAIL_SUSPENSION", "petitioner": "Marimuthu @ Pannu Marimuthu", "respondent": "State Rep. by Inspector of Police, Ariyalur", "legal_domain": "Civil Law", "category_facts": {"category": "BAIL_SUSPENSION", "surety_count": 2, "custody_period": null, "application_type": "Suspension of Sentence", "bail_bond_amount": 10000.0, "trial_court_fine": 10000.0, "reason_for_relief": "Substantial grounds raised in appeal", "reporting_condition": "appear before the Trial Court on any day, he", "trial_court_sentence": "undergo one year of SI for the offence under Section 115(2) of BNS and", "trial_court_fine_paid": true}, "activity_events": ["petition under section 430"], "profile_version": "2.5", "statutory_matrix": [{"act": "BNSS", "section": "430", "canonical": "Section 430 BNSS", "equivalents": ["Section 389 CrPC"]}], "activity_clusters": ["appellate_motion"], "scenario_clusters": ["appellate_conviction"], "scenario_keywords": ["simple imprisonment"], "procedural_posture": {"remedy": "Allowed", "disposition": "Allowed"}}
