uise of enquiry against the\npetitioners and their family members based on the false complaints given by the\n3rd respondent and his inmates.\n1/4\n\nCrl.OP(MD) No.14113 of 2026\nFor Petitioners : Mr.R.Babu Jaganath\nFor Respondents : Mr.B.Arun\nGovernment Advocate (Crl.Side)\nfor R1, R2\nORDER\nThe present petition has been filed by the petitioners seeking a\ndirection as against the second respondent Police not to harass the petitioners\nunder the guise of enquiry.\n2.It could be seen through the records that an FIR has been\nregistered as against the petitioners in Cr.No.58 of 2026 on 16.04.2026 ror the\nalleged offence under Sections 324(4), 191(2), 115(2), 118(1), 351(3) of BNS.\n3.A perusal of the FIR reveals that there was a dispute arising out\nassembly elections. Since the petitioners have not been arrested so far, there\nshall be a direction to the second respondent police to issue summons under\nSection 35(3) of BNSS (corresponding to Section 41A of Cr.P.C) and thereafter,\nproceed in accordance with law.\n2/4\n\nCrl.OP(MD) No.14113 of 2026\n4.With the aforesaid observations, this Criminal Original Petition\nstands disposed of.\n13.07.2026\nNCC : Yes/No\nIndex : Yes/No\nInternet: Yes/No\nPNM\nTo\n1.The Superintendent of Police\nRamanathapuram District.\n2. The Inspector of Police,\nPamban Police Station,\nRamanathapuram District. Crime No.57/2026.\n3.The Additional Public Prosecutor,\nMadurai Bench of Madras High Court, Madurai.\n3/4\n\nCrl.OP(MD) No.14113 of 2026\nR.VIJAYAKUMAR , J .\nPNM\nORDER MADE IN\nCrl.OP.(MD)No.14113 of 2026\n13.07.2026\n4/4	4	t	HCMA010141132026	Criminal Original Petition	2026-07-13	Single Bench	. Mahinth ... Petitioners	State of Tamil Nadu & Ors.	Mr.R.Babu Jaganath	Mr.B.Arun Government Advocate (Crl.Side)	Civil Law	In this judgment under Civil Law, the Court ruled on the dispute between 1Eubyodalkut5Eobjocqck-9Pqszll5O  Home   Judgements And Orders, Supreme Court And High Courts Of India and the Respondent.	0	2026 LexGuard (Judg)