g before the learned Chief\nMetropolitan Magistrate, Kolkata arising out of Shakeshpeare\nSarani P.S. Case No.157 of 2025 under Sections 61 (2), 316 (2),\n318 (4), 338, 339, 340 (2), 351 (2) BNS.\n4. This is an application seeking transit anticipatory bail.\n5. Considering the nature of allegation and the recitals in the\nABLAPL, it is directed that the Petitioner shall surrender before\nthe learned Chief Metropolitan Magistrate, Kolkata on or before\nPage 1 of 2.\n\n30.11.2026 in connection with Shakeshpeare Sarani P.S. Case\nNo.356 of 2026 and seek redressal in accordance with law.\n6. Till 30.11.2026, the Petitioner shall not be taken into custody\nin connection with the aforementioned case subject to any other\norder passed by Court(s) of competent Jurisdiction.\nIn the event the Petitioner fails to appear on or before\n30.11.2026 and/or subject to any other order passed by Court(s) of\ncompetent jurisdiction, it shall be open for the Investigating\nAgency to proceed in accordance with law.\n6. Accordingly, the ABLAPL stands disposed of.\n( A.K. Mohapatra)\nVacation Judge\nMadhu/Sisir\nPage 2 of 2.	2	t	ODHC010767442026	Judicial Precedent	2026-10-23	Single Bench	in connection with Shakeshpeare Sarani P.S. Case	1) STATE OF ODISHA ..... Opposite Parties 2) PRATEEK MISHRA Represented by Adv	\N	\N	Civil & Constitutional Law	In this matter, the High Court of Orissa at Cuttack adjudicated issues between Represented by Adv. - Atmajit Manmith Das and 1) STATE OF ODISHA ..... Opposite Parties 2) PRATEEK MISHRA Represented by Adv. The Court rendered a decision disposing of the application under statutory provisions.	0	2026 LexGuard (OHC) 0D445DD3	{"court": "High Court of Orissa at Cuttack", "title": "Represented by Adv. - Atmajit Manmith Das v. 1) STATE OF ODISHA ..... Opposite Parties 2) PRATEEK MISHRA Represented by Adv", "case_id": "0d445dd3-8ea1-4c05-baf3-bbac2738d04c", "case_no": "NO. 12130 of 2026", "parties": "Represented by Adv. - Atmajit Manmith Das v. 1) STATE OF