of 2026 arising\nout of Habra Police Station Case No.119 of 2026 dated 08.03.2026\nunder Sections 21(c)/29 of the NDPS Act and Sections\n303(2)/317(2) of Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023;\nAnd\nIn Re: Kamal Krishna Biswas alias Sona alias Kajal and others\n… Petitioners\nMr. Angshuman Chakraborty, Adv.\nMr. S. S. Saha, Adv.\n…For Petitioners\nMr. Ranjan Chakraborty, Adv.\nMr. Subrata Mukherjee, Adv.\nMs. Sanjana Jha, Adv.\n…For State\n1. The petitioners and the State are represented by learned\nAdvocates.\n2. On behalf of the petitioners, it is submitted that considering the\nfact that only 26.065 kg of ganja was recovered from the joint\npossession of the present three accused petitioners and also\nconsidering the fact that investigation has already been\ncompleted, the instant application for bail may be considered\nfavourably.\n3. While opposing the prayer for bail learned Advocate appearing on\nbehalf of the respondent State draws attention of this Court to the\nstatus report as submitted by the concerned SI. It is further\nsubmitted that the present petitioners have so many criminal\nantecedents.\n\n[2]\n4. On careful perusal of the entire materials as placed before this\nCourt, it appears that commercial quantity of contraband was\nseized from the accused petitioners. It further appears that so\nmany criminal antecedents of similar such offences are there\nagainst the present petitioners.\n5. Considering the entire circumstances, prayer for bail is rejected.\n6. Urgent photostat certified copy of the order, if applied for, be\ngiven to the parties, upon usual undertakings.\n(PARTHA SARATHI SEN, J.)	2	t	HCMA010023142026	Bail Application (NDPS)	\N	Single Bench	Kamal Krishna Biswas alias Sona alias Kajal & Others	State of West Bengal	Mr. Ranjan Chakraborty, Adv.	\N	Civil Law	In this judgment under Criminal Law, the Court ruled on the dispute between Kamal Krishna Biswas alias Sona alias Kajal & Others and State of West Bengal.	0	2026 LexGuard (Judg) 058E81	{"court":