 Advocate (Crl. Side) for R-2\nPrayer:\nTo cancel the bail granted by the Judicial Magistrate, Theni by impugned\norder dated 16.06.2026 in Crl.M.P.No.1623 of 2026, continue his committal in\ncutody.\nORDER\nThe defacto complainant in Crime No.1 of 2026 has come forward with this\npetition seeking cancellation of bail granted to the first respondent by the learned\nJudicial Magistrate, Theni, in Crl.M.P.No.1623 of 2026 dated 16.06.2026.\nhttps://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis\n\n--- PAGE 2 ---\n2. The learned counsel for the petitioner submits that some of the accused,\nwho are absconding in this case, are threatening the defacto complainant. He\nfurther submitted that the amount involved in this case is huge and it has not been\nproperly considered by the learned Magistrate while granting bail and hence,\ncancellation of bail granted to the first respondent would render justice.\n3. The learned Government Advocate (Crl. Side) appearing for the second\nrespondent reported that though the learned Judicial Magistrate has granted bail to\nthe first respondent, he was not released on bail and he is remanded in judicial\ncustody in another case. It is further stated that some of the accused are still\nabsconding.\n4. I have also gone through the order passed by the learned Magistrate in\nCrl.M.P.No.1623 of 2026 dated 16.06.2026. On careful perusal of the same, it\nreveals that the first respondent was released on default bail and it is a statutory\nbail and the same could not be cancelled on consideration of any merits at this\nstage of the case. Hence, this Court finds no infirmity in the order passed by the\nlearned Magistrate by exercising powers under Section 187(3) of BNSS and this\nCourt finds no merits in this petition.\n5. Accordingly, this Criminal Original Petition is dismissed.\n08-07-2026\nLm\nhttps://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis\n\n--- PAGE 3 ---\nTo\n1.The Judicial Magistrate,\nTheni.\n2.The Inspector of Police,\nDistrict Crime Branch Police Station,\nTheni District.\n3.The Additional Public Prosecutor,\nMadurai Bench of Madras High Court.\nhttps://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis\n\n--- PAGE 4 ---\nK.RAJASEKAR, J.\nLm\nCrl.O.P.(MD).No.13429 of 2026\n08.07.2026\nhttps://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis	4	t	HCMA010134292026	Criminal Original Petition (Bail)	2026-07-08	Single Bench	M.Santhi	Shanmugasundaram & State Rep. by Inspector of Police, Theni	Mr.M.Uthayasuriyan	Mr.J.Vishnu Government Advocate (Crl. Side) for R-2	Civil Law	In this judgment under Civil Law, the Court ruled on the dispute between 1Nnsjucuq1J6Esubcdtcgeaex3Sa51731 Home   Judgements And Orders, Supreme Court And High Courts Of India and the Respondent.	0	2026 LexGuard (Judg) 1C37D2	{"court": "Madras High Court (Principal Seat, Chennai)", "title": "M.Santhi v. Shanmugasundaram & State", "case_id": "1c37d289-8334-46bc-87fb-e8bc73d3a3c7", "case_no": "CRL OP(MD) NO. 13429 of 2026", "parties": "M.Santhi v. Shanmugasundaram & State", "category": "BAIL_SUSPENSION", "petitioner": "M.Santhi", "respondent": "Shanmugasundaram & State Rep. by Inspector of Police, Theni", "legal_domain": "Civil Law", "category_facts": {"category": "BAIL_SUSPENSION", "surety_count": null, "custody_period": null, "application_type": "Default Bail", "bail_bond_amount": null, "trial_court_fine": null, "reason_for_relief": null, "reporting_condition": null, "trial_court_sentence": null, "trial_court_fine_paid": false}, "activity_events": [], "profile_version": "2.5", "statutory_matrix": [], "activity_clusters": [], "scenario_clusters": [], "scenario_keywords": [], "procedural_posture": {"remedy": "Allowed", "disposition": "Allowed"}}
