AYER : For Bail in connection with the case in\nP.R.C.No.53 of 2026 before the Judicial Magistrate,\nKaraikudi, Sivagangai District, in Crime No.124 of\n2026 on the file of the Respondent Police.\n1/6\nhttps://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis\nCRL OP(MD). No.23258 of 2026\nORDER : The Court made the following order :-\nThe petitioners / accused 2 and 3, who are facing\na case for the offences punishable under Sections 49,\n191(2), 191(3), 126(2), 296(b), 115(2), 118(1), 109\nand 351(3) BNS, in P.R.C.No.53 of 2026, on the file\nof the Judicial Magistrate, Karaikudi, Sivagangai\nDistrict, in Crime No.124 of 2026, on the file of the\nrespondent police, seek bail.\n2. The case of the prosecution is that due to\nprevious enmity, on 08.07.2026, the petitioners along\nwith other accused abused the defacto complainant in\nfilthy language and attacked him with empty beer\nbottle. Hence, the complaint.\n3. No doubt, the petitioners' earlier petition\nfor bail in Crl.O.P(MD)No.17720 of 2026 came to be\ndismissed by this Court vide order dated 18.08.2026.\n4. The learned counsel appearing for the\npetitioners would submit that the petitioners are\ninnocent and they have not committed any offence as\n2/6\nhttps://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis\nCRL OP(MD). No.23258 of 2026\nalleged by the prosecution. He would further submit\nthat the fifth accused was granted anticipatory bail\nby the Sessions Court in Crl.M.P.No.1724 of 2026 on\n20.07.2026 and two other accused were released on\nbail by the Sessions Court in Crl.M.P.Nos.1830 and\n1665 of 2026 on 29.07.2026 and 15.07.2026, that\nsubsequent to the dismissal of the earlier bail\npetition, charge sheet came to be filed and the first\naccused was granted bail by the Principal Sessions\nCourt in Crl.M.P.No.2290 of 2026 on 03.09.2026 and\nthat the petitioner is in judicial custody from\n10.07.2026.\n5. The learned Additional Public Prosecutor\nappearing for the respondent police would submit that\nthere are totally eight accused in this case and the\npetitioners are arrayed accused 2 and 3 and that the\nfirst petitioner is having 12 previous cases and the\nsecond petitioner is having 19 previous cases and\nthey are history-sheeted persons.\n6. Considering the above facts and circumstances\n3/6\nhttps://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis\nCRL OP(MD). No.23258 of 2026\nand taking note of the fact that the petitioners are\nin judicial custody from 10.07.2026 and also the\nfacts that after completing the investigation, charge\nsheet came to be filed and that the first accused was\ngranted bail by the Principal Sessions Court, this\nCourt is inclined to grant bail to the petitioners\nsubject to the following conditions:\n7. Accordingly, the petitioners are ordered to\nbe released on bail on their executing a bond for a\nsum of Rs.25,000/- (Rupees Twenty Five Thousand only)\neach with two sureties each for a like sum to the\nsatisfaction of the learned Judicial Magistrate,\nKaraikudi, Sivagangai District, and on further\nconditions that:\n(i)the sureties shall affix their photographs\nand left thumb impression in the surety bond and the\nMagistrate / concerned court may obtain a copy of\ntheir Aadhar card or Bank Pass Book to ensure their\nidentity;\n(ii)the petitioners shall stay at Viluppuram and\nreport before the Inspector of Police, Viluppuram\nTown Police Station, Viluppuram, daily at 10.30 a.m.,\n4/6\nhttps://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis\nCRL OP(MD). No.23258 of 2026\nfor a period of thirty (30) days and thereafter,\nbefore the committal Court at 10.30 a.m., for a\nperiod of fifteen (15) days;\n(iii)the petitioners shall not tamper with the\nevidence or witness either during investigation or\ntrial;\n(iv)the petitioners shall not abscond either\nduring investigation or trial;\n(v)On breach of any of the aforesaid conditions,\nthe learned Magistrate / Trial Court is entitled to\ntake appropriate action against the petitioners in\naccordance with law as if the conditions have been\nimposed and the petitioners are released on bail by\nthe learned Magistrate / Trial Court himself as laid\ndown by the Hon'ble Supreme Court in P.K.Shaji vs.\nState of Kerala [(2005)AIR SCW 5560];\n(vi)If the accused thereafter abscond, a fresh\nFIR can be registered under Section 269 BNS, 2023.\n(K M S J)\n12.10.2026\nCSM\n5/6\nhttps://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis\nCRL OP(MD). No.23258 of 2026\nK.MURALI SHANKAR,J\nCSM\nTO\n1. The Judicial Magistrate,\nKaraikudi, Sivagangai District.\n2. Do through\nThe Chief Judicial Magistrate,\nSivagangai.\n3. The Officer-in-Charge,\nSub Jail, Sivagangai,\nSivagangai District.\n4. The Inspector of Police,\nKaraikudi South Police Station,\nSivagangai District.\n5. The Inspector of Police,\nViluppuram Town Police Station,\nViluppuram.\n6. The Additional Public Prosecutor,\nMadurai Bench of Madras High Court,\nMadurai.\nORDER\nIN\nCRL OP(MD) No.23258 of 2026\nDate : 12.10.2026\n6/6\nhttps://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis	6	t	HCMD010232582026	Criminal Original Petition (Bail)	\N	Single Bench	Naveen & Praveen	State Rep. by Inspector of Police, Karaikudi South	Mr.UM.Berdin Vinodh,	Mr.T.Lenin Kumar, Additional Public Prosecutor	Civil Law	In this criminal original petition under Criminal Law, the Court ruled on the dispute between . No.23258 of 2026 1.Naveen 2.Praveen and ..	0	2026 LexGuard (Crim) 1DDE56	{"court": "Madras High Court (Madurai Bench)", "title": "Naveen & Praveen v. State Rep. by Inspector of Police, Karaikudi South", "case_id": "1dde5609-5e9a-4e20-99ca-b9d216af74a8", "case_no": "CRL OP(MD). No.23258 of 2026", "parties": "Naveen & Praveen v. State Rep. by Inspector of Police, Karaikudi South", "category": "BAIL_SUSPENSION", "petitioner": "Naveen & Praveen", "respondent": "State Rep. by Inspector of Police, Karaikudi South", "legal_domain": "Civil Law", "category_facts": {"category": "BAIL_SUSPENSION", "surety_count": 2, "custody_period": null, "application_type": "Anticipatory Bail", "bail_bond_amount": 25000.0, "trial_court_fine": null, "reason_for_relief": null, "reporting_condition": "report before the Inspector of Police, Viluppuram", "trial_court_sentence": null, "trial_court_fine_paid": false}, "activity_events": [], "profile_version": "2.5", "statutory_matrix": [], "activity_clusters": [], "scenario_clusters": [], "scenario_keywords": [], "procedural_posture": {"remedy": "Disposed of with directions.", "disposition": "Disposed of with directions."}}
