n\nSECTIONS & PROVISIONS:\nCrPC Section 125, BNSS Section 144, CrPC Section 397\n\nKEY TOPICS & ISSUES:\nMaintenance, Section 125 CrPC, Standard of Living, Income Tax Returns, Financial Capacity\n\n================================================================================\n                                   JUDGMENT\n================================================================================\n\n1. FACTS OF THE CASE:\nHusband, earning Rs. 1.2 Lakhs as government school headmaster, neglected wife and daughter. Trial court granted meager Rs. 6,000.\n\n2. ISSUES FRAMED:\nWhat is the quantum benchmark for maintenance under Section 125 CrPC / 144 BNSS relative to husband's net salary?\n\n3. LEGAL RATIO & FINDINGS:\nWife and children are entitled to live with identical socioeconomic dignity and comfort enjoyed in the matrimonial household.\n\n4. FINAL ORDER:\nCriminal Revision Allowed; Maintenance enhanced from Rs. 6,000 to Rs. 22,000 per month reflecting husband's IT returns.\n\nOrdered and decreed accordingly.\n\nHon'ble Justice B. Pugalendhi\nMadras High Court (Madurai Bench)\n[LEXGUARD REPOSITORY CRYPTOGRAPHIC SEAL]\n	3	t	HCMD010003402026	Criminal Revision Case	\N	Single Bench	Selvi & Minor Daughter	K. Rajendran	\N	\N	Civil Law	In this criminal revision case under Criminal Law, the Court ruled on the dispute between Selvi & Minor Daughter and K. Rajendran.	0	2026 LexGuard (Crim) D7EEAD	{"court": "Madras High Court (Madurai Bench)", "title": "Selvi & Minor Daughter v. K. Rajendran", "case_id": "d7eead5e-6969-4ae5-9b5c-54a71a9345ba", "case_no": "Crl.R.C.(MD) No. 340 of 2026", "parties": "Selvi and Minor Daughter Kaviya", "category": "GENERAL_CONSTITUTIONAL", "petitioner": "Selvi & Minor Daughter", "respondent": "K. Rajendran", "legal_domain": "Civil Law", "category_facts": {"category": "GENERAL_CONSTITUTIONAL", "remedy_type": "Writ Petition / Criminal Appeal", "judicial_disposition": "Allowed", "constitutional_article": "Article 226 / Article 21"}, "activity_e