1e4a8d47-39e1-4bf4-b61f-9bbee40660c1	NO. 11957 of 2026	Mr. Subhalata Priyadarsini v. State of Orissa	High Court of Orissa at Cuttack	2026	Hon'ble MR. JUSTICE ADITYA KUMAR MOHAPATRA	Mr. Subhalata Priyadarsini v. State of Orissa	["Arms Act", "Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023", "the BNS"]	["Section 109(1) the BNS", "Section 115(2) the BNS", "Section 118(1) the BNS", "Section 126(2) the BNS", "Section 25(1)(a) Arms Act", "Section 296 the BNS", "Section 3(5) the BNS", "Section 351(3) the BNS"]	["civil & constitutional law", "ohc", "disposed"]	Judgment in NO. 11957 of 2026 delivered by Hon'ble MR. JUSTICE ADITYA KUMAR MOHAPATRA at High Court of Orissa at Cuttack. The proceedings concern Civil & Constitutional Law with respect to Section 482.	Disposed	storage/cases/OHC_2026_NO_11957_of_2026_1e4a8d47.pdf	d5f25ea297316ff66b8d66841283c7a3788497481f1d02f63f665b5afd19e2c9	\N	\N	\N	published	657396f3-5181-4922-8323-72d78b963be0	657396f3-5181-4922-8323-72d78b963be0	2026-10-25 14:51:54.533779+05:30	2026-10-25 14:51:54.533785+05:30	2026-10-26 10:38:07.340691+05:30	23.10.2026 Order No. 01. 1. This matter is taken up through Hybrid mode. 2. Heard learned counsel for the Petitioner as well as learned counsel for the State-Opposite Party. Perused the Anticipatory Bail Application as well as the F.I.R.	[]	Holding and principles affirmed in NO. 11957 of 2026 regarding Civil & Constitutional Law. The Court adjudicated upon Section 482.	[]	Disposed	[]	\N	unverified	Good Law (Binding Precedent)	IN THE HIGH COURT OF ORISSA AT CUTTACK\nABLAPL No.11957 of 2026\nCNR No. ODHC010801942026\nSantosh Gouda @ Santosh Kumar ..... Petitioner\nGouda\nRepresented by Adv. –\nMr. Subhalata\nPriyadarsini\n-versus-\nState of Orissa ..... Opposite Party\nRepresented by Adv. –\nMiss Bijaya Laxmi\nTripathy, ASC\nCORAM:\nMR. JUSTICE ADITYA KUMAR MOHAPATRA\nORDER\n23.10.2026\nOrder No.\n01. 1. This matter is taken up through Hybrid mode.\n2. Heard learned counsel for the Petitioner as well as learned\ncounsel for the State-Opposite Party. Perused the Anticipatory Bail\nApplication as well as the F.I.R.\n3. The present application has been filed under Section 482 of\nB.N.S.S., 2023 by the Petitioner seeking pre-arrest bail in\nconnection with Khallikote P.S. Case No.686 of 2026,\ncorresponding to G.R. Case No.1753 of 2026, pending in the court\nof the learned J.M.F.C., Khallikote, registered for alleged\ncommission of offences punishable under Sections\n126(2)/296/115(2)/118(1)/109(1)/351(3)/3(5) of the BNS, 2023 read\nwith Section 25(1)(a) of the Arms Act, 1959.\n4. Learned counsel for the Petitioner, at the outset, submitted that\nPage 1 of 1.\n\nthe Petitioner does not want to press this bail application and seeks\nliberty to surrender before the court below and moves an application\nfor bail. He further submitted that some of the co-accused persons\nhave already been released on bail in the meantime.\n5. Taking into consideration the nature and gravity of the\nallegation and on the request of the learned counsel for the\nPetitioner, the Petitioner is permitted to surrender before the learned\nJ.M.F.C., Khallikote in the aforesaid case in the first hour within\nfour weeks hence and move for bail. On such event, the learned\nMagistrate shall consider his application for bail in the first hour\nstrictly on the basis of the materials on record. In case of rejection of\nthe bail application, the Petitioner may move for bail before the\nhigher forum in the second hour. On such event, the higher forum\nshall consider and dispose of the bail application of the Petitioner on\nthe same day strictly on the basis of the materials on record by\nmaintaining the principles of parity, if applicable.\n6. The case diary be made available on the date of surrender on\nan application being filed by the Petitioner prior to his date of\nsurrender along with a copy of today’s order. Records be transmitted\nto the higher forum at the cost of the Petitioner, if applied for.\n7. The ABLAPL is, accordingly, disposed of.\nIssue urgent certified copy of this order as per Rules.\n( Aditya Kumar Mohapatra )\nVacation Judge\nDebasis\nPage 2 of 2.	2	t	ODHC010801942026	Judicial Precedent	2026-10-23	Single Bench	Mr. Subhalata Priyadarsini	State of Orissa	\N	\N	Civil & Constitutional Law	In this matter, the High Court of Orissa at Cuttack adjudicated issues between Mr. Subhalata Priyadarsini and State of Orissa. The Court rendered a decision disposing of the application under statutory provisions.	0	2026 LexGuard (OHC) 1E4A8D47	{"court": "High Court of Orissa at Cuttack", "title": "Mr. Subhalata Priyadarsini v. State of Orissa", "case_id": "1e4a8d47-39e1-4bf4-b61f-9bbee40660c1", "case_no": "NO. 11957 of 2026", "parties": "Mr. Subhalata Priyadarsini v. State of Orissa", "category": "BAIL_SUSPENSION", "petitioner": "Mr. Subhalata Priyadarsini", "respondent": "State of Orissa", "legal_domain": "Civil & Constitutional Law", "category_facts": {"category": "BAIL_SUSPENSION", "surety_count": null, "custody_period": null, "application_type": "Anticipatory Bail", "bail_bond_amount": null, "trial_court_fine": null, "reason_for_relief": null, "reporting_condition": null, "trial_court_sentence": null, "trial_court_fine_paid": false}, "activity_events": [], "profile_version": "2.5", "statutory_matrix": [], "activity_clusters": [], "scenario_clusters": [], "scenario_keywords": [], "procedural_posture": {"remedy": "Disposed", "disposition": "Disposed"}}
