tioner\nVersus\n\n5\nState of H.P. and Ors .....Respondents\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n27. CWP No.17907 of 2026\nDavinder Bhatia …..Petitioner\nVersus\nState of H.P. and Ors .....Respondents\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n28. CWP No.17908 of 2026\nSohan Singh and Ors …..Petitioners\nVersus\nState of H.P. and Ors .....Respondents\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCoram\nMs. Justice Jyotsna Rewal Dua\nWhether approved for reporting?1\nFor the Petitioners: M/s Yogesh K Chande, Mamta Garg,\nDiwan Singh Negi, Devender K\nSharma, Kush Sharma, Surender K\nSharma, Ajay Kumar Chauhan, Pawan\nK Sharma, Vaibhav Tanwar and\nMr. Naveen K Negi,\nAdvocates in the respective petitions.\nFor the Respondents: Mr. Y.P.S.Dhaulta and Mr. L.N.\nSharma, Additional Advocates General.\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nJyotsna Rewal Dua, Judge\nNotice. Mr. L.N. Sharma, learned Additional\nAdvocate General, appears and waives service of notice on\nbehalf of the respondents in all the writ petitions.\n1Whether reporters of print and electronic media may be allowed to see the order? Yes.\n\n6\n2. Petitioners’ grievance is that their\nrepresentations, annexed with the respective writ petitions,\nseeking applicability of Inder Singh Thakur & Ors Vs.\nState of H.P. & Ors2 have not been decided till date by\nthe respondents/competent authority. Learned counsel for\nthe petitioners submitted that the petitioners would be\ncontent in case the respondents/competent authority(s) are\ndirected to consider and decide the aforesaid\nrepresentations in accordance with law within a fixed-time\nschedule. Learned Additional Advocate General is not\naverse to this prayer.\n3. Having regard to the afore-submissions, but\nwithout examining the merits of the matters, these writ\npetitions are disposed of with a direction to the\nrespondents/competent authority to consider and decide\nthe aforesaid representations of the petitioners in\naccordance with law as well as taking into consideration\nthe above decision, within a period of six weeks from today.\nThe decision so arrived at shall also be communicated to\nthe petitioners.\n2 CWP No. 4830 of 2023, decided alongwith connected matter on 07.04.2025.\n\n7\nThe writ petitions stand disposed of in the above\nterms, so also the pending miscellaneous application(s), if\nany.\nJyotsna Rewal Dua\nOctober 12, 2026 Judge\nR.Atal	7	t	HCMA010179762026	Writ Petition	2026-10-23	Single Bench	..Petitioner	State of H.P. & Ors.	\N	\N	Civil & Constitutional Law	In this matter, the High Court of Judicature adjudicated issues between 1. CWP No.17976 of 2026 Sudesh Kumar and State of H.P. and Ors. The Court rendered a decision disposing of the application under statutory provisions.	0	2026 LexGuard (HC) 2A27DF25	{"court": "High Court of Judicature", "title": "Sudesh Kumar v. State of H.P. & Ors.", "case_id": "2a27df25-2dc1-4a5c-b7ff-423a9018ed96", "case_no": "CWP No. 17976 of 2026", "parties": "Sudesh Kumar v. State of H.P. & Ors.", "category": "SERVICE_WRIT", "petitioner": "Sudesh Kumar", "respondent": "State of H.P. & Ors.", "legal_domain": "Civil & Constitutional Law", "category_facts": {"category": "SERVICE_WRIT", "effective_dates": "12.10.2026, 07.04.2025", "monetary_claims": "Notional vs Actual consequential arrears", "delay_laches_raised": false, "service_relief_sought": "Service Benefits / Writ of Certiorari & Mandamus"}, "activity_events": [], "profile_version": "2.5", "statutory_matrix": [], "activity_clusters": [], "scenario_clusters": [], "scenario_keywords": [], "procedural_posture": {"remedy": "Disposed", "disposition": "Disposed"}}
