tation dated on 08.07.2026 and conduct enquiry on the\ncomplaint lodged by the Petitioner under monitoring of 2nd respondent within\nthe time stipulated by this Court.\nFor Petitioner : Mr.N.Arjunkumar\nFor Respondents : Mr.D.Rajaboopathy (R1 to R3)\nGovernment Advocate (Crl.Side)\n1/4\n\nW.P.Crl.(MD)No.3915 of 2026\nORDER\nThis writ petition has been filed seeking for a direction to the third\nRespondent to consider the Petitioner's representation dated on 08.07.2026 and\nconduct enquiry on the complaint lodged by the Petitioner.\n2. The learned counsel for the petitioner submitted that the\npetitioner had sent a representation seeking action against the persons, who had\ncommitted theft of his vehicle. However, no proper action was taken, and\ntherefore, this petition was filed.\n3.The learned Government Advocate (Crl.Side) appearing for the\nrespondents submitted that they have received the representation of the\npetitioner and the enquiry is pending.\n4. Heard the learned counsel on either side and carefully perused\nthe materials before this Court.\n5. Considering the facts and circumstances of this case, the third\nrespondent police is directed to consider the petitioner's representation dated\n08.07.2026 and conduct an enquiry in this regard, after issuing summons to the\n2/4\n\nW.P.Crl.(MD)No.3915 of 2026\nparties concerned, under Section 41A of Cr.P.C / 35(3) of BNSS, and conclude\nthe same, within a period of four weeks from the date of receipt of a copy of\nthis order.\n6. This writ petition is disposed with the above directions.\n16.07.2026\nNCC : Yes / No\nIndex : Yes / No\nPNM\nTO:-\n1. The Superintendent of Police,\nO/o.The Superintendent of Police, Theni District.\n2. The Deputy Superintendent Of Police,\nO/o.The Deputy Superintendent of Police\nUthamapalayam, Theni District.\n3. The Inspector of Police,\nOotaipatti Police Station, Ootaipatti,\nTheni District.\n4. The Additional Public Prosecutor,\nMadurai Bench of Madras High Court,\nMadurai.\n3/4\n\nW.P.Crl.(MD)No.3915 of 2026\nL.VICTORIA GOWRI, J.\nPNM\nORDER IN\nW.P.Crl.(MD)No.3915 of 2026\n16.07.2026\n4/4	4	t	HCMA010039152026	Writ Petition	2026-07-16	Single Bench	Alageswaran ... Petitioner	State of Tamil Nadu & Ors.	Mr.N.Arjunkumar	Mr.D.Rajaboopathy (R1 to R3) Government Advocate (Crl.Side)	Constitutional Law	In this judgment under Civil Law, the Court ruled on the dispute between 1Oihkgh7Jsa Jslzuzt4 Cx4Rczsrbvdi Home   Judgements And Orders, Supreme Court And High Courts Of India and the Respondent.	0	2026 LexGuard (Judg) 3548C0	{"court": "Madras High Court (Principal Seat, Chennai)", "title": "Alageswaran v. State of Tamil Nadu & Ors.", "case_id": "3548c03b-b799-4186-8e3c-fb425568426e", "case_no": "W.P.Crl.(MD)No.3915 of 2026", "parties": "Alageswaran v. State of Tamil Nadu & Ors.", "category": "GENERAL_CONSTITUTIONAL", "petitioner": "Alageswaran", "respondent": "State of Tamil Nadu & Ors.", "legal_domain": "Constitutional Law", "category_facts": {"category": "GENERAL_CONSTITUTIONAL", "remedy_type": "Writ of Mandamus", "judicial_disposition": "Dismissed", "constitutional_article": "Article 226 / Article 21"}, "activity_events": [], "profile_version": "2.5", "statutory_matrix": [], "activity_clusters": [], "scenario_clusters": [], "scenario_keywords": [], "procedural_posture": {"remedy": "Allowed", "disposition": "Allowed"}}
