ENCH:\nHon'ble Justice G. Ilangovan\n\nPARTIES:\nA. John Kennedy\n... Appellant(s) / Petitioner(s)\nVersus\nIntelligence Officer, Narcotics Control Bureau (NCB), Madurai Sub Zone\n... Respondent(s) / State\n\nSTATUTORY PROVISIONS & ACTS REFERRED:\nNarcotic Drugs and Psychotropic Substances Act 1985\n\nSECTIONS & CLAUSES UNDER CONSIDERATION:\nNDPS Act Section 8(c), NDPS Act Section 20(b)(ii)(C), NDPS Act Section 37\n\nKEY LEGAL DOMAINS & TOPICS:\nNDPS Bail, Commercial Quantity, Section 37 NDPS, Twin Conditions, Reasonable Grounds\n\n================================================================================\n                                   JUDGMENT\n================================================================================\n\n1. FACTUAL MATRIX:\nPetitioner was apprehended with 42 kg of Ganja (commercial quantity). Petitioner moved second regular bail application alleging procedural non-compliance with Section 50 NDPS Act.\n\n2. ISSUES FRAMED FOR ADJUDICATION:\n1. Whether non-compliance with Section 50 can be decided at bail stage when search was of vehicle and luggage?\n\n3. STATUTORY FRAMEWORK & PRECEDENTS:\nSection 37 NDPS mandates satisfaction that accused is not guilty and unlikely to commit offense while on bail.\n\n4. RATIO DECIDENDI:\nSection 50 NDPS Act applies only to personal search of the accused, not vehicle search. Twin conditions under Section 37 bar bail in commercial quantity seizure.\n\n5. FINAL DISPOSITION & ORDER:\nBail Application Dismissed; Commercial quantity recovery bars bail under Section 37 of NDPS Act.\n\nDecreed and ordered accordingly.\n\nHon'ble Justice G. Ilangovan\nMadras High Court (Madurai Bench)\n[LEXGUARD CRYPTOGRAPHIC VERIFIED REPOSITORY RECORD]\n	3	t	HCMD010045192026	Criminal Original Petition (Bail)	\N	Single Bench	A. John Kennedy	Intelligence Officer, Narcotics Control Bureau	\N	\N	Criminal Law	In this criminal original petition under Criminal Law, the Court ruled on the dispute between A. John Kennedy and Intelligence Officer, Narcotics Control Bureau.	0	2026 LexGuard (Crim) 36A8B4	{"court": "Madras High Court (Madurai Bench)", "title": "A. John Kennedy v. Intelligence Officer, Narcotics Control Bureau", "case_id": "36a8b4a0-6cb9-4e16-88eb-9a6a3468c32f", "case_no": "Crl.O.P.(MD) No. 4519 of 2026", "parties": "A. John Kennedy", "category": "NDPS", "petitioner": "A. John Kennedy", "respondent": "Intelligence Officer, Narcotics Control Bureau", "legal_domain": "Criminal Law", "category_facts": {"category": "NDPS", "custody_period": null, "contraband_type": "Ganja", "seized_quantity": "42 kg", "statutory_issue": "Bail / Pre-trial Release under NDPS Act", "quantity_category": "Commercial Quantity", "section_37_embargo": true, "search_compliance_sec_50": "Search from vehicle/bag (Section 50 personal search held inapplicable)"}, "activity_events": [], "profile_version": "2.5", "statutory_matrix": [], "activity_clusters": [], "scenario_clusters": ["pre_trial_custody", "narcotics_contraband"], "scenario_keywords": ["regular bail", "ndps", "commercial quantity", "section 37 ndps", "section 50 ndps"], "procedural_posture": {"remedy": "Dismissed", "disposition": "Dismissed"}}
