GJHC240562342026)\nIN THE HIGH COURT OF GUJARAT AT AHMEDABAD\nR/SPECIAL CIVIL APPLICATION NO. 12114 of 2026\n==========================================================\nM/S NEW INDIA DETERGENTS PVT LTD\nVersus\nUNION OF INDIA & ORS.\n==========================================================\nAppearance:\nMR ANAND NAINAWATI(5970) for the Petitioner(s) No. 1\nPARAM V SHAH(9473) for the Respondent(s) No. 1,2\nTIRTH NAYAK(8563) for the Respondent(s) No. 3,4\n==========================================================\nCORAM:HONOURABLE MR. JUSTICE A.S. SUPEHIA\nand\nHONOURABLE MS. JUSTICE VAIBHAVI D. NANAVATI\nDate : 22/10/2026\nORAL ORDER\n(PER : HONOURABLE MR. JUSTICE A.S. SUPEHIA)\n1. Pursuant to the order dated 13.10.2026 learned Senior Standing\nCouncil Mr.Tirth Nayak has tendered the Circular No.38/97 dated\n19.09.1997 and has submitted that if the petitioner makes fresh\napplication, the same will be considered in accordance with the aforesaid\ncircular and in accordance with law, more particularly paragraph Nos.4, 5\nand 6.\n2. Learned advocate Mr.Anand Nainawati has no objection to such\nproposition.\n3. Hence, we direct that the petitioner shall make an appropriate\napplication for execution of corporate guarantee or bond within a period\nof two weeks.\nPage 1 of 2\n\nC/SCA/12114/2026 ORDER DATED: 22/10/2026\n(GJHC240562342026)\n4. Under the circumstances, if the petitioner files an application for\nfurnishing the corporate guarantee or bond instead of bank guarantee, the\nsame shall be considered by the authority in light of the circular dated\n19.09.1997 and in accordance with law and pass appropriate order within\na period of four weeks thereafter. If the petitioner is aggrieved by any\ndecision of the respondent authority, it will be open for him to file\nappropriate application before appropriate forum.\n5. The present writ petition stands disposed of.\n(A. S. SUPEHIA, J)\n(VAIBHAVI D. NANAVATI,J)\nK.K. SAIYED/83\nPage 2 of 2	2	t	GJHC010121142026	Judicial 