44444444-0018-4000-8000-000000000018	Writ Petition (Civil) No. 35293 of 2018	Fathima Thasneem (represented by father) v. State of Kerala & Christ Nagar Senior Secondary School	High Court of Kerala at Ernakulam	2018	Hon'ble A. Muhamed Mustaque, J.	Fathima Thasneem (represented by father) v. State of Kerala & Christ Nagar Senior Secondary School	["Constitution of India", "Right of Children to Free and Compulsory Education Act, 2009"]	["Article 19(1)(g)", "Article 25", "Article 26"]	["headscarf in school", "private school uniform code", "competing fundamental rights", "institution autonomy"]	Justice A. Muhamed Mustaque held that the institutional autonomy of a private school to prescribe a uniform dress code prevails over an individual student's religious preference to wear a headscarf.	Disposed	storage/cases/KHC_2018_WP_Civil_No_35293_of_2018_44440018.pdf	5bac124e8bcd259171592699aaee5044b7aece26611899c37b37857fe59d42ea	\N	\N	\N	published	657396f3-5181-4922-8323-72d78b963be0	657396f3-5181-4922-8323-72d78b963be0	2026-10-25 11:24:40.911872+05:30	2026-10-25 11:24:40.911877+05:30	2026-10-26 10:38:08.546918+05:30	\N	[]	When individual fundamental rights under Article 25 clash with the institutional autonomy of a private school to manage its affairs under Article 19(1)(g), the larger public interest of secular uniform discipline in a private school prevails.	[]	Disposed	[]	\N	unverified	Good Law (Binding Kerala HC Precedent)	High Court of Kerala at Ernakulam\nWrit Petition (Civil) No. 35293 of 2018\nFathima Thasneem v. State of Kerala and Others\nBench: Hon'ble A. Muhamed Mustaque, J.\nDate: 2018-12-04\nCitation: 2018:KHC:1120\n\nRATIO DECIDENDI:\nWhen individual fundamental rights under Article 25 clash with the institutional autonomy of a private school to manage its affairs under Article 19(1)(g), the larger public interest of secular uniform discipline in a private school prevails.\n\nSUMMARY:\nJustice A. Muhamed Mustaque held that the institutional autonomy of a private school to prescribe a uniform dress code prevails over an individual student's religious preference to wear a headscarf.\n\nSTATUTES: Article 19(1)(g), Article 25, Article 26\nDISPOSITION: Private School Uniform Policy Upheld	2	f	HCMA010352932018	Writ Petition	2018-12-04	Single Judge	Fathima Thasneem (represented by father)	State of Kerala & Christ Nagar Senior Secondary School	Advocate Babu S. Nair	Senior Advocate Kurian George Kannanthanam	Education Law & School Uniform Autonomy	Private schools have the legal authority to enforce a neutral school uniform policy. Students cannot demand permission to wear additional religious attire like headscarves contrary to the school's dress code.	0	2018:KHC:1120	{"court": "High Court of Kerala at Ernakulam", "title": "Fathima Thasneem v. State of Kerala and Others", "case_id": "44444444-0018-4000-8000-000000000018", "case_no": "Writ Petition (Civil) No. 35293 of 2018", "parties": "Fathima Thasneem (represented by father) v. State of Kerala & Christ Nagar Senior Secondary School", "category": "GENERAL_CONSTITUTIONAL", "petitioner": "Fathima Thasneem (represented by father)", "respondent": "State of Kerala & Christ Nagar Senior Secondary School", "legal_domain": "Education Law & School Uniform Autonomy", "category_facts": {"category": "GENERAL_CONSTITUTIONAL", "remedy_type": "Writ Petition / Criminal Appeal", "judicial_disposition": "Dismissed", "constitutional_article": "Article 226 / Article 21"}, "activity_events": [], "profile_version": "2.5", "statutory_matrix": [{"act": "CONSTITUTION", "section": "19", "canonical": "Section 19 CONSTITUTION", "equivalents": []}, {"act": "CONSTITUTION", "section": "25", "canonical": "Section 25 CONSTITUTION", "equivalents": []}, {"act": "CONSTITUTION", "section": "26", "canonical": "Section 26 CONSTITUTION", "equivalents": []}], "activity_clusters": [], "scenario_clusters": ["constitutional_fundamental"], "scenario_keywords": ["fundamental rights"], "procedural_posture": {"remedy": "Dismiss