44444444-0019-4000-8000-000000000019	Writ Petition (Civil) No. 1081 of 2020	Foundation for Media Professionals v. UT of Jammu and Kashmir & Union of India	Supreme Court of India	2020	Hon'ble N.V. Ramana, R. Subhash Reddy, B.R. Gavai, JJ.	Foundation for Media Professionals v. UT of Jammu and Kashmir & Union of India	["Constitution of India", "Indian Telegraph Act, 1885"]	["Article 19(1)(a)", "Article 21"]	["4G internet restoration", "special review committee", "COVID-19 healthcare access", "online education"]	Three-judge bench directed the constitution of a Special Committee headed by Union Home Secretary to urgently examine restoration of 4G mobile internet in J&K, balancing national security against public healthcare and online education.	Disposed	storage/cases/SC_2020_WP_Civil_No_1081_of_2020_44440019.pdf	4071a178e1c37ad0ec06e88b4ca521ec0830502051b6bcd99c0caf31685d9b60	\N	\N	\N	published	657396f3-5181-4922-8323-72d78b963be0	657396f3-5181-4922-8323-72d78b963be0	2026-10-25 11:24:40.932762+05:30	2026-10-25 11:24:40.932768+05:30	2026-10-26 10:38:08.547608+05:30	\N	[]	While national security is paramount, access to healthcare and education during a global pandemic requires a calibrated, periodic review of telecommunications restrictions rather than blanket indefinite throttles.	[]	Disposed	[{"court": "Supreme Court of India", "title": "Judicial Precedent [2020) 5 SCC 746]", "status": "Good Law (External Authority)", "case_id": null, "citation": "2020) 5 SCC 746", "treatment": "Cited / Considered"}]	\N	unverified	Good Law (Binding 3-Judge Precedent)	Supreme Court of India\nWrit Petition (Civil) No. 1081 of 2020\nFoundation for Media Professionals v. Union Territory of Jammu and Kashmir and Another\nBench: Hon'ble N.V. Ramana, R. Subhash Reddy, B.R. Gavai, JJ.\nDate: 2020-05-11\nCitation: (2020) 5 SCC 746\n\nRATIO DECIDENDI:\nWhile national security is paramount, access to healthcare and education during a global pandemic requires a calibrated, periodic review of telecommunications restrictions rather than blanket indefinite throttles.\n\nSUMMARY:\nThree-judge bench directed the constitution of a Special Committee headed by Union Home Secretary to urgently examine restoration of 4G mobile internet in J&K, balancing national security against public healthcare and online education.\n\nSTATUTES: Article 19(1)(a), Article 21\nDISPOSITION: Special Review Committee Constituted	2	f	SCIN010010812020	Writ Petition	2020-05-11	Three-Judge Bench	Foundation for Media Professionals	UT of Jammu and Kashmir & Union of India	Senior Advocate Huzefa Ahmadi, Salman Khurshid	Attorney General K.K. Venugopal, Solicitor General Tushar Mehta	Telecommunications Law & Health Rights during Pandemic	During the pandemic, the Supreme Court required the Central Government to review internet speed restrictions in J&K to ensure students and doctors could access online education and medical guidance.	0	(2020) 5 SCC 746	{"court": "Supreme Court of India", "title": "Foundation for Media Professionals v. Union Territory of Jammu and Kashmir and Another", "case_id": "44444444-0019-4000-8000-000000000019", "case_no": "Writ Petition (Civil) No. 1081 of 2020", "parties": "Foundation for Media Professionals v. UT of Jammu and Kashmir & Union of India", "category": "GENERAL_CONSTITUTIONAL", "petitioner": "Foundation for Media Professionals", "respondent": "UT of Jammu and Kashmir & Union of India", "legal_domain": "Telecommunications Law & Health Rights during Pandemic", "category_facts": {"category": "GENERAL_CONSTITUTIONAL", "remedy_type": "Writ Petition / Criminal Appeal", "judicial_disposition": "Dismissed", "constitutional_article": "Article 226 / Article 21"}, "activity_events": [], "profile_version": "2.5", "statutory_matrix": [{"act": "CONSTITUTION", "section": "19", "canonical": "Section 19 CONSTITUTION", "equivalents": []}, {"act": "CONSTITUTION", "section": "21", "canonical": "Section 21 CONSTITUTION", "equivalents": []}], "activity_clusters": [], "scenario_clusters": ["constitutional_fundamental"], "scenario_keywords": ["article 21"], "procedural_posture": {"remedy": "Directions Issued", "disposition": "Directions Issued"}}
