freedom under Article 26(b) cannot be absolute so as to trample upon individual human dignity and civil rights. The power of excommunication having serious civil consequences must be tested against constitutional morality.\n\nSUMMARY:\nFive-judge Constitution Bench held that earlier 1962 ruling in Sardar Syedna upholding excommunication rights required reconsideration by a larger bench, harmonizing religious autonomy under Article 26 with civil rights and human dignity.\n\nSTATUTES: Article 25, Article 26(b), Article 21\nDISPOSITION: Excommunication Reconsideration Referred to 9-Judge Bench	2	f	SCIN010007401986	Civil Appeal	2004-12-17	Constitution Bench (5 Judges)	Central Board of Dawoodi Bohra Community & Another	State of Maharashtra & Another	Senior Advocate F.S. Nariman	Senior Advocate K.K. Venugopal	Religious Autonomy & Civil Rights	The Supreme Court ruled that a religious head cannot arbitrarily excommunicate community members and strip them of civil rights. The issue was referred to the larger 9-judge bench examining religious practices.	0	(2005) 2 SCC 673	{"court": "Supreme Court of India", "title": "Central Board of Dawoodi Bohra Community and Another v. State of Maharashtra and Another", "case_id": "44444444-0020-4000-8000-000000000020", "case_no": "Civil Appeal No. 740 of 1986", "parties": "Central Board of Dawoodi Bohra Community & Another v. State of Maharashtra & Another", "category": "GENERAL_CONSTITUTIONAL", "petitioner": "Central Board of Dawoodi Bohra Community & Another", "respondent": "State of Maharashtra & Another", "legal_domain": "Religious Autonomy & Civil Rights", "category_facts": {"category": "GENERAL_CONSTITUTIONAL", "remedy_type": "Writ Petition / Criminal Appeal", "judicial_disposition": "Dismissed", "constitutional_article": "Article 226 / Article 21"}, "activity_events": [], "profile_version": "2.5", "statutory_matrix": [{"act": "CONSTITUTION", "section": "25", "canonical": "Section 25 CONSTITUTION", "equivalents": []}, {"act": "CONSTITUTION", "section": "26", "canonical": "Section 26 CONSTITUTION", "equivalents": []}, {"act": "CONSTITUTION", "section": "21", "canonical": "Section 21 CONSTITUTION", "equivalents": []}], "activity_clusters": [], "scenario_clusters": ["constitutional_fundamental"], "scenario_keywords": ["article 21"], "procedural_posture": {"remedy": "Referred to Larger Bench", "disposition": "Referred to Larger Bench"}}
