026 and WMP No.48851 of 2026\nCNR: {HCMA012567302026}\nS.Kulandaisamy\nS/o. Late. Sabari Muthu,\nNo. 113, Thirumalai Nagar Annexe,\nOMR , Rajiv Gandhi Salai,\nChennai 96\n..Petitioner(s)\nVs\n1. The Additional Secretary to Government\nHousing and Urban Development Department,\nSecretariat, Chennai 09\n2. The Commissioner\nGreater Chennai Corporation,\nRipon Buildings, Chennai 03\n3. The District Collector\nChengalpattu District\n4. The Revenue Divisional Officer\nTambaram Division,\nTambaram , Chennai 45\n5. The Thasildar\nTambaram Taluk\n6. The Executive Engineer\nGreater Chennai Corporation,\nChennai\n..Respondent(s)\n__________\nPage1 of 5\nhttps://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis\n\nWP No. 43531 of 2026\nWrit Petition filed under Article 226 of the Constitution of India to issue a\nwrit of Mandamus forbearing the respondents particularly 6th respondent from\ndemolishing the petitioners building in S.No. 35/1A1 part measuring to an\nextent of 3560 sq.ft situated at Plot No.113, Thirumalai Nagar Annexe,\nPerungudi Village, Tambaram Taluk, presently Kancheepuram district till the\nfinal order passed by the 1st respondent.\nFor Petitioner(s): Mr.K.Praveen Raj\nfor Mr.G.Mohammed Aseef\nFor Respondent(s): Mr.K.Surendar\nSpecial Government Pleader\nFor R.1, R.3 to R.5\nORDER\n(Order of the Court was made by Sunder Mohan J.)\nThe writ petition is for issuance of a Mandamus forbearing the\nrespondents, particularly the sixth respondent from demolishing the petitioner’s\nbuilding in Survey No.35/1A/1 Part, pending disposal of the revision filed under\nSection 80A of the Tamil Nadu Town and Country Planning Act, 1971 dated\n24.07.2026.\n2. The learned Special Government Pleader, on instructions, would\nsubmit that the revision is pending consideration and orders would be passed\nwithin a period of three weeks as the petitioner and the respondents have\nalready been personally heard.\n__________\nPage2 of 5\nhttps://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis\n\nWP No. 43531 of 2026\n3. In view of the above submission, the respondents are directed to\ndispose the revision within a period of four weeks from the date of receipt of a\ncopy of this order and shall not take any action for eviction pending disposal of\nthe revision under Section 80A of the Tamil Nadu Town and Country Planning\nAct, 1971.\n4. With the above observation, the writ petition is disposed of. No costs.\nConsequently, connected miscellaneous petition is closed.\n(S.M.,J.) (G.K.M.,J.)\n23-10-2026\nIndex: Yes/No\nSpeaking/Non-speaking order\nNeutral Citation: Yes/No\nSR/MMI\nTo\n1. The Additional Secretary to Government\nHousing and Urban Development department,\nSecretariat, Chennai 09.\n2. The Commissioner\nGreater Chennai Corporation,\nRipon Buildings, Chennai 03\n3. The District Collector\nChengalpattu District\n__________\nPage3 of 5\nhttps://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis\n\nWP No. 43531 of 2026\n4. The Revenue Divisional Officer\nTambaram Division,\nTambaram , Chennai 45\n5. The Thasildar\nTambaram Taluk\n6. The Executive Engineer\nGreater Chennai Corporation,\nChennai\n__________\nPage4 of 5\nhttps://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis\n\nWP No. 43531 of 2026\nSUNDER MOHAN, J.\nAND\nGK.MUTHUKUMAAR, J.\nSR/MMI\nWP No. 43531 of 2026\n23-10-2026\n__________\nPage5 of 5\nhttps://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis	5	t	HCMA012567302026	Writ Petition	2026-10-23	Single Bench	S.Kulandaisamy	1. The Additional Secretary to Government Housing and Urban Development Department	Mr.K.Praveen Raj	Mr.K.Surendar Special Government Pleader	Civil & Constitutional Law	In this matter, the Madras High Court (Principal Seat, Chennai) adjudicated issues between Chennai 96 and 1. The Additional Secretary to Government Housing and Urban Development Department. The Court rendered a decision disposing of the application under statutory provisions.	0	2026 LexGuard (MHC) 28D2869E	{"court": "Madras High Court (Principal Seat, Chennai)", "title": "Chennai 96 v. 1. The Additional Secretary to Government Housing and Urban Development Department", "case_id": "28d2869e-b7f7-47be-a770-d4d4d2f2a6a3", "case_no": "NO. 43531 of 2026", "parties": "Chennai 96 v. 1. The Additional Secretary to Government Housing and Urban Development Department", "category": "GENERAL_CONSTITUTIONAL", "petitioner": "Chennai 96", "respondent": "1. The Additional Secretary to Government Housing and Urban Development Department", "legal_domain": "Civil & Constitutional Law", "category_facts": {"category": "GENERAL_CONSTITUTIONAL", "remedy_type": "Writ of Mandamus", "judicial_disposition": "Dismissed", "constitutional_article": "Article 226 / Article 21"}, "activity_events": [], "profile_version": "2.5", "statutory_matrix": [{"act": "CONSTITUTION", "section": "226", "canonical": "Section 226 CONSTITUTION", "equivalents": []}], "activity_clusters": [], "scenario_clusters": ["constitutional_fundamental"], "scenario_keywords": ["article 226"], "procedural_posture": {"remedy": "Disposed", "disposition": "Disposed"}}
060b0443-5dee-4738-b15d-a1b2d4892706	CRL OP(MD) No. 24107 of 2026	Abishek v. State of Tamilnadu Rep. by The Inspector of Police	Madras High Court (Madurai Bench)	2026	Hon'ble Mr. Justice P.Murugan	Abishek v. State of Tamilnadu Rep. by The Inspector of Police	["Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita, 2023", "Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023", "Narcotic Drugs and Psychotropic Substances Act, 1985", "of BNSS"]	["Section 355 of BNSS"]	["civil & constitutional law", "mhc", "disposed"]	Judgment in NO. 24107 of 2026 delivered by Hon'ble Bench at Madras High Court (Madurai Bench). The proceedings concern Civil & Constitutional Law with respect to procedural compliance.	Disposed	storage/cases/MHC_2026_NO_24107_of_2026_060b0443.pdf	f753da5982b4fc6c589e251675688d18eb2027289d16712e226077b17345f7a6	\N	\N	\N	published	657396f3-5181-4922-8323-72d78b963be0	657396f3-5181-4922-8323-72d78b963be0	2026-10-25 14:52:01.4235+05:30	2026-10-25 14:52:01.423505+05:30	2026-10-26 10:38:07.69024+05:30	2. The case of the prosecution is that on secret information, the respondent police were conducting surveillance near Thanjavur East Gate AV Road, where they found the petitioner and the other accused carrying a bag. On seeing the respondent police, the petitioner and the other accused tried to escape. However, the respondent police apprehended them and found 200 prohibited tablets, namely, TAPENTADOL, in the possession of the petitioner. The petitioner and the other accused confessed that they had ordered the same online and received them through Professional Courier Service for sale to others. 3.	[]	Holding and principles affirmed in NO. 24107 of 2026 regarding Civil & Constitutional Law. The Court adjudicated upon applicable judicial standards.	[]	Disposed	[]	\N	unverified	Good Law (Binding Precedent)	CRL OP(MD) No. 24107 of 2026\nBEFORE THE MADURAI BENCH OF MADRAS HIGH COURT\n( Criminal Jurisdiction)\nDATED: 23.10.2026\nPRESENT\nTHE HON'BLE DR.JUSTICE P.MURUGAN\nCRL OP(MD) No. 24107 of 2026\nCNR:{HCMD011528062026}\nAbishek\n..Petitioner\nVs\nState of Tamilnadu\nRep. by The Inspector of Police,\nThanjavur Town West Police Station,\nThanjavur District.\n(Crime No.451 of 2026)\n..Respondent\nFor Petitioner : Mr.A.Arun Prasad,\nAdvocate\nFor Respondent : Mr.N.Balasubramanian\nGovernment Advocate (Crl. Side)\nPETITION FOR BAIL Under Section 483 of B.N.S.S.\nPRAYER :-\nFor Bail in Crime No.451 of 2026 on the file of the\nRespondent Police.\n__________\nPage 1 of 6\nhttps://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis\n\nCRL OP(MD) No. 24107 of 2026\nORDER : The Court made the following order:-\nThe petitioner / A1, who was arrested and remanded to\njudicial custody on 12.09.2026 for the offences punishable under\nSections 123 and 278 of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita (BNS), 2023,\nin Crime No.451 of 2026, on the file of the respondent police, seeks\nbail.\n2. The case of the prosecution is that on secret information, the\nrespondent police were conducting surveillance near Thanjavur East\nGate AV Road, where they found the petitioner and the other\naccused carrying a bag. On seeing the respondent police, the\npetitioner and the other accused tried to escape. However, the\nrespondent police apprehended them and found 200 prohibited\ntablets, namely, TAPENTADOL, in the possession of the petitioner.\nThe petitioner and the other accused confessed that they had ordered\nthe same online and received them through Professional Courier\nService for sale to others.\n3. The learned counsel appearing for the petitioner submitted\nthat the petitioner is innocent and has not committed any offence as\nalleged by the prosecution. He further submitted that the petitioner\nhas been in judicial custody since 12.09.2026.\n__________\nPage 2 of 6\nhttps://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis\n\nCRL OP(MD) No. 24107 of 2026\n4. The learned Government Advocate (Criminal Side)\nappearing for the respondent police submitted that the petitioner has\ntwo previous cases under the NDPS Act and other offences and that\nthe co-accused (A2) had already been enlarged on bail by this Court\nin Crl.O.P.(MD) No.21856 of 2026 vide order dated 28.09.2026.\n5. Though the petitioner was granted bail in two earlier cases,\nconsidering the fact that the co-accused (A2) was also granted bail\nby this Court on 28.09.2026 and taking into account the period of\nincarceration of 40 days, this Court is inclined to grant bail to the\npetitioner, subject to the certain conditions.\n6. Accordingly, the petitioner is ordered to be released on bail\non his executing a bond for a sum of Rs.10,000/- (Rupees Ten\nThousand only) with two sureties each for a like sum to the\nsatisfaction of the learned Judicial Magistrate No.I, Thanjavur and\non further conditions as follows:-\n[a] The petitioner and the sureties shall affix their photographs\nand left thumb impression in the surety bond and the Magistrate may\nobtain a copy of their Aadhaar card or bank pass book to ensure their\nidentity;\n[b] On execution of the surety, the accused is directed to\nappear before the learned Judicial Magistrate No.I, Thanjavur for a\nperiod of 30 working days at 10.30 am. Thereafter, the accused\n__________\nPage 3 of 6\nhttps://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis\n\nCRL OP(MD) No. 24107 of 2026\nshall appear before the said Court on every Wednesday at 10.30 am\nfor a period of 10 weeks;\n[c] In the event that the accused is unable to appear before the\nsaid Court, the counsel for the accused may file accused absence\npetition on behalf of the accused under Section 355 of BNSS and the\nsame may be considered by the Court;\n[d] In the event that neither the accused appear nor his counsel\nfile any such accused absent petition, the Court has to issue a Non\nBailable Warrant against the accused and secure him and commit\nhim to custody;\n[e] If the accused thereafter absconds, a fresh FIR shall be\nregistered under Section 269 BNS, 2023;\n[f] If the investigating agency requires the presence of the\naccused, after the execution of the bail bond, the Investigating\nOfficer has to issue a summons to the accused for interrogation.\nHowever, the interrogation should not amount to harassment of the\naccused. The issuance of the summons to the accused and the\ninterrogation of the accused should be reflected in the CD file as\nwell as in the General Diary. The said exercise shall be done by the\nInvestigating Officer at once or twice during the daytime. Once the\npurpose of the interrogation is over, the accused shall be sent out\nfrom the police station without any further delay;\n[g] On compliance of the above conditions for appearance of\nthe accused all the conditions referred above shall stand relaxed;\n[h] The petitioner shall not tamper with the evidence or\nwitness either during investigation or trial;\n__________\nPage 4 of 6\nhttps://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis\n\nCRL OP(MD) No. 24107 of 2026\n[i] The petitioner shall not abscond either during investigation\nor trial;\n[j] On breach of any of the aforesaid conditions, the learned\nMagistrate / Trial Court is entitled to take appropriate action against\nthe petitioner in accordance with law as if the conditions have been\nimposed and the petitioner is released on bail by the learned\nMagistrate / Trial Court himself as laid down by the Hon'ble\nSupreme Court in P.K.Shaji vs. State of Kerala [(2005)AIR SCW\n5560].\n23.10.2026\nIndex: Yes/No\nSpeaking/Non-speaking order\nNeutral Citation: Yes/No\nJEN\nTo\n1. The Judicial Magistrate No.I, Thanjavur\n2. The Inspector of Police,\nThanjavur Town West Police Station,\nThanjavur District.\n3. The Additional Public Prosecutor,\nMadurai Bench of Madras High Court,\nMadurai.\n4. The prison in-charge,\nSubJail, Thanjavur.\n__________\nPage 5 of 6\nhttps://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis\n\nCRL OP(MD) No. 24107 of 2026\nDR.P.MURUGAN, J.\nJEN\nCRL OP(MD) No. 24107 of 2026\n23.10.2026\n__________\nPage 6 of 6\nhttps://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis	6	t	HCMD011528062026	Criminal Original Petition (Bail)	2026-10-23	Single Bench	Abishek	State of Tamilnadu Rep. by The Inspector of Police	Mr.A.Arun Prasad,	Mr.N.Balasubramanian Government Advocate (Crl. Side)	Civil & Constitutional Law	In this matter, the Madras High Court (Madurai Bench) adjudicated issues between Abishek and State of Tamilnadu Rep. by The Inspector of Police. The Court rendered a decision disposing of the application under statutory provisions.	0	2026 LexGuard (MHC) 060B0443	{"court": "Madras High Court (Madurai Bench)", "title": "Abishek v. State of Tamilnadu Rep. by The Inspector of Police", "case_id": "060b0443-5dee-4738-b15d-a1b2d4892706", "case_no": "NO. 24107 of 2026", "parties": "Abishek v. State of Tamilnadu Rep. by The Inspector of Police", "category": "NDPS", "petitioner": "Abishek", "respondent": "State of Tamilnadu Rep. by The Inspector of Police", "legal_domain": "Civil & Constitutional Law", "category_facts": {"category": "NDPS", "custody_period": null, "contraband_type": "Contraband / Narcotics", "seized_quantity": null, "statutory_issue": "Bail / Pre-trial Release under NDPS Act", "quantity_category": "Intermediate Quantity", "section_37_embargo": false, "search_compliance_sec_50": "Search procedure evaluated"}, "activity_events": [], "profile_version": "2.5", "statutory_matrix": [], "activity_clusters": [], "scenario_clusters": ["narcotics_contraband"], "scenario_keywords": ["ndps"], "procedural_posture": {"remedy": "Disposed", "disposition": "Disposed"}}
