e Deputy Superintendent Of Police,\nSamayanallur, Madurai, Madurai District.\n3. The Inspector of Police,\nAlanganallur, Madurai District.\n4. V. Rajagopal\n... Respondents\nPRAYER: Criminal Original Petition is filed under Section 528 of BNSS Act,\nto direct the respondent 2 and 3 herein not to harass the petitioner and his\nfamily members by considering the pendency of the civil suit in O.S.No.\n247/2026 on the file of the VI Additional District Court, Madurai.\nFor Petitioner : Mr.M.Thirunavukkarasu\nFor Respondents : Mr.B.Arun\nGovernment Advocate (Crl.Side)\nfor R1 to R3\n1/4\n\nCrl.OP(MD) No.13330 of 2026\nORDER\nThe present petition has been filed to direct the second and third\nrespondents police not to interfere in the civil dispute and harass the petitioner\nunder the guise of enquiry.\n2.It could be seen from the records that the 4th respondent herein is\nthe brother of the petitioner and the petitioner has already filed a suit in OS No.\n247 of 2026 before the VI Additional District Court, Madurai seeking the reliefs\nof declaration and partition and the same is pending. The 4th respondent has\nlodged a complaint as against the petitioner herein and an FIR has been\nregistered as against the petitioner on 01.06.2026 in Cr.No.251 of 2026 on the\nfile of third respondent police and in which, the petitioner is alleged to have\ncommitted offence under Sections 296(b), 351(2) of BNS.\n3.The learned counsel appearing for the petitioner submitted that\nthe third respondent is insisting the petitioner to withdraw the civil suit.\n2/4\n\nCrl.OP(MD) No.13330 of 2026\n4.In such view of the matter, there shall be a direction to the\nrespondents police not to summon the petitioner, except by issuance of notice\nunder Section 35 of BNSS (Section 41A of Cr.P.C).\n5.With the aforesaid observations, this Criminal Original Petition\nstands disposed of.\n06.07.2026\nNCC : Yes/No\nIndex : Yes/No\nInternet: Yes/No\nPNM\nTo\n1. The Superintendent of Police,\nMadurai Rural, Madurai District.\n2. The Deputy Superintendent Of Police,\nSamayanallur, Madurai, Madurai District.\n3. The Inspector of Police,\nAlanganallur, Madurai District.\n4.The Additional Public Prosecutor,\nMadurai Bench of Madras High Court, Madurai.\n3/4\n\nCrl.OP(MD) No.13330 of 2026\nR.VIJAYAKUMAR , J .\nPNM\nORDER MADE IN\nCrl.OP.(MD)No.13330 of 2026\n06.07.2026\n4/4	4	t	HCMA010133302026	Criminal Original Petition	2026-07-06	Single Bench	V.Balaji ... Petitioner	Superintendent of Police, Madurai Rural & Ors.	Mr.M.Thirunavukkarasu	Mr.B.Arun Government Advocate (Crl.Side)	Civil Law	In this judgment under Civil Law, the Court ruled on the dispute between 17Agnxj Yqrgvbuhnu2C9Qlnrlqq9E2Pe Home   Judgements And Orders, Supreme Court And High Courts Of India and the Respondent.	0	2026 LexGuard (Judg) 02A7CB	{"court": "Madras High Court (Principal Seat, Chennai)", "title": "V.Balaji v. Superintendent of Police, Madurai Rural & Ors.", "case_id": "02a7cb61-54db-46b1-a53f-74ffff99be92", "case_no": "Crl.OP(MD) No.13330 of 2026", "parties": "V.Balaji v. Superintendent of Police, Madurai Rural & Ors.", "category": "QUASHING", "petitioner": "V.Balaji", "respondent": "Superintendent of Police, Madurai Rural & Ors.", "legal_domain": "Civil Law", "category_facts": {"category": "QUASHING", "civil_cloak": true, "quash_ground": "Purely civil transaction given criminal cloak", "compromise_affidavit": false, "bhajan_lal_principles": true, "proceedings_challenged": "First Information Report (FIR)"}, "activity_events": [], "profile_version": "2.5", "statutory_matrix": [], "activity_clusters": [], "scenario_clusters": [], "scenario_keywords": [], "procedural_posture": {"remedy": "Allowed", "disposition": "Allowed"}}
