HANI\n==========================================================\nApproved for Reporting Yes No\n✔\n==========================================================\nSTATE OF GUJARAT\nVersus\nANILSINH DIPSINH CHAUHAN & ANR.\n==========================================================\nAppearance:\nMR ROHAN RAVAL APP for the Appellant(s) No. 1\nMR DK DESAI(278) for the Opponent(s)/Respondent(s) No. 1,2\nMS DARSHANA TRIVEDI(2388) for the Opponent(s)/Respondent(s) No. 1,2\n==========================================================\nCORAM:HONOURABLE MR. JUSTICE ILESH J. VORA\nand\nHONOURABLE MR. JUSTICE R. T. VACHHANI\nDate : 22/10/2026\nORAL JUDGMENT\n(PER : HONOURABLE MR. JUSTICE R. T. VACHHANI)\n1. Feeling aggrieved and dissatisfied with the judgment and order of\nacquittal dated 16/08/2002 passed by the learned Additional Sessions\nJudge, Ahmedabad Rural in Sessions Case No.57 of 2000 acquitting the\nrespondents- accused from the charge of offence punishable under\nSections 504, 302 and 34 of the Indian Penal Code and under Section 135\nPage 1 of 21\n\nR/CR.A/1040/2002 JUDGMENT DATED: 22/10/2026\n(GJHC240303002002)\nof the Bombay Police Act, the appellant – State has preferred the present\nappeal under Section 378(1)(3) of the Code of Criminal Procedure, 1973\n(for short “the Code”).\n2. The brief facts leading to the filing of the present appeals, are as\nunder:\n2.1. The prosecution case in brief is that the complainant is residing at\nvillage Kolvada, district: Gandhinagar with his family and he is earning\nhis livelihood by way of driving rickshaw. That on 21.8.2000 complainant\ncame to his village and at about 9 O'clock, he was in the Hanuman\nMandir situated in the same village. At that time, his uncle's son\nArvindsinh Waghela came there running and informed him that the\nbrother of the complainant Dilipsinh had a quarrel with the accused at\nthree road Kolwada and that accused Anilsinh had given knife blows to\nDilipsinh. He, further, informed the complainant that Dilipsinh is\nadmitted in the Civil Hospital, Gandhinagar. The complainant, therefore,\nrushed to Gandhinagar, Civil Hospital, where his brother informed him\nthat he was traveling in the rickshaw of Vanrajsinh and that rickshaw\ncollided with the rickshaw of accused No.1. Anilsinh. Rickshaw of\nAnilsinh had some damage and, therefore, in order to avoid quarrel\nDilipsinh told Anilsinh that he would pay the repairing charges of the\nRickshaw. However, while the deceased Dilipsinh was standing near\nthree road of Kolvada, the accused came to him and started quarreling.\nThat accused No.3 Pravinsinh Hamtuji Chauhan and the deceased\nChampaksinh alias Bhurio Dipsinh Chauhan caught hold of the deceased\nand Anilsinh Dipsinh Chauhan inflicted knife blows on the stomach and\nhand of the deceased. Thereafter, the deceased became unconscious. He\nPage 2 of 21\n\nR/CR.A/1040/2002 JUDGMENT DATED: 22/10/2026\n(GJHC240303002002)\nwas then shifted to Ahmedabad Civil Hospital where he died during\ntreatment. The complaint was filed with Pethapur Police Station and the\nPolice after investigation chargesheeted the accused. However, the\noriginal accused No.2 Champaksinh alias Bhurio Dipsinh Chauhan\nexpired during the pendency of the trial and, therefore, the case against\nhim is abated.\n3. In pursuance of the complaint lodged by the complainant,\ninvestigating agency recorded statements of the witnesses, collected\nrelevant evidence in form of medical evidence and drawn various\nPanchnamas and other relevant evidence for the purpose of proving the\noffence. After having found material against the respondent accused,\ncharge-sheet came to be filed in the Court of learned JMFC, as said Court\nlacked jurisdiction to try the offence, it committed the case to the\nSessions Court provided under section 209 of the Code	21	t	GJHC010010402026	Criminal Appeal	2026-10-22	Single Bench	STATE OF GUJARAT	Anilsinh Dipsinh Chauhan & Anr.	\N	\N	Civil Law	In this judgment under Criminal Law, the C