06296748-a41c-4985-9592-f012bcc1b965	CRM (NDPS) 2334 of 2026	Petitioner v. Respondent / State	High Court of Judicature	2026	Hon'ble Bench	Petitioner v. Respondent / State	["Immigration and Foreigners Act", "NDPS Act", "Narcotic Drugs and Psychotropic Substances Act, 1985", "the Code"]	["Section 21 Immigration and Foreigners Act", "Section 21(c) NDPS Act", "Section 29 NDPS Act", "Section 439 the Code"]	["civil & constitutional law", "hc", "disposed"]	Judgment in Matter No. B43ED5CC/2026 delivered by Hon'ble Bench at High Court of Judicature. The proceedings concern Civil & Constitutional Law with respect to Section 439.	Disposed	storage/cases/HC_2026_Matter_No_B43ED5CC_2026_06296748.pdf	b43ed5cc281e46ec5693d835a1b77a4e615e46072e0379a94f0f50537a0f39ea	\N	\N	\N	published	657396f3-5181-4922-8323-72d78b963be0	657396f3-5181-4922-8323-72d78b963be0	2026-10-25 14:51:35.926062+05:30	2026-10-25 14:51:35.926066+05:30	2026-10-26 10:38:07.691271+05:30	\N	[]	Holding and principles affirmed in Matter No. B43ED5CC/2026 regarding Civil & Constitutional Law. The Court adjudicated upon Section 439.	[]	Disposed	[]	\N	unverified	Good Law (Binding Precedent)	23.10.2026\nSl. No. 03\nCt. No. 7\nA.N.\n(Vacation Bench)\n(ALLOWED)\nC.R.M. (NDPS) 2334 OF 2026\nIn Re : An application for bail under Section 439 of the Code of\nCriminal Procedure, 1973 corresponding to Section 483 of the\nBhartiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita, 2023 in connection with N\n143/2026 arising out of Bagdah Police Station Case No.\n468/2026 dated 28.06.2026 under Sections 21(c)/29 of the\nNDPS Act, 1985 and Section 21 of the Immigration and\nForeigners Act.\nAnd\nIn the matter of : Abdul Ahad Khan alias AAhat Khan\n…. Petitioner\nMr. Angshuman Chakraborty\nMr. S. S. Saha\n… For the petitioner\nMr. Gouranga Kumar Das\nMr. Amal Kumar Datta\nMr. Debayan Ghosh\n… for the State\n1. The petitioner and the State are represented.\n2. It is submitted that the present accused petitioner has\nbeen falsely implicated in the present case and the basis of\nthe implication of the present accused petitioner is the\nstatement of the co-accused.\n3. Learned advocate representing the State submits before\nthis Court that from the materials as placed before this\nCourt, it would reveal that the present petitioner is\nactively involved in the alleged crime.\n\n4. On careful perusal of the entire materials as available in\nthe case diary, it appears that no contraband was seized\nfrom the possession of the co-accused. It further appears\nthat the name of the present accused petitioner transpires\nfrom the statement of the co-accused.\n5. Considering such circumstances, this Court is inclined to\nallow the prayer for bail of the present petitioner.\n6. It is ordered that the present petitioner namely Abdul\nAhad Khan alias AAhat Khan shall be released on bail\nupon furnishing a Bond of Rs. 20,000/- with two\nregistered sureties of Rs. 10,000/- each subject to the\nsatisfaction of the learned Chief Judicial Magistrate,\nBarasat, North 24 Parganas and also on condition that the\naccused /petitioner shall meet the investigating officer of\nthis case thrice in a week till conclusion of the\ninvestigation.\n7. In the event, the charge sheet is filed against the\npetitioner, he is directed to appear before the learned Trial\nCourt on each and every date of substantive hearing and\nshall not leave the territorial jurisdiction of the learned\nTrial Court till conclusion of the trial unless specifically\npermitted by the learned Trial Court.\n8. Accordingly CRM (NDPS) 2334 of 2026 stands disposed\nof.\n\n9. All parties shall act on the server copy of this order duly\ndownloaded from the official website of this Court.\n10.Urgent photostat certified copy of this order, duly applied\nfor, be given to the parties upon compliance of all usual\nrequisite formalities.\n(Partha Sarathi Sen, J.).	3	t	HCMA010000432026	Bail Application (NDPS)	2026-10-23	Single Bench	Petitioner	Respondent / State	\N	\N	Civil & Constitutional La