", "ratio_key": "Section 41A CrPC notice and safeguards against automatic arrest", "treatment": "Followed / Relied Upon"}]	https://mhc.tn.gov.in/judis	verified	Good Law	CONT.P.(MD)No.1532 of 2025\n\nDATED : 18.06.2025\nCORAM:\nTHE HONOURABLE MR.JUSTICE S.M.SUBRAMANIAM\nAND\nTHE HONOURABLE DR.JUSTICE A.D.MARIA CLETE\nCont.P.(MD)No.1532 of 2025\nin\nCriminal Appeal.No.1277 of 2014\nR.Udhayakumar ... Petitioner\nVs.\n1.Lingapandian,\nInspector of Police,\nTown Police Station,\nSivagangai.\n(Currently in Avaniyapuram Police Station,\nMadurai)\n2.Hari Krishnan,\nSub Inspector of Police,\nTown Police Station,\nSivagangai.\n(Currently in Taluk Police Station, Sivagangai)\n3.Ilayaraja,\nSub Inspector of Police,\nTown Police Station,\nSivagangai. ...Respondents\n1/4\n\nCONT.P.(MD)No.1532 of 2025\nPRAYER: Petition filed under Section 11 of the Contempt of Courts Act, to\npunish the respondents for their willful disobedience of the order made in CA.No.\n1277 of 2014, dated 02.07.2014 on the file of the Hon'ble Supreme Court.\nFor Petitioner : Mr.R.Maanjal Kumar\nFor Respondents : Mr.T.Senthil Kumar,\nAdditional Public Prosecutor\nORDER\n(Order of the Court was made by S.M.SUBRAMANIAM, J.)\nThis Contempt Petition has been instituted to punish the respondents for\ntheir willful disobedience of the order made in CA.No.1277 of 2014, dated\n02.07.2014 on the file of the Hon'ble Supreme Court of India in the case of\nArnesh Kumar Vs. State of Bihar and another.\n2.A perusal of the final report / charge sheet filed by the investigating\nofficer reveals that on 23.06.2024, the petitioner picked up quarrel with the traffic\nSub Inspector of Police and threatened him by saying that how date the Sub\nInspector of Police imposed fine for traffic violations. Thus, arrest was made due\nto necessity and considering the gravity of the offence on the spot. Thus, the\nquestion of issuance of Section 41A Cr.P.C., does not arise at all. Therefore, no\n2/4\n\nCONT.P.(MD)No.1532 of 2025\ncontempt arises in this matter. Thus, this Court do not find any reason to entertain\nthis Contempt Petition. Accordingly, this Contempt Petition stands dismissed.\n(S.M.S., J.) & (A.D.M.C., J.)\n18.06.2025\nNCC : Yes / No\nIndex : Yes / No\nYuva\nTo\n1.Lingapandian,\nInspector of Police,\nTown Police Station,\nSivagangai.\n(Currently in Avaniyapuram Police Station,\nMadurai)\n2.Hari Krishnan,\nSub Inspector of Police,\nTown Police Station,\nSivagangai.\n(Currently in Taluk Police Station, Sivagangai)\n3.Ilayaraja,\nSub Inspector of Police,\nTown Police Station,\nSivagangai.\n3/4\n\nCONT.P.(MD)No.1532 of 2025\nS.M.SUBRAMANIAM, J.\nAND\nDR.A.D.MARIA CLETE, J.\nYuva\nCONT.P.(MD)No.1532 of 2025\n18.06.2025\n4/4	4	t	HCMA010015322026	Judicial Precedent	2025-06-18	Single Bench	R.Udhayakumar ... Petitioner	Lingapandian, Inspector of Police & Ors.	Mr.R.Maanjal Kumar	Mr.T.Senthil Kumar, Additional Public Prosecutor	Civil Law	In this judgment under Civil Law, the Court ruled on the dispute between 1Nnsvgann4M4Bzahevlprgdabkokgaypv Home   Judgements And Orders, Supreme Court And High Courts Of India and the Respondent.	0	2026 LexGuard (Judg) 085825	{"court": "Madras High Court (Principal Seat, Chennai)", "title": "R.Udhayakumar v. Lingapandian & Ors.", "case_id": "08582552-2383-405e-ad45-33414c6724a5", "case_no": "CONT.P.(MD)No.1532 of 2025", "parties": "R.Udhayakumar v. Lingapandian, Inspector of Police & Ors.", "category": "GENERAL_CONSTITUTIONAL", "petitioner": "R.Udhayakumar", "respondent": "Lingapandian, Inspector of Police & Ors.", "legal_domain": "Civil Law", "category_facts": {"category": "GENERAL_CONSTITUTIONAL", "remedy_type": "Criminal Appeal Against Conviction", "judicial_disposition": "Dismissed", "constitutional_article": "Article 226 / Article 21"}, "activity_events": [], "profile_version": "2.5", "statutory_matrix": [], "activity_clusters": [], "scenario_clusters": [], "scenario_keywords": [], "procedural_posture": {"remedy": "Allowed", "disposition": "Allowed"}}
