5ea63a1c-fedc-4f0a-89f7-82cfaff70aad	NO. 34871 of 2026	Represented by Mr. S. Mohanty, Advocate v. State of Odisha and others . ... Opp. Parties Represented by	High Court of Orissa at Cuttack	2026	Hon'ble JUSTICE SASHIKANTA MISHRA	Represented by Mr. S. Mohanty, Advocate v. State of Odisha and others . ... Opp. Parties Represented by	[]	[]	["civil & constitutional law", "ohc", "disposed"]	Judgment in NO. 34871 of 2026 delivered by Hon'ble JUSTICE SASHIKANTA MISHRA at High Court of Orissa at Cuttack. The proceedings concern Civil & Constitutional Law with respect to procedural compliance.	Disposed	storage/cases/OHC_2026_NO_34871_of_2026_5ea63a1c.pdf	45d3ab55d294d85e796b021148724c8a9c923f29c9ebb2afd2be10a9ca94726a	\N	\N	\N	published	657396f3-5181-4922-8323-72d78b963be0	657396f3-5181-4922-8323-72d78b963be0	2026-10-25 14:51:51.049249+05:30	2026-10-25 14:51:51.049256+05:30	2026-10-26 10:38:08.557178+05:30	2. The Petitioner has approached this Court with the following prayer: “It is therefore humbly prayed that this Hon'ble Court may graciously be pleased to admit the case kindly issue notice to the Opp. Parties and after hearing the parties, this Hon'ble Court may be pleased to direct the Tahasildar, saintala/ Opp. Paty no.4 to consider representations under annexure-3 series and settled land vide plot No. 466 corresponding to khata No.65, mouza - Kuekeda under Saintala Tahasil in the district of Bolangir in favour of the petitioner And pass such other order/orders as would be deemed fit and proper; And for this act of kindness, the petitioner as in duty bound shall ever pray.” 3.	[]	Holding and principles affirmed in NO. 34871 of 2026 regarding Civil & Constitutional Law. The Court adjudicated upon applicable judicial standards.	[]	Disposed	[]	\N	unverified	Good Law (Binding Precedent)	IN THE HIGH COURT OF ORISSA AT CUTTACK\nW.P.(C). NO. 34871 of 2026\nODHC010830722026\nDilip Sagar .… Petitioner\nRepresented by\nMr. S. Mohanty, Advocate\n-Versus-\nState of Odisha and others .… Opp. Parties\nRepresented by\nMr. G. Mohanty, Standing Counsel\nCORAM:\nJUSTICE SASHIKANTA MISHRA\nORDER\n23.10.2026\nOrder No.\nW.P.(C). No.34871 of 2026 &\n01.\n. I.A. No.20632 of 2026\n1. This matter is taken up through hybrid mode.\n2. The Petitioner has approached this Court with the following\nprayer:\n“It is therefore humbly prayed that this Hon'ble\nCourt may graciously be pleased to admit the case kindly\nissue notice to the Opp. Parties and after hearing the\nparties, this Hon'ble Court may be pleased to direct the\nTahasildar, saintala/ Opp. Paty no.4 to consider\nrepresentations under annexure-3 series and settled land\nvide plot No. 466 corresponding to khata No.65, mouza -\nKuekeda under Saintala Tahasil in the district of Bolangir\nin favour of the petitioner\nAnd pass such other order/orders as would be\ndeemed fit and proper;\nAnd for this act of kindness, the petitioner as in duty\nbound shall ever pray.”\n3. In course of hearing, it is brought to the notice of this Court\nthat highlighting the same grievance, the Petitioner has already\nPage 1 of 2\n\nsubmitted a representation to the Tahasildar, Saintala on 8th\nSeptember, 2026. It is submitted that no decision has been taken on\nsuch representation as yet.\n4. Considering the above facts, the writ petition is disposed of\ndirecting the Tahasildar, Saintala to consider and dispose of the\nrepresentation submitted by the Petitioner after granting him\nopportunity of hearing and by passing a reasoned order within four\nweeks from today.\n5. Till such time, no coercive action shall be taken against the\nPetitioner in respect of Plot No.466 under Khata No.65 of Mouza-\nKuikeda. It goes without saying that the Tahasildar shall consider\nwhether the land can be settled in favour of the Petitioner as per the\nstatute.\n(Sashikanta Mishra)\nVacation Judge\nRojalin\nPage 2 of 2	2	t	ODHC010830722026	Judicial Precedent	2026-10-23	Single Bench	Represented by Mr. S. Mohanty, Advocate	State of Odisha and others . ... Opp. Parties Represented by	\N	\N	Civil & Constitutional Law	In this matter, the High Court of Orissa at Cuttack adjudicated issues between Represented by Mr. S. Mohanty, Advocate and State of Odisha and others . ... Opp. Parties Represented by. The Court rendered a decision disposing of the application under statutory provisions.	0	2026 LexGuard (OHC) 5EA63A1C	{"court": "High Court of Orissa at Cuttack", "title": "Represented by Mr. S. Mohanty, Advocate v. State of Odisha and others . ... Opp. Parties Represented by", "case_id": "5ea63a1c-fedc-4f0a-89f7-82cfaff70aad", "case_no": "NO. 34871 of 2026", "parties": "Represented by Mr. S. Mohanty, Advocate v. State of Odisha and others . ... Opp. Parties Represented by", "category": "GENERAL_CONSTITUTIONAL", "petitioner": "Represented by Mr. S. Mohanty, Advocate", "respondent": "State of Odisha and others . ... Opp. Parties Represented by", "legal_domain": "Civil & Constitutional Law", "category_facts": {"category": "GENERAL_CONSTITUTIONAL", "remedy_type": "Writ Petition / Criminal Appeal", "judicial_disposition": "Dismissed", "constitutional_article": "Article 226 / Article 21"}, "activity_events": [], "profile_version": "2.5", "statutory_matrix": [], "activity_clusters": [], "scenario_clusters": [], "scenario_keywords": [], "procedural_posture": {"remedy": "Disposed", "disposition": "Disposed"}}
