rimonial Equality, Article 44, Succession Rights, Law Commission\n\n================================================================================\n                                   JUDGMENT\n================================================================================\n\n1. FACTS OF THE CASE:\nPublic interest litigation seeking uniform matrimonial property rights and maintenance standards for women regardless of religious denomination.\n\n2. ISSUES FRAMED:\nDoes disparity in maintenance and succession laws across personal codes violate equality under Articles 14 and 15?\n\n3. LEGAL RATIO & FINDINGS:\nGender justice and equal matrimonial protections are fundamental constitutional imperatives that transcend statutory distinctions.\n\n4. FINAL ORDER:\nWrit Petition Disposed; Law Commission requested to submit final report on inter-faith matrimonial equality within 6 months.\n\nOrdered and decreed accordingly.\n\nHon'ble Constitution Bench (3 Judges)\nSupreme Court of India\n[LEXGUARD REPOSITORY CRYPTOGRAPHIC SEAL]\n	3	t	SCIN010002102026	Writ Petition	\N	Single Bench	Dr. Subhash Kashyap	Union of India & Ors.	\N	\N	Constitutional Law	In this writ petition under Constitutional Law, the Court ruled on the dispute between Dr. Subhash Kashyap and Union of India & Ors..	0	2026 LexGuard (Writ) 6C645C	{"court": "Supreme Court of India", "title": "Dr. Subhash Kashyap v. Union of India & Ors.", "case_id": "6c645cde-d3e0-4504-bb37-039ab20f9364", "case_no": "W.P.(Civil) No. 210 of 2026", "parties": "Dr. Subhash Kashyap (Constitutional Scholar)", "category": "GENERAL_CONSTITUTIONAL", "petitioner": "Dr. Subhash Kashyap", "respondent": "Union of India & Ors.", "legal_domain": "Constitutional Law", "category_facts": {"category": "GENERAL_CONSTITUTIONAL", "remedy_type": "Writ Petition / Criminal Appeal", "judicial_disposition": "Dismissed", "constitutional_article": "Article 226 / Article 21"}, "activity_events": [], "profile_version": "2.5", "statutory_matrix": [{"act": "CONSTITUTION", "section": "14", "canonical": "Section 14 CONSTITUTION", "equivalents": []}, {"act": "CONSTITUTION", "section": "15", "canonical": "Section 15 CONSTITUTION", "equivalents": []}, {"act": "CONSTITUTION", "section": "21", "canonical": "Section 21 CONSTITUTION", "equivalents": []}, {"act": "CONSTITUTION", "section": "44", "canonical": "Section 44 CONSTITUTION", "equivalents": []}], "activity_clusters": [], "scenario_clusters": ["constitutional_fundamental"], "scenario_keywords": ["article 14", "article 21"], "procedural_posture": {"remedy": "Disposed", "disposition": "Disposed"}}
