strict\n... Respondent(s)\n\nSTATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:\nMines and Minerals (Development and Regulation) Act 1957, Code of Criminal Procedure 1973\n\nSECTIONS & PROVISIONS:\nMMDR Act Section 21, CrPC Section 451, BNSS Section 497\n\nKEY TOPICS & ISSUES:\nIllegal Sand Mining, Vehicle Seizure, Interim Custody, Section 451 CrPC, District Mineral Foundation\n\n================================================================================\n                                   JUDGMENT\n================================================================================\n\n1. FACTS OF THE CASE:\nVehicle seized for transporting river sand without valid e-transit pass. Magistrate dismissed interim custody petition.\n\n2. ISSUES FRAMED:\nShould commercial vehicles seized in mineral offenses be kept idle in police stations causing natural decay?\n\n3. LEGAL RATIO & FINDINGS:\nSeized commercial vehicles should not be allowed to rust at police stations; conditional interim custody must be granted under Sunderbhai Ambalal Desai.\n\n4. FINAL ORDER:\nInterim Custody Granted with conditions; Tipper lorry released subject to deposit of Rs. 1 Lakh before mineral foundation.\n\nOrdered and decreed accordingly.\n\nHon'ble Justice K.K. Ramakrishnan\nMadras High Court (Madurai Bench)\n[LEXGUARD REPOSITORY CRYPTOGRAPHIC SEAL]\n	3	t	HCMD010051202026	Criminal Original Petition	\N	Single Bench	P. Chelladurai	State represented by Inspector of Police	\N	\N	Civil Law	In this criminal original petition under Criminal Law, the Court ruled on the dispute between P. Chelladurai and State represented by Inspector of Police.	0	2026 LexGuard (Crim) 73E228	{"court": "Madras High Court (Madurai Bench)", "title": "P. Chelladurai v. State represented by Inspector of Police", "case_id": "73e228cc-0e67-4536-bfd9-228f1cad770a", "case_no": "Crl.O.P.(MD) No. 5120 of 2026", "parties": "P. Chelladurai", "category": "QUASHING", "petitioner": "P. Chelladurai", "respondent": "State represented by Inspector of Police", "