riminal Procedure 1973, Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita 2023\n\nSECTIONS & PROVISIONS:\nCrPC Section 437(5), CrPC Section 439(2), BNSS Section 483(3)\n\nKEY TOPICS & ISSUES:\nBail Cancellation, Supervening Circumstances, Tampering with Evidence, Personal Liberty, High Threshold\n\n================================================================================\n                                   JUDGMENT\n================================================================================\n\n1. FACTS OF THE CASE:\nState sought cancellation of bail granted to political activist on grounds that he addressed public rallies criticizing the investigating agency.\n\n2. ISSUES FRAMED:\nWhat constitute valid legal grounds for cancelling bail under Section 439(2) CrPC / Section 483(3) BNSS?\n\n3. LEGAL RATIO & FINDINGS:\nRejection of bail and cancellation of bail stand on entirely different legal footings; bail cannot be cancelled without cogent proof of witness tampering.\n\n4. FINAL ORDER:\nCriminal Appeal Dismissed; Bail cancellation refused; No evidence of witness tampering or misuse of liberty.\n\nOrdered and decreed accordingly.\n\nHon'ble Justice B.R. Gavai & Justice Sandeep Mehta\nSupreme Court of India\n[LEXGUARD REPOSITORY CRYPTOGRAPHIC SEAL]\n	3	t	SCIN010008902026	Criminal Appeal	\N	Single Bench	State of Maharashtra	Sanjay Nirupam	\N	\N	Civil Law	In this criminal appeal under Criminal Law, the Court ruled on the dispute between State of Maharashtra and Sanjay Nirupam.	0	2026 LexGuard (Crim) 750436	{"court": "Supreme Court of India", "title": "State of Maharashtra v. Sanjay Nirupam", "case_id": "750436f8-352a-4144-8ad5-22c28d635bd2", "case_no": "Crl.A. No. 890 of 2026", "parties": "State of Maharashtra", "category": "BAIL_SUSPENSION", "petitioner": "State of Maharashtra", "respondent": "Sanjay Nirupam", "legal_domain": "Civil Law", "category_facts": {"category": "BAIL_SUSPENSION", "surety_count": null, "custody_period": null, "application_type": "Regular Bail", "bai