LI SHANKAR\nCRL OP(MD). No.22381 of 2026\n1.Balamurugan\n2.Uma Maheswari\n3.Latha\n... Petitioners/\nAccused\nVs\nThe State of Tamil Nadu rep by\nThe Inspector of Police,\nVillur Police Station,\nMadurai District.\n(Crime No.70 of 2026)\n... Respondent/\nComplainant\nFor Petitioners: Mr.S.Pradeep,\nAdvocate\nFor Respondent : Mr.T.Lenin Kumar,\nAdditional Public Prosecutor\nPETITION FOR BAIL Under Section 483 of B.N.S.S.\nPRAYER :-\nFor Bail in Crime No.70 of 2026 on the file of the\nRespondent Police.\n1/8\n\nCRL OP(MD). No.22381 of 2026\nORDER : The Court made the following order :-\nThe petitioners / accused, who were arrested and\nremanded to judicial custody on 25.08.2026 for the\noffences punishable under Sections 103(1), 191(2),\n191(3), 238, 296(b), 3(5), 351(2) and 61(2) BNS, in\nCrime No.70 of 2026, on the file of the respondent\npolice, seek bail.\n2. The case of the prosecution is that earlier,\nthe first accused had assaulted the defacto\ncomplainant’s cousin, in respect of which a case was\nregistered. Since the defacto complainant’s brother\nMurugan had advised his cousin not to compromise in\nthe said case, the accused 1 and 2 threatened the\ndefacto complainant and his brother, Murugan. On\n19.08.2026, at about 06.50 a.m., one Muralitharan\ninformed the defacto complainant that his brother\nMurugan, had been murdered. When he went to the place\nof occurrence, some of his relatives informed him\nthat on 18.08.2026, at about 09.15 p.m., accused 1\nand 2 had quarrelled with his brother Murugan. Hence,\nan FIR was registered in Crime No.70 of 2026 on\n2/8\n\nCRL OP(MD). No.22381 of 2026\n19.08.2026 against the accused 1 and 2. Subsequently,\nbased on the confession statements allegedly given by\nthe said accused, the present petitioners were also\nimplicated in the case.\n3. The learned counsel appearing for the\npetitioners would submit that the petitioners are\ninnocent and they have not committed any offence as\nalleged by the prosecution. He would further submit\nthat the petitioners are in judicial custody from\n25.08.2026.\n4. The learned Additional Public Prosecutor\nappearing for the respondent police would submit that\nthere are totally five accused in this case and the\npetitioners are arrayed as accused 3 to 5, that the\npetitioners 1 and 2 are the parents of the first\naccused and the third petitioner is the mother of the\nsecond accused, that the specific overt act\nattributed to the first petitioner is that he\ninstigated the accused 1 and 2, whereas, the\npetitioners 2 and 3 allegedly concealed the evidence,\n3/8\n\nCRL OP(MD). No.22381 of 2026\nthat the accused 1 and 2 are still in custody and\nthat the investigation is pending. He would further\nsubmit that the petitioners are not having any\nprevious cases.\n5. Considering the nature of the charges\nlevelled against the petitioners and also the facts\nthat the petitioners are in judicial custody from\n25.08.2026 and that the petitioners are not having\nany bad antecedents, this Court is inclined to grant\nbail to the petitioners subject to the following\nconditions:\n6. Accordingly, the petitioners are ordered to\nbe released on bail on their executing a bond for a\nsum of Rs.25,000/- (Rupees Twenty Five Thousand only)\neach with two sureties each for a like sum to the\nsatisfaction of the learned Judicial Magistrate,\nPeraiyur, and on further conditions that:\n(i)the sureties shall affix their photographs\nand left thumb impression in the surety bond and the\nMagistrate / concerned court may obtain a copy of\n4/8\n\nCRL OP(MD). No.22381 of 2026\ntheir Aadhar card or Bank Pass Book to ensure their\nidentity;\n(ii)the petitioners shall stay at Viluppuram and\nreport before the Inspector of Police, Viluppuram\nTown Police Station, Viluppuram, daily at 10.30 a.m.,\nfor a period of thirty (30) days and thereafter,\nbefore the respondent police for a period of fifteen\n(15) days and thereafter as and when required for\ninterrogation;\n(iii)the petitioners shall not tamper with the\nevidence or witness either during investigation or\ntrial;\n(iv)the petitioners shall not abscond either\nduring investigation or trial;\n(v)On breach of any of the aforesaid conditions,\nthe learned Magistrate / Trial Court is entitled to\ntake appropriate action against the petitioners in\naccordance with law as if the conditions have been\nimposed and the petitioners are released on bail by\nthe learned Magistrate / Trial Court himself as laid\ndown by the Hon'ble Supreme Court in P.K.Shaji vs.\nState of Kerala [(2005)AIR SCW 5560];\n(vi)If the accused thereafter abscond, a fresh\nFIR can be registered under Section 269 BNS, 2023.\n(K M S J)\n09.10.2026\nCSM\n5/8\n\nCRL OP(MD). No.22381 of 2026\nTO\n1. The Judicial Magistrate,\nPeraiyur.\n2. Do through\nThe Chief Judicial Magistrate,\nMadurai.\n3. The Superintendent,\nCentral Prison,\nMadurai.\n4. The Superintendent,\nCentral Prison (Women),\nMadurai.\n5. The Inspector of Police,\nVillur Police Station,\nMadurai District.\n6. The Inspector of Police,\nViluppuram Town Police Station,\nViluppuram.\n7. The Additional Public Prosecutor,\nMadurai Bench of Madras High Court,\nMadurai.\n6/8\n\nCRL OP(MD). No.22381 of 2026\n7/8\n\nCRL OP(MD). No.22381 of 2026\nK.MURALI SHANKAR,J\nCSM\nORDER\nIN\nCRL OP(MD) No.22381 of 2026\nDate : 09.10.2026\n8/8	8	t	HCMA010223812026	Criminal Original Petition (Bail)	\N	Single Bench	Accused	State of Tamil Nadu Rep. by Inspector of Police, Villur	Mr.S.Pradeep,	Mr.T.Lenin Kumar, Additional Public Prosecutor	Civil Law	In this criminal original petition under Civil Law, the Court ruled on the dispute between 13 Crl-Op-Md-22381-2026 and the Respondent.	0	2026 LexGuard (Crim) 72CA7C	{"court": "Madras High Court (Principal Seat, Chennai)", "title": "Balamurugan & Ors. v. State of Tamil Nadu Rep. by Inspector of Police, Villur", "case_id": "72ca7cb1-bf6d-4853-8474-d6f8fc2cb386", "case_no": "CRL OP(MD). No.22381 of 2026", "parties": "Balamurugan & Ors. v. State of T