ce D. Krishnakumar & Justice P.B. Balaji\n\nPARTIES:\nK. Balasubramanian and 14 others\n... Appellant(s) / Petitioner(s)\nVersus\nState of Tamil Nadu represented by Principal Secretary, Revenue Department & District Collector, Kancheepuram\n... Respondent(s) / State\n\nSTATUTORY PROVISIONS & ACTS REFERRED:\nRight to Fair Compensation and Transparency in Land Acquisition Act 2013, Constitution of India\n\nSECTIONS & CLAUSES UNDER CONSIDERATION:\nRFCTLARR Act Section 11, RFCTLARR Act Section 15, Article 226, Article 300A\n\nKEY LEGAL DOMAINS & TOPICS:\nLand Acquisition, Social Impact Assessment, Public Purpose, Natural Justice, Writ of Mandamus\n\n================================================================================\n                                   JUDGMENT\n================================================================================\n\n1. FACTUAL MATRIX:\nPetitioners' agricultural lands were acquired for airport expressway expansion without publishing mandatory Social Impact Assessment study report under Section 4 and without hearing objections under Section 15.\n\n2. ISSUES FRAMED FOR ADJUDICATION:\n1. Whether compliance with Social Impact Assessment under Chapter II of RFCTLARR Act 2013 is mandatory prior to preliminary notification?\n\n3. STATUTORY FRAMEWORK & PRECEDENTS:\nSection 4 of the 2013 Act imposes an inescapable statutory obligation on the government to prepare and evaluate SIA in consultation with local authorities.\n\n4. RATIO DECIDENDI:\nAcquisition proceedings initiated without prior Social Impact Assessment study under RFCTLARR Act 2013 suffer from fatal jurisdictional defect and are void ab initio.\n\n5. FINAL DISPOSITION & ORDER:\nWrit Petition Allowed; Acquisition notifications under Act 30 of 2013 quashed for failure to conduct social impact assessment.\n\nDecreed and ordered accordingly.\n\nHon'ble Justice D. Krishnakumar & Justice P.B. Balaji\nMadras High Court (Principal Seat, Chennai)\n[LEXGUARD CRYPTOGRAPHIC VERIFIED REPOSITORY RECORD]\n	3	t	HCMA010189202026	Writ Petition	\N	Single Bench	K. Balasubramanian & Ors.	State of Tamil Nadu & Anr.	\N	\N	Constitutional Law	In this writ petition under Constitutional Law, the Court ruled on the dispute between K. Balasubramanian & Ors. and State of Tamil Nadu & Anr..	0	2026 LexGuard (Writ) 2978C8	{"court": "Madras High Court (Principal Seat, Chennai)", "title": "K. Balasubramanian & Ors. v. State of Tamil Nadu & Anr.", "case_id": "2978c861-f889-481a-aff6-307bcc352ec0", "case_no": "W.P. No. 18920 of 2026", "parties": "K. Balasubramanian and 14 others", "category": "QUASHING", "petitioner": "K. Balasubramanian & Ors.", "respondent": "State of Tamil Nadu & Anr.", "legal_domain": "Constitutional Law", "category_facts": {"category": "QUASHING", "civil_cloak": false, "quash_ground": "Absence of prima facie ingredients", "compromise_affidavit": false, "bhajan_lal_principles": true, "proceedings_challenged": "FIR / Investigation"}, "activity_events": [], "profile_version": "2.5", "statutory_matrix": [{"act": "CONSTITUTION", "section": "226", "canonical": "Section 226 CONSTITUTION", "equivalents": []}, {"act": "CONSTITUTION", "section": "300A", "canonical": "Section 300A CONSTITUTION", "equivalents": []}], "activity_clusters": [], "scenario_clusters": ["constitutional_fundamental"], "scenario_keywords": ["writ of mandamus", "article 226"], "procedural_posture": {"remedy": "Allowed", "disposition": "Allowed"}}
