2d7b2c0e-d0d3-4fca-8068-0f67e11f0f65	CRL OP No. 30764 of 2026	. Krishnaveni v. The State Rep by The Inspector of Police Kallavi Police Station, Kallavi, Krishnagiri District.	Madras High Court (Principal Seat, Chennai)	2026	Hon'ble Mr. Justice N.Ramesh	. Krishnaveni v. The State Rep by The Inspector of Police Kallavi Police Station, Kallavi, Krishnagiri District.	["Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita, 2023", "Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023", "of BNSS"]	["Section 194 of BNSS"]	["civil & constitutional law", "mhc", "disposed"]	Judgment in NO. 30764 of 2026 delivered by Hon'ble Bench at Madras High Court (Principal Seat, Chennai). The proceedings concern Civil & Constitutional Law with respect to procedural compliance.	Bail Granted	storage/cases/MHC_2026_NO_30764_of_2026_2d7b2c0e.pdf	8a6bbb5273b90466f83cd5c5f5d185106b0983811df7f5873b8bbc2ebee623d8	\N	\N	\N	published	657396f3-5181-4922-8323-72d78b963be0	657396f3-5181-4922-8323-72d78b963be0	2026-10-25 14:51:29.563656+05:30	2026-10-25 14:51:29.563661+05:30	2026-10-26 10:38:09.121817+05:30	2. The case of the prosecution is that the deceased, Arun Kumar, aged about 32 years, who was mentally challenged since birth, was suffering from chest and stomach pain. On 31.08.2026, he locked himself inside his room and shouted in pain. On 01.09.2026, the defacto complainant found him dead on his bed. Hence, the complaint. 3.	[]	Regular bail granted in CRL OP No. 30764 of 2026 under applicable statutory provisions, considering the duration of incarceration and absence of flight risk, subject to executing bond and standard reporting conditions.	[]	Allowed	["ble Supreme Court in P.K.Shaji vs. State of Kerala [(2005)13 SCC 283]"]	\N	unverified	Good Law (Binding Precedent)	CRL OP No. 30764 of 2026\nIN THE HIGH COURT OF JUDICATURE AT MADRAS\nDATED: 23-10-2026\nCORAM\nTHE HON'BLE MR.JUSTICE N.RAMESH\nCRL OP No. 30764 of 2026\nCNR: {HCMA012563802026}\n1. Krishnaveni\nW/o Ganesan,\nNo.66/99, Karuvanur,\nKallavi Village, Uthangarai Taluk,\nKrishnagiri District.\n2. Rani\nW/o Kaliappan,\nKilkurumbur Street,\nSupalli Pattu Village,\nTirupathur District.\n..Petitioner(s)\nVs\nThe State Rep by The Inspector of Police\nKallavi Police Station,\nKallavi, Krishnagiri District.\nCrime no.144 of 2026.\n..Respondent(s)\nPRAYER : Criminal Original Petition filed under Section 483 of Bharatiya\nNagarik Suraksha Sanhita, 2023, to enlarge the petitioners on bail pending\ninvestigation in Crime no.144 of 2026 on the file of the Inspector of Police,\nKallavi Police Station, Kallavi, Krishnagiri District.\nFor Petitioner(s): Mr.G.Vinodhkumar\nFor Respondent(s): Mr.M.M.I. Khaleel\nGovernment Advocate (Crl.Side)\nORDER\nThe petitioners, who were arrested and remanded to judicial custody on\n13.09.2026 for the alleged offence under Section 194 of BNSS 2023 @ Sections\n__________\nPage1 of 6\nhttps://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis\n\nCRL OP No. 30764 of 2026\n103(1), 238(a), 3(5), 332(a) of BNS, 2023 in Crime No. 144 of 2026 on the file\nof the respondent police, seeks bail.\n2. The case of the prosecution is that the deceased, Arun Kumar, aged\nabout 32 years, who was mentally challenged since birth, was suffering from\nchest and stomach pain. On 31.08.2026, he locked himself inside his room and\nshouted in pain. On 01.09.2026, the defacto complainant found him dead on his\nbed. Hence, the complaint.\n3. The learned counsel for the petitioners submitted that the petitioners\nare the mother and grandmother of the deceased, respectively. He further\nsubmitted that the deceased was mentally challenged since birth and was\nsuffering from chest and stomach pain. He further submitted that the petitioners\nhave been falsely implicated and that there is no foul play involved in the death\nof the deceased. Hence, he prayed for the grant of bail to the petitioners.\n4. Per contra, the learned Government Advocate (Criminal Side)\nappearing for the Respondent Police reiterated the prosecution case and\nsubmitted that the deceased is the son of the first petitioner. On the date of\nalleged occurrence, the first petitioner compelled the deceased to get married\nand unable to bear the torture, the deceased died by strangulation. He further\nsubmitted that the deceased was mentally ill and that was undergoing\n__________\nPage2 of 6\nhttps://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis\n\nCRL OP No. 30764 of 2026\ntreatment. However, he opposed the grant of bail to the petitioners.\n5. I have given my anxious consideration to either side submissions and\nperused the materials available on record.\n6. Considering the nature of the allegations, the mental condition of the\ndeceased, the relationship between the parties and also considering the period of\nincarceration already undergone by the petitioners, this Court is inclined to\ngrant bail to the petitioners subject to certain conditions.\n7. Accordingly, the petitioners are ordered to be released on bail on their\nexecuting a separate bond for a sum of Rs.25,000/- (Rupees Twenty Five\nThousand only) with two sureties each, for a like sum to the satisfaction of the\nlearned Judicial Magistrate, Uthangarai, and on further conditions that:\n[a] the sureties shall affix their photographs and Left\nThumb Impression in the Application for Surety slip\n[Judicial Form No.46 annexed to 'The Criminal Rules of\nPractice, 2019']. The learned Magistrate shall obtain a copy\nof any one of the identity proofs to ensure their identity;\n[b] the petitioners shall report before the respondent\npolice daily at 10.30 a.m., until further orders;\n[c] the petitioners shall not abscond either during\ninvestigation or trial;\n[d] the petitioners shall not tamper with the evidence or\n__________\nPage3 of 6\nhttps://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis\n\nCRL OP No. 30764 of 2026\nwitness either during investigation or trial;\n[e] On breach of any of the aforementioned conditions,\nthe learned Magistrate/Trial Court is entitled to pass\nappropriate orders against the petitioners in accordance with\nlaw as if the aforementioned conditions have been imposed\nand the petitioners released on bail by the learned\nMagistrate/Trial Court himself as laid down by the Hon'ble\nSupreme Court in P.K.Shaji vs. State of Kerala [(2005)13\nSCC 283];\n[f] If the accused thereafter absconds, a fresh FIR can be\nregistered under Section 269 of B.N.S.\n23-10-2026\nDRL\nNote:\n1. Registry is directed to forthwith upload\nthis order in the Official Website of this\nCourt.\n2. All concerned to act on this order being\nuploaded in Official Website of this Court\nwithout insisting on certified hard copies. To\nbe noted, this order when uploaded in the\nofficial website of this Court will be\nwatermarked and will also have a QR code.\n__________\nPage4 of 6\nhttps://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis\n\nCRL OP No. 30764 of 2026\nTo\n1.The Judicial Magistrate,\nUthangarai.\n2. The Inspector of Police\nKallavi Police Station,\nKallavi, Krishnagiri District.\n3.The Superintendent,\nSpecial Prison for Women, Vellore.\n4.The Public Prosecutor,\nHigh Court, Madras.\n__________\nPage5 of 6\nhttps://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis\n\nCRL OP No. 30764 of 2026\nN.RAMESH, J.\nDRL\nCRL OP No. 30764 of 2026\n23-10-2026\n__________\nPage6 of 6\nhttps://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis	6	t	HCMA012563802026	Criminal Original Petition (Bail)	2026-10-23	Single Bench	. Krishnaveni	The State Rep by The Inspector of Police Kallavi Police Station, Kallavi, Krishnagiri District.	Mr.G.Vinodhkumar	Mr.M.M.I. Khaleel Government Advocate (Crl.Side)	Civil & Constitutional Law	In this matter, the Madras High Court (Principal Seat, Chennai) adjudicated issues between Tirupathur District and The State Rep by The Inspector of Police Kallavi Police Station. The Court rendered a decision disposing of the application under statutory provisions.	0	2026 LexGuard (MHC) 2D7B2C0E	{"court": "Madras High Court (Principal Seat, Chennai)", "title": "Tirupathur District v. The State Rep by The Inspector of Police Kallavi Police Station", "case_id": "2d7b2c0e-d0d3-4fca-8068-0