he Superintendent of Police,\nTheni District,\nTheni\n2. The Inspector of Police,\nGudaloor North Police Station,\nTheni District,\nTheni.\n..Respondent(s)\nPRAYER: To issue a Writ of Certiorarified Mandamus to call for the records\nin Na.Ka.No.10/ inspector of police/Gudalur North Police station/2026 dated\n25.09.2026 and to quash the same as illegal and arbitrary and consequently\ndirect the 2nd Respondent to grant appropriate permission and adequate police\nprotection to conduct the Sri Mandhaiamman Koil Thiruvizhia with the Adalum\nPadalum function on 14.10.2026 within the time that may be stipulated by this\ncourt.\n__________\n\nWP Crl.(MD) No. 5602 of 2026\nFor Petitioner(s): Mr.S.Vidhya Sagar\nFor Respondent(s): Mr.C.Susikumar\nGovt. Advocate (Crl. Side)\nORDER\nThis petition has been filed challenging the rejection order passed by the\nsecond respondent in Na.Ka.No.10/ inspector of police/Gudalur North Police\nstation/2026 dated 25.09.2026 with a consequential direction to the respondents\nto grant appropriate permission and adequate police protection to conduct the\nSri Mandhaiamman Koil Thiruvizhia situated at Ankoorpalayam,\nUthamapalaiyaim, Keelagudalur, Theni with the Adalum Padalum function on\n14.10.2026.\n2. It is brought to the notice of this Court that the Director General of\nPolice, Tamil Nadu issued two circulars bearing\nRc.No.159539/Crime.4(3)/2018, signed on 31.10.2018 and\nRc.007301/GenlI(1)/2019, dated 09.04.2019, wherein instructions have been\ngiven to the Inspectors of Police throughout Tamil Nadu for consideration of\napplications seeking permission for conducting cultural programme.\n__________\n\nWP Crl.(MD) No. 5602 of 2026\n3. In view of the above, the impugned order dated 25.09.2026 is hereby\nquashed. This Writ Petition is allowed on the following conditions:-\n(a) The petitioner is permitted to conduct Adal Padal program on\n14.10.2026 from 08.00 p.m., to 10.00 p.m., in Sri Mandhaiamman Koil\nThiruvizhia situated at Ankoorpalayam, Uthamapalaiyaim,\nKeelagudalur, Theni.\n(b) The organisers, who shall be the responsible members of the festival\ncommittee, shall ensure that only cultural programs having some relevance to\nthe temple or the festival in question would be conducted and there shall not be\nany obscene display/dance being conducted;\n(c) The program shall not extend beyond 10 p.m.;\n(d) No women participating in the cultural program would be depicted or\nportrayed in an obscene or undignified manner either in the form of clothing or\notherwise;\n(e) The music that shall be used shall be in sync with the precincts of the\ntemple and double meaning songs should not be played;\n(f) There shall be no supply of alcohol or any intoxicating material in and\naround the area where cultural program is scheduled to be held;\n(g) None of the songs or dances performed in the said programme shall\n__________\n\nWP Crl.(MD) No. 5602 of 2026\nexhibit any political tone, tenor, or colour, nor shall they relate to or promote\nany religion, community, or caste.\n(h) Organizers shall not erect any digital banners/placards on either side\nof the arterial roads, platforms, walkways/major roads and any other roads;\n(i) the function should not affect caste, religious or communal harmony\nand shall be conducted without any discrimination;\n(j) The attire of the dancers performing in the said programme should be\nmodest and does not involve exposure of the midriff, thighs, legs or chest. Any\nviolation of this condition shall result in legal action, including the arrest of the\norganisers and all members of the temple committee.\n(k) the Police is empowered to stop the programme, if it exceeds beyond\nthe permitted time;\n(l) if any untoward incident takes place, the organizers of the programme\nbe made responsible for the same;\n(m) the organizers shall have to obtain all other required permission from\nthe authorities concerned;\n(n) Any other conditions as the authority concerned consider to impose\naccording to the ground reality.\n__________\n\nWP Crl.(MD) No. 5602 of 2026\nIn case of violation of any conditions, it is open to the authorities to\ninitiate such action as is required under law and the persons who are the\norganisers/committee members shall be held responsible. No costs.\n09-10-2026\nIndex: Yes/No\nSpeaking/Non-speaking order\nNeutral Citation: Yes/No\nskn\nTo\n1. The Superintendent of Police,\nTheni District,\nTheni\n2. The Inspector of Police,\nGudaloor North Police Station,\nTheni District,\nTheni.\n__________\n\nWP Crl.(MD) No. 5602 of 2026\nK.GOVINDARAJAN THILAKAVADI, J.\nskn\nWP Crl.(MD) No. 5602 of 2026\n09-10-2026\n__________	6	t	HCMD011427832026	Writ Petition	2026-10-09	Single Bench	Chandirasekaran Veeranan	1. The Superintendent of Police,	Mr.S.Vidhya Sagar	Mr.C.Susikumar Govt. Advocate (Crl. Side)	Civil Law	In this writ petition under Civil Law, the Court ruled on the dispute between 02 Wpcrl-Md-5602-2026 and the Respondent.	0	2026 LexGuard (Writ) 320D08	{"court": "Madras High Court (Principal Seat, Chennai)", "title": "Keelagudalur, v. 1. The Superintendent of Police,", "case_id": "320d080d-48b7-48c9-bb61-cb5824f014eb", "case_no": "WP Crl.(MD) No. 5602 of 2026", "parties": "02 Wpcrl-Md-5602-2026", "category": "QUASHING", "petitioner": "Keelagudalur,", "respondent": "1. The Superintendent of Police,", "legal_domain": "Civil Law", "category_facts": {"category": "QUASHING", "civil_cloak": false, "quash_ground": "Absence of prima facie ingredients", "compromise_affidavit": false, "bhajan_lal_principles": true, "proceedings_challenged": "FIR / Investigation"}, "activity_events": [], "profile_version": "2.5", "statutory_matrix": [], "activity_clusters": [], "scenario_clusters": ["constitutional_fundamental"], "scenario_keywords": ["article 226"], "procedural_posture": {"remedy": "Allowed", "disposition": "Allowed"}}
