33333333-0015-4000-8000-000000000015	Criminal Appeal No. 278 of 2021	Aparna Bhat & Senior Women Advocates v. State of Madhya Pradesh & Another	Supreme Court of India	2021	Hon'ble A.M. Khanwilkar & S. Ravindra Bhat, JJ.	Aparna Bhat & Senior Women Advocates v. State of Madhya Pradesh & Another	["Code of Criminal Procedure, 1973", "Indian Penal Code, 1860"]	["Section 437(3) CrPC", "Section 438 CrPC", "Section 354 IPC"]	["gender stereotyping in bail barred", "rakhi tying condition quashed", "dignity of victim", "judicial conduct guidelines"]	Supreme Court set aside an order directing an accused in a molestation case to tie Rakhi to the victim as a bail condition, establishing mandatory guidelines prohibiting patriarchal or compromise-inducing bail conditions in sexual offences.	Disposed	storage/cases/SC_2021_Crl_App_No_278_of_2021_33330015.pdf	6d7de01f8bf33d2e566c03c2769bc1cccfe97bea33e375792cef06baffb1a217	\N	\N	\N	published	657396f3-5181-4922-8323-72d78b963be0	657396f3-5181-4922-8323-72d78b963be0	2026-10-25 11:22:39.597683+05:30	2026-10-25 11:22:39.597689+05:30	2026-10-26 10:38:09.125804+05:30	\N	[]	Using Rakhi tying as a condition for bail transforms a molester into a brother by a judicial fiat, trivializing sexual violence. Courts must scrupulously avoid any stereotypes, moral lecturing, or forcing contact between accused and victim in bail orders.	[]	Disposed	[{"court": "Supreme Court of India", "title": "Judicial Precedent [2021) 16 SCC 241]", "status": "Good Law (External Authority)", "case_id": null, "citation": "2021) 16 SCC 241", "treatment": "Cited / Considered"}]	\N	unverified	Good Law (Binding Gender Justice Landmark)	Supreme Court of India\nCriminal Appeal No. 278 of 2021\nAparna Bhat and Others v. State of Madhya Pradesh and Another\nBench: Hon'ble A.M. Khanwilkar & S. Ravindra Bhat, JJ.\nDate: 2021-03-18\nCitation: (2021) 16 SCC 241\n\nRATIO DECIDENDI:\nUsing Rakhi tying as a condition for bail transforms a molester into a brother by a judicial fiat, trivializing sexual violence. Courts must scrupulously avoid any stereotypes, moral lecturing, or forcing contact between accused and victim in bail orders.\n\nSUMMARY:\nSupreme Court set aside an order directing an accused in a molestation case to tie Rakhi to the victim as a bail condition, establishing mandatory guidelines prohibiting patriarchal or compromise-inducing bail conditions in sexual offences.\n\nSTATUTES: Section 437(3) CrPC, Section 438 CrPC, Section 354 IPC\nDISPOSITION: Patriarchal Bail Condition Set Aside with Binding Guidelines	2	f	SCIN010002782021	Criminal Appeal	2021-03-18	Division Bench (2 Judges)	Aparna Bhat & Senior Women Advocates	State of Madhya Pradesh & Another	Senior Advocate Sanjay Parikh	Senior Advocate Saurabh Trivedi	Bail Conditions & Gender Sensitivity	Courts cannot impose ridiculous or humiliating bail conditions like tying Rakhi to a sexual abuse victim or forcing compromise. Bail conditions must strictly relate to ensuring trial appearance.	0	(2021) 16 SCC 241	{"court": "Supreme Court of India", "title": "Aparna Bhat and Others v. State of Madhya Pradesh and Another", "case_id": "33333333-0015-4000-8000-000000000015", "case_no": "Criminal Appeal No. 278 of 2021", "parties": "Aparna Bhat & Senior Women Advocates v. State of Madhya Pradesh & Another", "category": "BAIL_SUSPENSION", "petitioner": "Aparna Bhat & Senior Women Advocates", "respondent": "State of Madhya Pradesh & Another", "legal_domain": "Bail Conditions & Gender Sensitivity", "category_facts": {"category": "BAIL_SUSPENSION", "surety_count": null, "custody_period": null, "application_type": "Anticipatory Bail", "bail_bond_amount": null, "trial_court_fine": null, "reason_for_relief": null, "reporting_condition": null, "trial_court_sentence": null, "trial_court_fine_paid": false}, "activity_events": [], "profile_version": "2.5", "statutory_matrix": [{"act": "CRPC", "section": "437", "canonical": "Section 437 CRPC", "equivalents": []}, {"act": "CRPC", "section": "438", "can