ces and non-custodial bail guidelines", "treatment": "Followed / Relied Upon"}, {"court": "Supreme Court of India", "title": "Arnesh Kumar v. State of Bihar", "status": "Good Law (Binding Precedent)", "case_id": "11111111-0003-4000-8000-000000000003", "citation": "(2014) 8 SCC 273", "ratio_key": "Section 41A CrPC notice and safeguards against automatic arrest", "treatment": "Followed / Relied Upon"}]	https://mhc.tn.gov.in/judis	verified	Binding Precedent	IN THE MADRAS HIGH COURT (MADURAI BENCH)\nAT MADURAI\n\nCASE NO: Crl.O.P.(MD) No. 3421 of 2026\nCNR NUMBER: HCMD010234562026\nDECISION DATE: 2026-03-10\nYEAR: 2026\n\nCORAM / BENCH:\nHon'ble Justice B. Pugalendhi\n\nPARTIES:\nM. Karuppasamy\n... Appellant(s) / Petitioner(s)\nVersus\nThe State represented by Sub-Inspector of Police, Oomachikulam Police Station, Madurai District\n... Respondent(s) / State\n\nSTATUTORY PROVISIONS & ACTS REFERRED:\nCode of Criminal Procedure 1973, Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita 2023, Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita 2023\n\nSECTIONS & CLAUSES UNDER CONSIDERATION:\nCrPC Section 438, BNSS Section 482, BNS Section 115, BNS Section 352\n\nKEY LEGAL DOMAINS & TOPICS:\nAnticipatory Bail, Pre-Arrest Bail, Civil Dispute, Custodial Interrogation, Cooperation\n\n================================================================================\n                                   JUDGMENT\n================================================================================\n\n1. FACTUAL MATRIX:\nPetitioner sought anticipatory bail in an FIR alleging boundary dispute altercation. No grievous injury was suffered by the complainant and weapon was already recovered.\n\n2. ISSUES FRAMED FOR ADJUDICATION:\n1. Whether custodial interrogation is indispensable in land boundary scuffle when weapon is recovered?\n\n3. STATUTORY FRAMEWORK & PRECEDENTS:\nApplying Arnesh Kumar and Satender Kumar Antil principles on personal liberty under Article 21 and Section 438 CrPC / 482 BNSS.\n\n4. RATIO DECIDENDI:\nWhere offense carries punishment under 7 years and custodial interrogation is unnecessary, anticipatory bail should normally be granted.\n\n5. FINAL DISPOSITION & ORDER:\nAnticipatory Bail Granted with conditions; Petitioner directed to appear before IO daily for 2 weeks.\n\nDecreed and ordered accordingly.\n\nHon'ble Justice B. Pugalendhi\nMadras High Court (Madurai Bench)\n[LEXGUARD CRYPTOGRAPHIC VERIFIED REPOSITORY RECORD]\n	3	t	HCMD010034212026	Criminal Original Petition (Bail)	\N	Single Bench	M. Karuppasamy	The State represented by Sub-Inspector of Police	\N	\N	Civil Law	In this criminal original petition under Criminal Law, the Court ruled on the dispute between M. Karuppasamy and The State represented by Sub-Inspector of Police.	0	2026 LexGuard (Crim) 349D8B	{"court": "Madras High Court (Madurai Bench)", "title": "M. Karuppasamy v. The State represented by Sub-Inspector of Police", "case_id": "349d8b46-ba45-495e-a70b-516557061c35", "case_no": "Crl.O.P.(MD) No. 3421 of 2026", "parties": "M. Karuppasamy", "category": "BAIL_SUSPENSION", "petitioner": "M. Karuppasamy", "respondent": "The State represented by Sub-Inspector of Police", "legal_domain": "Civil Law", "category_facts": {"category": "BAIL_SUSPENSION", "surety_count": null, "custody_period": null, "application_type": "Anticipatory Bail", "bail_bond_amount": null, "trial_court_fine": null, "reason_for_relief": null, "reporting_condition": "appear before IO daily for 2 weeks", "trial_court_sentence": null, "trial_court_fine_paid": false}, "activity_events": [], "profile_version": "2.5", "statutory_matrix": [{"act": "CRPC", "section": "438", "canonical": "Section 438 CRPC", "equivalents": []}, {"act": "BNSS", "section": "482", "canonical": "Section 482 BNSS", "equivalents": ["Section 438 CrPC"]}, {"act": "BNS", "section": "115", "canonical": "Section 115 BNS", "equivalents": ["Section 323 IPC"]}, {"act": "BNS", "section": "352", "canonical": "Section 352 BNS", "equivalents": []}, {"act": "BNSS", "section": "438", "canonical