Ors.\n... Respondent(s) / State\n\nSTATUTORY PROVISIONS & ACTS REFERRED:\nInsolvency and Bankruptcy Code 2016\n\nSECTIONS & CLAUSES UNDER CONSIDERATION:\nIBC Section 30(4), IBC Section 31, IBC Section 53\n\nKEY LEGAL DOMAINS & TOPICS:\nIBC, Commercial Wisdom, Committee of Creditors, Resolution Plan, NCLAT Jurisdiction\n\n================================================================================\n                                   JUDGMENT\n================================================================================\n\n1. FACTUAL MATRIX:\nNCLAT interfered with the resolution plan approved by 88% majority of Committee of Creditors on grounds of equitable distribution to operational creditors.\n\n2. ISSUES FRAMED FOR ADJUDICATION:\n1. Is the commercial wisdom of Committee of Creditors subject to judicial review by NCLT/NCLAT on grounds of equity?\n\n3. STATUTORY FRAMEWORK & PRECEDENTS:\nReaffirming Essar Steel and K. Sashidhar: CoC commercial wisdom is non-justiciable provided statutory requirements of Section 30(2) are satisfied.\n\n4. RATIO DECIDENDI:\nJudicial review of resolution plan approved by Committee of Creditors is limited strictly to Section 30(2) IBC compliance; adjudicating authorities cannot substitute their business judgment.\n\n5. FINAL DISPOSITION & ORDER:\nCivil Appeal Allowed; NCLAT order setting aside CoC approval quashed; Commercial wisdom of CoC upheld.\n\nDecreed and ordered accordingly.\n\nHon'ble Justice Sanjiv Khanna & Justice Dipankar Datta\nSupreme Court of India\n[LEXGUARD CRYPTOGRAPHIC VERIFIED REPOSITORY RECORD]\n	3	t	SCIN010029812026	Civil Appeal	\N	Single Bench	State Bank of India	Consortium of Resolution Applicants	\N	\N	Civil Law	In this civil appeal under Civil Law, the Court ruled on the dispute between State Bank of India and Consortium of Resolution Applicants.	0	2026 LexGuard (Civi) 408BA2	{"court": "Supreme Court of India", "title": "State Bank of India v. Consortium of Resolution Applicants", "case_id": "408ba206-842c-48ba-a4b6-1c60fdd74e12", "case_no": "Civil Appeal No. 2981 of 2026", "parties": "State Bank of India (Lead Financial Creditor)", "category": "QUASHING", "petitioner": "State Bank of India", "respondent": "Consortium of Resolution Applicants", "legal_domain": "Civil Law", "category_facts": {"category": "QUASHING", "civil_cloak": false, "quash_ground": "Absence of prima facie ingredients", "compromise_affidavit": false, "bhajan_lal_principles": true, "proceedings_challenged": "First Information Report (FIR)"}, "activity_events": [], "profile_version": "2.5", "statutory_matrix": [], "activity_clusters": [], "scenario_clusters": [], "scenario_keywords": [], "procedural_posture": {"remedy": "Allowed", "disposition": "Allowed"}}
