s\nwell as the prayer made therein.\n3. The present application has been filed under Section 482 of\nBNSS, 2023 by the Petitioner seeking pre-arrest bail in connection\nwith Sundargarh Town P.S. Case No.80 of 2026, corresponding to\nG.R. Case No.272 of 2026, pending in the court of learned S.D.J.M.,\nSundargarh, for alleged commission of offences punishable under\nSection 318(4) of BNS.\nPage 1 of 3.\n\n4. At this stage, learned counsel for the Petitioner submitted that\nthe Petitioner does not want to press this bail application and seeks\nliberty to surrender before the court below and moves an application\nfor bail.\n5. Considering such submissions, the Petitioner is permitted to\nsurrender before the learned court in seisin over the matter within a\nperiod of three weeks from today and move an application for bail.\nIn such eventuality, learned court in seisin over the matter shall\nrelease the Petitioner on bail subject to such terms and conditions as\nthe learned Magistrate may deem just and proper with further\nconditions that:-\nI. shall not indulge in similar type of offences while on\nbail;\nII. shall appear before the jurisdictional Police Station once\nin a fortnight for a period three months, preferably on\n‘Sunday’ in between 10.00 A.M. to 1 P.M.\nViolation of any of the terms and conditions shall entail\ncancellation of the bail.\n6. It is further directed that the bail granted to the Petitioner shall\nbe subject to the verification of his criminal antecedent. In the event\nthe Petitioner is having more than two criminal antecedents, then\nthis order shall stand automatically revoked.\n7. It is further directed that the bail granted to the Petitioner is\nsubject to depositing of a cash security of Rs.4,000/- (Rupees Four\nThousand) before the learned Court in seisin over the matter, which\nshall be kept in any Nationalized Bank in interest bearing account\nPage 2 of 3.\n\ninitially for a period of one year which will be renewable from time\nto time till conclusion of trial and the same shall be abide by the\nfinal outcome of the trial of the case.\n8. The ABLAPL is disposed of accordingly.\nUrgent certified copy of this order be granted as per rules.\n( Aditya Kumar Mohapatra )\nVacation Judge\nS.K. Rout\nPage 3 of 3.	3	t	ODHC010799612026	Judicial Precedent	2026-10-23	Single Bench	Represented by Adv. - Manoj Kumar Panda	STATE OF ODISHA ..... Opposite Parties Smt. Siva Mohanty	\N	\N	Civil & Constitutional Law	In this matter, the High Court of Orissa at Cuttack adjudicated issues between Represented by Adv. - Manoj Kumar Panda and STATE OF ODISHA ..... Opposite Parties Smt. Siva Mohanty. The Court rendered a decision disposing of the application under statutory provisions.	0	2026 LexGuard (OHC) ACC24FA2	{"court": "High Court of Orissa at Cuttack", "title": "Represented by Adv. - Manoj Kumar Panda v. STATE OF ODISHA ..... Opposite Parties Smt. Siva Mohanty", "case_id": "acc24fa2-7433-43ed-af02-14f28fc9e90b", "case_no": "NO. 11931 of 2026", "parties": "Represented by Adv. - Manoj Kumar Panda v. STATE OF ODISHA ..... Opposite Parties Smt. Siva Mohanty", "category": "BAIL_SUSPENSION", "petitioner": "Represented by Adv. - Manoj Kumar Panda", "respondent": "STATE OF ODISHA ..... Opposite Parties Smt. Siva Mohanty", "legal_domain": "Civil & Constitutional Law", "category_facts": {"category": "BAIL_SUSPENSION", "surety_count": null, "custody_period": null, "application_type": "Anticipatory Bail", "bail_bond_amount": null, "trial_court_fine": null, "reason_for_relief": null, "reporting_condition": "appear before the jurisdictional Police Station once", "trial_court_sentence": null, "trial_court_fine_paid": false}, "activity_events": [], "profile_version": "2.5", "statutory_matrix": [], "activity_clusters": [], "scenario_clusters": [], "scenario_keywords": [], "procedural_posture": {"remedy": "Disposed", "disposition": "Disposed"}}
