421 of 2026\nRamya,\nW/o. Praveen Kumar,\nNo.25, Voc Main Street,\nSrv Nagar, Harvipatti,\nThirunagar, Madurai District.. ... Petitioner/Accused No.2\nVs\nState of Tamilnadu Rep by,\nThe Inspector of Police,\nCCB Police Station,\nMadurai District.\nCrime No.9/2026. ... Respondent/Complainant\nFor Petitioner : Mr.B. Aravinthan,\nAdvocate.\nFor Respondent : Mr.T.Lenin Kumar\nGovernment Advocate (Crl.Side)\nPETITION FOR ANTICIPATORY BAIL Under Sec.482 of BNSS\nPRAYER :- C-24AB. For Anticipatory Bail in Crime No.9/2026 on the\nfile of the Respondent Police.\n1/6\n\nCRL OP(MD). No.12421 of 2026\nORDER : The Court made the following order :-\nThe petitioner, who apprehends arrest at the hands of the\nrespondent for the offences punishable under Sections 318(4), 336(2),\n336(3) and 351(3) of BNS, 2023 in Crime No.9 of 2026 on the file of the\nrespondent police, seeks anticipatory bail.\n2. The case of the prosecution is that the defacto complainant is\nrunning V.V.Gold works by manufacturing gold jewels and gave it to\nretailers and the petitioner and her husband were introduced by one\nRajesh to the defacto complainant and the defacto complainant gave\njewels to the petitioner and her husband, who is running a business in the\nname and style of 'Sri Guhan Gold and Silvers' from the year 2023 and\nthe petitioner's husband/A1 also introduced A3 to the defacto\ncomplainant and the defacto complainant also gave jewels to him.\nThereafter, when the defacto complainant demanded a sum of Rs.\n4,20,00,000/- for the 3590 grams of jewels received by the accused, the\naccused threatened him with dire consequences and then only, he came to\nknow that they cheated him. Hence, the case.\n2/6\n\nCRL OP(MD). No.12421 of 2026\n3.This Court had earlier considered the anticipatory bail\napplications filed by the petitioner and dismissed them twice in Crl.O.P.\n(MD) Nos.2933 of 2026 and 7738 of 2026, vide orders dated 12.02.2026\nand 30.04.2026, respectively.\n4.The learned counsel appearing for the petitioner would submit\nthat the petitioner is an innocent and she was falsely implicated in this\ncase and she has no way connected in the above said incident. He would\nfurther submit that this is the third anticipatory bail petition and the\nchange in circumstances in the present petition is that the main\naccused/A1 has been released on bail. Hence, he prays to grant\nanticipatory bail to the petitioner.\n5. The learned Counsel for State of TN (Crl. Side) would submit\nthat A1 in this case was only granted default bail and so far, no recovery\nhas been effected. It is further submitted that the investigation in this\ncase is still pending. Hence, he opposes to grant anticipatory bail to the\npetitioner.\n3/6\n\nCRL OP(MD). No.12421 of 2026\n6. Heard both sides and perused the materials available on record.\n7.Considering the fact that the petitioner's bail application was\ntwice dismissed by this Court and though the petitioner relies on the\nchange in circumstance that A1 has been released on bail, the fact\nremains that A1 was released only on default bail, the investigation in\nthis case is still pending, the property has not yet been recovered and\ntherefore, there is no ground to revisit the earlier orders dismissing the\npetitioner's bail application, hence, this Court is not inclined to revisit the\nearlier orders.\n8.Accordingly, this Criminal Original Petition stands dismissed.\n(K R S J)\n23.07.2026\nVSG\n4/6\n\nCRL OP(MD). No.12421 of 2026\nTO\n1. The Inspector of Police,\nCCB Police Station,\nMadurai District.\n2. The Additional Public Prosecutor,\nMadurai Bench of Madras High Court, Madurai.\n5/6\n\nCRL OP(MD). No.12421 of 2026\nK. RAJASEKAR,J.,\nvsg\nORDER\nIN\nCRL OP(MD) No.12421 of 2026\nDate : 23/07/2026\n6/6	6	t	HCMA010124212026	Criminal Original Petition (Bail)	\N	Single Bench	Ramya	State of Tamilnadu Rep by, The Inspector of Police, CCB Police Station, Madurai District.	Mr.B. Aravinthan,	Mr.T.Lenin Kumar Government Advocate (Crl.Sid