815461d4-9059-4907-a6b1-6280fdbe49c8	WP(C) No.33935 of 2026	Represented by Adv. Mr. S. Patnaik v. State of Odisha & another ..... Opposite Parties Represented by	High Court of Orissa at Cuttack	2026	Hon'ble MR. JUSTICE SASHIKANTA MISHRA	Represented by Adv. Mr. S. Patnaik v. State of Odisha & another ..... Opposite Parties Represented by	["the Act"]	["Section 19 the Act"]	["civil & constitutional law", "ohc", "disposed"]	Judgment in NO. 33935 delivered by Hon'ble MR. JUSTICE SASHIKANTA MISHRA at High Court of Orissa at Cuttack. The proceedings concern Civil & Constitutional Law with respect to procedural compliance.	Quashed	storage/cases/OHC_2026_NO_33935_815461d4.pdf	fe2f0371fafcb08e9427b59c089b47d65936e6db98027ebc7178bbaf27f3d627	\N	\N	\N	published	657396f3-5181-4922-8323-72d78b963be0	657396f3-5181-4922-8323-72d78b963be0	2026-10-25 14:51:59.286478+05:30	2026-10-25 14:51:59.286485+05:30	2026-10-26 10:38:09.13765+05:30	The petitioner has approached this Court with the following prayer:- “The petitioner therefore humbly prays that this Hon'ble Court may graciously be pleased to issue notice to the opp. parties to show cause as to why the letter dtd.01.10.2026 and 05.10.2026 under annexure-5 and annexure- 6 respectively be not quashed and opp. Party No.6 be not be restrained from demolishing/evicting the structure of the petitioner and be further directed not to interfere with the peaceful possession and structure of the petitioner over the schedule land till the final disposal of the application under Section 19 of the Act, 1951 under annexure-7 pending before the Commissioner of Endowment and on perusal of causes shown, in any make the said rule absolute. And may pass such other order(s) deem fit and proper. Page 1 of 2. And for this act of kindness the petitioner as in duty bound shall ever pray.” 4.	[]	Criminal proceedings quashed in WP(C) No.33935 of 2026 on finding that allegations do not disclose a prima facie cognizable offence, preventing abuse of the judicial process.	[]	Allowed	[]	\N	unverified	Good Law (Binding Precedent)	IN THE HIGH COURT OF ORISSA AT CUTTACK\nWP(C) No.33935 of 2026\nCNR No. ODHC010809512026\nSrikanta Kumar Khatei ..... Petitioner\nRepresented by Adv.\nMr. S. Patnaik\n-versus-\nState of Odisha & another ..... Opposite Parties\nRepresented by\nMr. S.K.Jee, AGA\nCORAM:\nMR. JUSTICE SASHIKANTA MISHRA\nORDER\n23.10.2026\nOrder No. 1. This matter is taken up through hybrid mode.\n01\n2. Heard Mr. S. Patnaik, learned counsel for the petitioner and\nMr. S.K. Jee, learned Addl. Government Advocate for the State.\n3. The petitioner has approached this Court with the following\nprayer:-\n“The petitioner therefore humbly prays that this\nHon'ble Court may graciously be pleased to issue\nnotice to the opp. parties to show cause as to why\nthe letter dtd.01.10.2026 and 05.10.2026 under\nannexure-5 and annexure- 6 respectively be not\nquashed and opp. Party No.6 be not be restrained\nfrom demolishing/evicting the structure of the\npetitioner and be further directed not to interfere\nwith the peaceful possession and structure of the\npetitioner over the schedule land till the final\ndisposal of the application under Section 19 of the\nAct, 1951 under annexure-7 pending before the\nCommissioner of Endowment and on perusal of\ncauses shown, in any make the said rule absolute.\nAnd may pass such other order(s) deem fit and\nproper.\nPage 1 of 2.\n\nAnd for this act of kindness the petitioner as in\nduty bound shall ever pray.”\n4. In course of hearing, Mr. Patnaik referring to the letter under\nAnnexure-5 of the Tahasildar addressed to the Sub-Collector,\nNayagarh submits that the OPLE proceeding initiated against the\npetitioner has been dropped, since the land is said to be within the\nmunicipal area limits. Accordingly, the Sub-Collector, Nayagarh has\nwritten to the Executive Officer, Nayagarh Municipality by letter\ndated 05.10.2026 (Annexure-6) requesting to take legal steps to\nremove the unauthorized construction from the disputed land as per\nthe provision contained in the Odisha Municipal Act and Rules.\n5. Mr. Patnaik further submits that no action has yet been taken\nby the Nayagarh Municipality pursuant to the letter under Annexure-\n6 as yet.\n6. Having regard to the fact that several factual aspects require\nconsideration, it would not be proper for the writ Court to interfere at\nthis stage.\n7. The writ petition is disposed of directing the Executive\nOfficer, Nayagarh Municipality to grant an opportunity of hearing to\nthe petitioner and also all other necessary parties before taking a\nfinal decision in accordance with law pursuant to Annexure-6.\n8. Let a final decision be taken within three weeks from today.\nTill such time, no coercive action shall be taken against the\npetitioner in respect of the property standing over the disputed land.\n(Sashikanta Mishra)\nVacation Judge\nPage 2 of 2.\nB.C. Tudu	2	t	ODHC010809512026	Writ Petition	2026-10-23	Single Bench	Represented by Adv. Mr. S. Patnaik	State of Odisha & another ..... Opposite Parties Represented by	\N	\N	Civil & Constitutional Law	In this matter, the High Court of Orissa at Cuttack adjudicated issues between Represented by Adv. Mr. S. Patnaik and State of Odisha & another ..... Opposite Parties Represented by. The Court rendered a decision disposing of the application under statutory provisions.	0	2026 LexGuard (OHC) 815461D4	{"court": "High Court of Orissa at Cuttack", "title": "Represented by Adv. Mr. S. Patnaik v. State of Odisha & another ..... Opposite Parties Represented by", "case_id": "815461d4-9059-4907-a6b1-6280fdbe49c8", "case_no": "NO. 33935", "parties": "Represented by Adv. Mr. S. Patnaik v. State of Odisha & another ..... Opposite Parties Represented by", "category": "QUASHING", "petitioner": "Represented by Adv. Mr. S. Patnaik", "respondent": "State of Odisha & another ..... Opposite Parties Represented by", "legal_domain": "Civil & Constitutional Law", "category_facts": {"category": "