dge, City Civil Court,\nChennai.\n\nC.M.P.No.14931 of 2026 in A.S.SR.No.121873 of 2025\nR.KALAIMATHI, J.,\nssn\n2. Heard the learned counsel for the petitioner and the learned counsel\nfor the respondents.\n3. Being satisfied with the reasons stated in the affidavit filed in support\nof this petition, this petition shall stand allowed on condition of payment of\ncosts of Rs.4000/- (Rupees Four Thousand Only) payable in favour of the\nHigh Court Legal Services Authority, Chennai on or before 29.10.2026. Failing\nwhich, this petition shall automatically stand dismissed without any further\nreference to this Court.\n4. Compliance report by then.\n09.10.2026\nssn\nNote: Issue order copy on or before 12.10.2026.\nTo\nThe XIX Additional Judge,\nCity Civil Court, Chennai.\nC.M.P.No.14931 of 2026\nin\nA.S.SR.No.121873 of 2025	2	t	HCMA010149312026	Judicial Precedent	2026-10-09	Single Bench	Petitioner	Lakshmi Sigamani (Deceased) & Ors.	Mr.G.Shivasurya	Mr.Adinarayana Rao	Civil Law	In this judgment under Civil Law, the Court ruled on the dispute between 21 Cmp-14931-2026 and the Respondent.	0	2026 LexGuard (Judg) F7562E	{"court": "Madras High Court (Principal Seat, Chennai)", "title": "S.Parthiban v. Lakshmi Sigamani (Deceased) & Ors.", "case_id": "f7562e77-9b22-40e6-a2d4-ab633f42128f", "case_no": "C.M.P. No. 14931 of 2026", "parties": "S.Parthiban v. Lakshmi Sigamani (Deceased) & Ors.", "category": "COMMERCIAL_CIVIL", "petitioner": "S.Parthiban", "respondent": "Lakshmi Sigamani (Deceased) & Ors.", "legal_domain": "Civil Law", "category_facts": {"category": "COMMERCIAL_CIVIL", "dispute_type": "Commercial Dispute", "statutory_basis": "Commercial Courts Act / Civil Procedure Code", "interim_injunction_granted": false}, "activity_events": [], "profile_version": "2.5", "statutory_matrix": [], "activity_clusters": [], "scenario_clusters": [], "scenario_keywords": [], "procedural_posture": {"remedy": "Allowed", "disposition": "Allowed"}}
