ng his grievance, the Petitioner has\napproached the Commissioner, Bhubaneswar Municipal\nCorporation, while submitting a representation on 10.10.2026.\nNo action has been taken on such representation as yet.\n4. Having regard to the submissions as above, the Writ\nApplication is disposed of with a direction to the\nCommissioner, Bhubaneswar Municipal Corporation to\nconsider and dispose of the representation of the Petitioner\nafter granting him an opportunity of hearing within ten days\nfrom today.\n5. Till such time, no coercive action shall be taken against\nthe Petitioner with respect to the suit land.\n(Sashikanta Mishra)\nVacation Judge\nSipra\nPage 2 of 2.	2	t	ODHC010831792026	Writ Petition	2026-10-23	Single Bench	– Mr. Ajaya Kumar Moharana	State Of Odisha & others ..... Opposite Parties Represented by Adv. –	\N	\N	Civil & Constitutional Law	In this matter, the High Court of Orissa at Cuttack adjudicated issues between – Mr. Ajaya Kumar Moharana and State Of Odisha & others ..... Opposite Parties Represented by Adv. –. The Court rendered a decision disposing of the application under statutory provisions.	0	2026 LexGuard (OHC) 94AF5810	{"court": "High Court of Orissa at Cuttack", "title": "– Mr. Ajaya Kumar Moharana v. State Of Odisha & others ..... Opposite Parties Represented by Adv. –", "case_id": "94af5810-e486-4f0e-98b7-97a1bedbc4a5", "case_no": "NO. 34843", "parties": "– Mr. Ajaya Kumar Moharana v. State Of Odisha & others ..... Opposite Parties Represented by Adv. –", "category": "GENERAL_CONSTITUTIONAL", "petitioner": "– Mr. Ajaya Kumar Moharana", "respondent": "State Of Odisha & others ..... Opposite Parties Represented by Adv. –", "legal_domain": "Civil & Constitutional Law", "category_facts": {"category": "GENERAL_CONSTITUTIONAL", "remedy_type": "Writ Petition / Criminal Appeal", "judicial_disposition": "Dismissed", "constitutional_article": "Article 226 / Article 21"}, "activity_events": [], "profile_version": "2.5", "statutory_matrix": [], "activ