18.09.2025 for grant of Diwali\nBonus to the petitioner, the petitioner has approached this Court seeking a\nmandamus in that regard.\n2. Mr.S.Iniyan Karthik, learned Government Advocate, accepts notice\nfor the first respondent. Mr.R.Murali, learned counsel, accepts notice for the\nsecond respondent.\n3. After pointing out that a licensee, such as the petitioner, cannot\nseek parity of treatment with employees, learned counsel for the second\nrespondent submits that the representation would be considered and\ndisposed of on merits within two weeks.\n4. Recording the said submission, this Writ Petition is disposed of by\ndirecting the second respondent to consider and dispose of the petitioner's\n_____________\nPage No. 2 of 4\n\nW.P.(MD) No.28835 of 2026\nrepresentation dated 18.09.2025 on merits within two weeks from the date\nof receipt of a copy of this order. There shall be no order as to costs.\n06.10.2026\nJEN\nNCC : No\nIndex : No\nTo\n1.The Commissioner,\nHindu Religious and Charitable Endowment,\nChennai.\n2.The Joint Commissioner / Executive Officer,\nArulmigu Dhandayudhapani Swamy Temple,\nPalani, Dindigul District.\n_____________\nPage No. 3 of 4\n\nW.P.(MD) No.28835 of 2026\nSENTHILKUMAR RAMAMOORTHY, J.\nJEN\nW.P.(MD) No.28835 of 2026\n06.10.2026\n_____________\nPage No. 4 of 4	4	t	HCMD011407472026	Writ Petition	2026-10-06	Single Bench	Periyasamy ... Petitioner	Commissioner, HR&CE & Anr.	Mr.B.Ramnath	\N	Constitutional Law	In this judgment under Civil Law, the Court ruled on the dispute between 1Vf7Huorqvh923Santrex5Tzoqvabok18 Home   Judgements And Orders, Supreme Court And High Courts Of India and the Respondent.	0	2026 LexGuard (Judg) A1F34E	{"court": "Madras High Court (Principal Seat, Chennai)", "title": "Periyasamy v. Commissioner, HR&CE & Anr.", "case_id": "a1f34efc-ba3e-4b4e-8257-69214a650d66", "case_no": "W.P.(MD) No.28835 of 2026", "parties": "Periyasamy v. Commissioner, HR&CE & Anr.", "category": "GENERAL_CONSTITUTIONAL", "petitioner": "Periy