issioner, Madurai\n... Respondent(s) / State\n\nSTATUTORY PROVISIONS & ACTS REFERRED:\nTamil Nadu Hindu Religious and Charitable Endowments Act 1959, Constitution of India\n\nSECTIONS & CLAUSES UNDER CONSIDERATION:\nHR&CE Act Section 78, HR&CE Act Section 79, Article 226\n\nKEY LEGAL DOMAINS & TOPICS:\nTemple Lands, HR&CE, Encroachment, Public Trust, Parens Patriae\n\n================================================================================\n                                   JUDGMENT\n================================================================================\n\n1. FACTUAL MATRIX:\nEncroachers erected commercial shops on 12 acres of ancient temple property in Madurai without valid lease. HR&CE failed to enforce eviction under Section 78.\n\n2. ISSUES FRAMED FOR ADJUDICATION:\n1. Does the Court have duty under Parens Patriae jurisdiction to protect temple properties from unlawful alienation?\n\n3. STATUTORY FRAMEWORK & PRECEDENTS:\nSections 78 and 79 HR&CE Act grant summary powers to evict encroachers of religious endowments.\n\n4. RATIO DECIDENDI:\nIdol is a perpetual minor; High Court exercising Parens Patriae jurisdiction is duty-bound to order eviction of encroachers from temple lands.\n\n5. FINAL DISPOSITION & ORDER:\nWrit Petition Allowed; HR&CE Department directed to recover encroached temple lands within 90 days.\n\nDecreed and ordered accordingly.\n\nHon'ble Justice G.R. Swaminathan\nMadras High Court (Madurai Bench)\n[LEXGUARD CRYPTOGRAPHIC VERIFIED REPOSITORY RECORD]\n	3	t	HCMD010067122026	Writ Petition	\N	Single Bench	T. Packiaraj	The Commissioner, Hindu Religious and Charitable Endowments	\N	\N	Constitutional Law	In this writ petition under Constitutional Law, the Court ruled on the dispute between T. Packiaraj and The Commissioner, Hindu Religious and Charitable Endowments.	0	2026 LexGuard (Writ) A7EDE3	{"court": "Madras High Court (Madurai Bench)", "title": "T. Packiaraj v. The Commissioner, Hindu Religious and Charitable Endowments", "cas