For Petitioners: Mr.G.R.Nesakkaran,\nAdvocate\nFor Respondent : Mr.N.Balasubramanian,\nCounsel for State of TN(Crl.Side)\nPETITION FOR BAIL Under Section 483 of B.N.S.S.\nPRAYER :-\nFor Bail in Crime No.206 of 2026 on the file of\nthe Respondent Police.\n1/6\n\nCRL OP(MD). No.23127 of 2026\nORDER : The Court made the following order :-\nThe petitioners / accused 5 and 3, who were\narrested and remanded to judicial custody on\n17.09.2026 for the offence punishable under Section\n25(1B)(b) of Arms Act, in Crime No.206 of 2026, on\nthe file of the respondent police, seek bail.\n2. The case of the prosecution is that on\n17.09.2026, at about 10.30 a.m., while the respondent\npolice, along with the police party, were on patrol\nduty near the Devar Statue at Villipathiri Bus Stop\nto prevent law and order issues, the petitioners and\nthe other accused were allegedly found in possession\nof two long patta knives. They were allegedly rubbing\nthe knives against the road, causing sparks and\nthereby creating fear and alarm among the members of\nthe public. The police apprehended the petitioners\nand accused 1 and 2, while the fourth accused\nescaped from the place of occurrence.\n3. The learned counsel appearing for the\npetitioners would submit that the petitioners are\n2/6\n\nCRL OP(MD). No.23127 of 2026\ninnocent and they have not committed any offence as\nalleged by the prosecution. He would further submit\nthat the petitioners are in judicial custody from\n17.09.2026.\n4. The learned Counsel for State of TN (Criminal\nSide) appearing for the respondent police would\nsubmit that as of now, the petitioners are not having\nany pending previous cases.\n5. Considering the nature of the charges\nlevelled as against the petitioners and also the\nfacts that the petitioners are in judicial custody\nfrom 17.09.2026 and that as of now, the petitioners\nare not having any pending previous cases, this Court\nis inclined to grant bail to the petitioners subject\nto the following conditions:\n6. Accordingly, the petitioners are ordered to\nbe released on bail on their executing a bond for a\nsum of Rs.25,000/- (Rupees Twenty Five Thousand only)\neach with two sureties each for a like sum to the\n3/6\n\nCRL OP(MD). No.23127 of 2026\nsatisfaction of the learned Principal District and\nSessions Judge, Srivilliputtur, Virudhunagar\nDistrict, and on further conditions that:\n(i)the sureties shall affix their photographs\nand left thumb impression in the surety bond and the\nSessions Judge / concerned court may obtain a copy of\ntheir Aadhar card or Bank Pass Book to ensure their\nidentity;\n(ii)the petitioners shall report before the\nrespondent police daily at 10.30 a.m., for a period\nof one month and thereafter, as and when required for\ninterrogation;\n(iii)the petitioners shall not tamper with the\nevidence or witness either during investigation or\ntrial;\n(iv)the petitioners shall not abscond either\nduring investigation or trial;\n(v)On breach of any of the aforesaid conditions,\nthe learned Sessions Judge / Trial Court is entitled\nto take appropriate action against the petitioners in\naccordance with law as if the conditions have been\nimposed and the petitioners are released on bail by\nthe learned Sessions Judge / Trial Court himself as\nlaid down by the Hon'ble Supreme Court in P.K.Shaji\n4/6\n\nCRL OP(MD). No.23127 of 2026\nvs. State of Kerala [(2005)AIR SCW 5560];\n(vi)If the accused thereafter abscond, a fresh\nFIR can be registered under Section 269 BNS, 2023.\n(K M S J)\n09.10.2026\nCSM\nTO\n1. The Principal District and Sessions Judge,\nSrivilliputtur, Virudhunagar District.\n2. Do through\nThe Chief Judicial Magistrate,\nVirudhunagar.\n3. The Officer-in-Charge,\nDistrict Prison,\nVirudhunagar.\n4. The Inspector of Police,\nMallanginar Police Station,\nVirudhunagar District.\n5. The Additional Public Prosecutor,\nMadurai Bench of Madras High Court,\nMadurai.\n5/6\n\nCRL OP(MD). No.23127 of 2026\nK.MURALI SHANKAR,J\nCSM\nORDER\nIN\nCRL OP(MD) No.23127 of 2026\nDate : 09.10.2026\n6/6	6	t	HCMA010231272026	Criminal Original Petition (Bail)	\N	Single Bench	Jeyaprakash @ Jeyaprakashraj & Praveenkumar	State of Tamil Nadu Rep. by Inspector of Police, Mallanginar	Mr.G.R.Nesakkaran,	Mr.N.Balasubramanian, Counsel for State of TN(Crl.Side)	Civil Law	In this criminal original petition under Civil Law, the Court ruled on the dispute between 09 Crl-Op-Md-23127-2026 and the Respondent.	0	2026 LexGuard (Crim) C37791	{"court": "Madras High Court (Principal Seat, Chennai)", "title": "Jeyaprakash @ Jeyaprakashraj & Praveenkumar v. State of Tamil Nadu Rep. by Inspector of Police, Mallanginar", "case_id": "c3779143-f267-46a1-b96e-458b0dd06bc2", "case_no": "CRL OP(MD). No.23127 of 2026", "parties": "Jeyaprakash @ Jeyaprakashraj & Praveenkumar v. State of Tamil Nadu Rep. by Inspector of Police, Mallanginar", "category": "BAIL_SUSPENSION", "petitioner": "Jeyaprakash @ Jeyaprakashraj & Praveenkumar", "respondent": "State of Tamil Nadu Rep. by Inspector of Police, Mallanginar", "legal_domain": "Civil Law", "category_facts": {"category": "BAIL_SUSPENSION", "surety_count": 2, "custody_period": null, "application_type": "Regular Bail", "bail_bond_amount": 25000.0, "trial_court_fine": null, "reason_for_relief": null, "reporting_condition": null, "trial_court_sentence": null, "trial_court_fine_paid": false}, "activity_events": [], "profile_version": "2.5", "statutory_matrix": [{"act": "BNSS", "section": "483", "canonical": "Section 483 BNSS", "equivalents": ["Section 439 CrPC"]}], "activity_clusters": [], "scenario_clusters": ["pre_trial_custody"], "scenario_keywords": ["remand"], "procedural_posture": {"remedy": "Allowed", "disposition": "Allowed"}}
