891232026\nYEAR: 2026\n\nCORAM / BENCH:\nHon'ble Justice G.R. Swaminathan\n\nPARTIES:\nS. Muthulakshmi\n... Petitioner(s) / Appellant(s)\nVersus\nHome Secretary, Government of Tamil Nadu & Superintendent of Police, Thoothukudi\n... Respondent(s)\n\nSTATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:\nConstitution of India, Code of Criminal Procedure 1973\n\nSECTIONS & PROVISIONS:\nArticle 21, Article 22, CrPC Section 176(1A)\n\nKEY TOPICS & ISSUES:\nCustodial Torture, Human Rights Violation, D.K. Basu Guidelines, Public Law Remedy, Strict Liability\n\n================================================================================\n                                   JUDGMENT\n================================================================================\n\n1. FACTS OF THE CASE:\nPetitioner's son suffered multiple fractures and renal failure while detained illegally for 3 days in police custody.\n\n2. ISSUES FRAMED:\nWhether public law compensation under Article 226 is available for custodial torture independent of private civil suit?\n\n3. LEGAL RATIO & FINDINGS:\nCustodial violence is an assault on human dignity and democracy; constitutional courts have duty to award strict liability compensation under Article 21.\n\n4. FINAL ORDER:\nPetition Allowed; Compensation of Rs. 15 Lakhs awarded for custodial torture and CB-CID inquiry directed.\n\nOrdered and decreed accordingly.\n\nHon'ble Justice G.R. Swaminathan\nMadras High Court (Madurai Bench)\n[LEXGUARD REPOSITORY CRYPTOGRAPHIC SEAL]\n	3	t	HCMD010062142026	Criminal Original Petition	\N	Single Bench	S. Muthulakshmi	Home Secretary & 4 Ors.	\N	\N	Civil Law	In this criminal original petition under Criminal Law, the Court ruled on the dispute between S. Muthulakshmi and Home Secretary & 4 Ors..	0	2026 LexGuard (Crim) C7D937	{"court": "Madras High Court (Madurai Bench)", "title": "S. Muthulakshmi v. Home Secretary & 4 Ors.", "case_id": "c7d93770-1e0b-4a36-9f87-03bcb688832a", "case_no": "Crl.O.P.(MD) No. 6214 of 2026", "parties": "S. Muthulakshm