, Kutty Andavar Kovil Street,\nChinnoor, Parangipettai,\nCuddalore District.\n..Petitioner(s)\nVs\n1. The State represented by,\nThe Home Secretary,\nHome Department (Prison),\nSecretariat, Fort St.George, Chennai.\n2. The Deputy Inspector General or Prisons,\nChennai Range,\nChennai.\n3. The Superintendent of Prison,\nCentral Prison I,\nPuzhal, Chennai.\n4. The Inspector of Police,\nParangipettai Police Station,\nParangipettai,\nCuddalore District.\n..Respondent(s)\n__________\nPage1 of 6\n\nWP Crl. No. 2571 of 2026\nWrit Petition (Criminal) filed under Section 226 of the Constitution of\nIndia to issue a Writ of Certiorarified Mandamus to call for the records relating\nto the proceedings of the third respondent in No.6084/Tha.Gu.2/2026 dated\n26.05.2026 insofar as it imposes the condition of police escort upon the\npetitioner’s husband viz. Veeravel, S/o.Palanivel, Convict Prisoner No.8170,\nPID No.42030, while granting 28 days ordinary leave, quash the same to the\nlimited extent of the escort condition, and consequently direct the respondents\nto permit the petitioner’s husband to avail the said 28 days ordinary leave\nwithout escort, subject to such reasonable conditions as may be imposed by this\nCourt.\nFor Petitioner(s): Ms.S.Shiney\nFor Respondent(s): Mr.C.R.Malarvannan,\nAdditional Public Prosecutor\nORDER\n(made by A.D.Jagadish Chandira, J.)\nChallenging the order dated 26.05.2026 bearing No.6084/Tha.Gu.2/2026\npassed by the third respondent and quash the same to the limited extent of the\nescort condition and consequently, direct the respondents to grant 28 days\nordinary leave without escort, to the detenu, Veeravel, S/o.Palanivel, Convict\nPrisoner No.8170, PID No.42030, detained at Central Prison-I, Puzhal, Chennai,\nthe petitioner has filed the present petition.\n__________\nPage2 of 6\n\nWP Crl. No. 2571 of 2026\n2. It is the contention of the learned counsel for the petitioner that the\npetitioner’s husband, who is the convict prisoner, was convicted for the offence\nunder Section 6 of the Protection of Children from Sexual Offences Act, 2012\nand sentenced to undergo ten years rigorous imprisonment and he has served the\nsentence for more than six years; therefore, the convict prisoner sought ordinary\nleave for 28 days under the Tamil Nadu Suspension of Sentence Rules, 1982, to\nattend his family affairs and responsibilities, pursuant to which, the second\nrespondent, vide order dated 25.05.2026, in proceedings No.203/Mu.C1/2026,\ngranted 28 days ordinary leave with police escort to him and subsequently, the\nthird respondent, vide order dated 26.05.2026 bearing No.6084/Tha.Gu.2/2026,\ncalled upon the petitioner and the convict prisoner to furnish the requisite\nbonds/sureties for availing the leave; the convict prisoner has already been\ngranted ordinary leave without escort on several occasions and during such\ntime, no untoward incident has happened. Hence, he seeks quashment of the\nimpugned order by granting ordinary leave without escort to the convict\nprisoner.\n3. The learned Additional Public Prosecutor appearing for the\nrespondents fairly submitted that since the petitioner’s husband/convict prisoner\nhas completed six years of imprisonment, he is entitled to 28 days ordinary\nleave per annum.\n4. Heard the learned counsel on either side and perused the entire\nmaterials.\n__________\nPage3 of 6\n\nWP Crl. No. 2571 of 2026\n5. It is seen from the records that the convict prisoner has already\nundergone sentence for more than six years and he sought ordinary leave only\non the ground to attend his family affairs and responsibilities, which he is\nactually entitled to as per the Tamil Nadu Suspension of Sentence Rules, 1982.\n6. In such view of the matter, the impugned order dated 26.05.2026\nbearing No.6084/Tha.Gu.2/2026 passed by the third respondent is set aside to\nthe limited extent of the escort condition and the convict prisoner viz. Veeravel,\nS/o.Palanivel, Convict Prisoner No.8170, PID No.42030, detained at Central\nPrison-I, Puzhal, Chennai, is granted twenty eight days ordinary leave from\n13.10.2026 to 09.11.2026 without escort. Further, the convict prisoner, during\nthis leave period, shall appear before the Inspector of Police, Parangipettai\nPolice Station, Parangipettai, Cuddalore District, everyday at 6.30 p.m. After\nexpiry of the ordinary leave, the convict prisoner shall surrender before the\nprison authorities on or before 10.00 a.m. on 10.11.2026. It is made clear that\nthe convict prisoner shall utilize the leave only for the purpose, for which, it has\nbeen granted and shall not indulge in any other activities.\nWith the above directions, this writ petition (criminal) stands allowed.\n(A.D.J.C.,J.) (K.G.R.,J.)\n09-10-2026\nIndex: Yes/No\nSpeaking/Non-speaking order\nNeutral Citation: Yes/No\nnsd\nNote: Issue copy of this order on 12.10.2026.\n__________\nPage4 of 6\n\nWP Crl. No. 2571 of 2026\nTo\n1. The Home Secretary,\nHome Department(Prison),\nSecretariat, Fort St.George,\nChennai.\n2. The Deputy Inspector General or Prisons,\nChennai Range,\nChennai.\n3. The Superintendent of Prison,\nCentral Prison I,\nPuzhal, Chennai.\n4. The Inspector of Police,\nParangipettai Police Station,\nParangipettai,\nCuddalore District.\n5. The Public Prosecutor,\nMadras High Court, Chennai.\n__________\nPage5 of 6\n\nWP Crl. No. 2571 of 2026\nA.D.JAGADISH CHANDIRA J.\nAND\nKRISHNASWAMY GOVINDARAJAN J.\nnsd\nWP Crl. No. 2571 of 2026\n09-10-2026\n__________\nPage6 of 6	6	t	HCMA012247452026	Writ Petition	2026-10-09	Single Bench	V.Geetha	1. The State represented by,	Ms.S.Shiney	Mr.C.R.Malarvannan, Additional Public Prosecutor	Constitutional Law	In this writ petition under Civil Law, the Court ruled on the dispute between 15 Wpcrl-2571-2026 and the Respondent.	0	2026 LexGuard (Writ) 881A44	{"court": "Madras High Court (Principal Seat, Chennai)", "title": "V.Geetha v. 1. The State represented by,", "case_id": "881a4485-cf40-484f-b7c5-b3ba0545a804", "case_no