in the nature of WRIT OF MANDAMUS directing the\nrespondents to provide adequate police protection, at S. Meyyappanpatti,\nMelur Taluk, Madurai District, on 10.10.2026 and 11.10.2026 during the\nconduct of the 8th year Oru Ur Kabaddi Potti by the Siva Sakthi Kabaddi\n__________\n\nWP Crl.(MD) No. 5620 of 2026\nClub,’ on the basis of the . petitioner's representation dated 06.10.2026,\nand pass such * further or other orders as this Hon'ble Court deems fit\nand proper in the circumstances of the case, and thus render justice.\nFor Petitioner(s): Mr.Muthuvel M\nFor Respondent(s): Mr.C.Susikumar\nGovt. Advocate (Crl. Side)\nORDER\nThis writ petition is filed seeking a direction to the respondents to\nprovide adequate police protection, at S. Meyyappanpatti, Melur Taluk,\nMadurai District, on 10.10.2026 and 11.10.2026 during the conduct of the\n8th year Oru Ur Kabaddi Potti by the Siva Sakthi Kabaddi Club,’ on the\nbasis of the petitioner's representation dated 06.10.2026.\n2. The learned Government Advocate (Crl.side) submitted that\nthere is an apprehension that some law and order problem will arise\nduring the tournament. Hence, he sought for dismissal of the writ\npetition.\n3. Heard the learned counsel on either side and carefully perused\nthe materials available on record.\n4. The third respondent police is directed to grant permission for\nconducting the Kabadi tournament on 10.10.2026 and 11.10.2026, by\nimposing the following conditions:\n__________\n\nWP Crl.(MD) No. 5620 of 2026\n“i) The petitioner and other participants shall not shout,\nraise any slogan for or against any party or party leader, any\ncaste, community or creed;\nii) The petitioner shall ensure that no untoward incident is\ncaused disturbing the public peace and tranquillity;\niii)The petitioner shall ensure proper first aid arrangements\nby keeping one or two doctors in the venue;\niv)The participants of “Kabadi” tournament shall not wear\nany form of dress showing offending slogans or picture of\nany communal/political leader which may cause disturbance;\nv)Songs praising communal leader or having communal\novertones should not be played;\nvi)The petitioner will ensure that no flex board or hoardings\ndepicting particular community or leader will be displayed;\nvii)There should not be any Flex Boards representing any\ncommunity or political leaders;\nviii)If there is any violation of any one of the conditions\nimposed, the concerned Police Officer is at liberty to take\nnecessary action, as per law and stop such performance;\nix)Similarly, the police is empowered to stop the Kabadi\ntournament, if it exceeds beyond the permitted time;\nx) The participants of the tournament shall not intake any\nkind of toxic substance or liquor during the tournament;\nxi) If there is any untoward incident took place, the village\npeople and the organizers of the tournament be made\nresponsible for the same;\nxii) The Refree must be authorized person from the District\nAssociation; and\n__________\n\nWP Crl.(MD) No. 5620 of 2026\nxiii) The respondents are at liberty to put any further\nrestrictions or to impose any conditions purely in the interest\nof preserving public order and tranquillity, so as to maintain\nlaw and order and communal harmony.\nxiv) The respondents are directed to strictly adhere to the\nStandard Operating Procedure adopted by the Government\nof Tamil Nadu.\nxv) The respondents are directed to afford necessary police\nprotection for the conduct of the kabadi tournament on\npayment of necessary charges in terms of G.O(Ms)No.139,\nHome (Pol-VIII) Department, dated 04.03.2019.”\n5. The petitioner is also directed to ensure that the conditions are\nstrictly complied with and also to ensure that no law and order problem is\ncreated in the course of conducting the tournament.\n6. With the above directions, this Writ Petition stands disposed of.\n09-10-2026\nIndex: Yes/No\nSpeaking/Non-speaking order\nNeutral Citation: Yes/No\nskn\n__________\n\nWP Crl.(MD) No. 5620 of 2026\nTo\n1. The Superintendent of Police,\nMadurai District,\nMadurai.\n2. The Deputy Superintendent of Police\nMelur Sub-Division,\nMelur,\nMadurai District.\n3. The Inspector of Police\nKeezhavalavu Police Station,\nKeezhavalavu,\nMadurai District.\n__________\n\nWP Crl.(MD) No. 5620 of 2026\nK.GOVINDARAJAN THILAKAVADI, J.\nskn\nWP Crl.(MD) No. 5620 of 2026\n09-10-2026\n__________	6	t	HCMD011462162026	Writ Petition	2026-10-09	Single Bench	Prasanth	1. The Superintendent of Police,	Mr.Muthuvel M	Mr.C.Susikumar Govt. Advocate (Crl. Side)	Civil Law	In this writ petition under Civil Law, the Court ruled on the dispute between 08 Wpcrl-Md-5620-2026 and the Respondent.	0	2026 LexGuard (Writ) 58E165	{"court": "Madras High Court (Principal Seat, Chennai)", "title": "S/o.Chinnakaruppan, v. 1. The Superintendent of Police,", "case_id": "58e165d8-c4e0-4475-9c12-c723e9d5cfc1", "case_no": "WP Crl.(MD) No. 5620 of 2026", "parties": "08 Wpcrl-Md-5620-2026", "category": "GENERAL_CONSTITUTIONAL", "petitioner": "S/o.Chinnakaruppan,", "respondent": "1. The Superintendent of Police,", "legal_domain": "Civil Law", "category_facts": {"category": "GENERAL_CONSTITUTIONAL", "remedy_type": "Writ of Mandamus", "judicial_disposition": "Dismissed", "constitutional_article": "Article 226 / Article 21"}, "activity_events": [], "profile_version": "2.5", "statutory_matrix": [], "activity_clusters": [], "scenario_clusters": ["constitutional_fundamental"], "scenario_keywords": ["writ of mandamus"], "procedural_posture": {"remedy": "Allowed", "disposition": "Allowed"}}
