tive rooms to the\nPetitioner, he has instructions to withdraw the writ petition.\n2. The writ petition, therefore, stands dismissed as withdrawn.\n(AMIT BORKAR, J.)\n1	1	t	BHCB010098762026	Judicial Precedent	2026-10-19	Single Bench	Vishal Mumbai Shikshan Prasarak Mandal	Estate Manager, Goregaon Maharashtra Housing & Area Development Board	\N	\N	Civil & Constitutional Law	In this matter, the High Court of Judicature at Bombay adjudicated issues between Vishal Mumbai Shikshan Prasarak Mandal and Estate Manager, Goregaon Maharashtra Housing & Area Development Board. The Court rendered a decision disposing of the application under statutory provisions.	0	2026 LexGuard (BHC) 5D883CBF	{"court": "High Court of Judicature at Bombay", "title": "Vishal Mumbai Shikshan Prasarak Mandal v. Estate Manager, Goregaon Maharashtra Housing & Area Development Board", "case_id": "5d883cbf-5a2d-4813-af50-116f7cee29fd", "case_no": "NO. 9876 OF 2016", "parties": "Vishal Mumbai Shikshan Prasarak Mandal v. Estate Manager, Goregaon Maharashtra Housing & Area Development Board", "category": "GENERAL_CONSTITUTIONAL", "petitioner": "Vishal Mumbai Shikshan Prasarak Mandal", "respondent": "Estate Manager, Goregaon Maharashtra Housing & Area Development Board", "legal_domain": "Civil & Constitutional Law", "category_facts": {"category": "GENERAL_CONSTITUTIONAL", "remedy_type": "Writ Petition / Criminal Appeal", "judicial_disposition": "Dismissed", "constitutional_article": "Article 226 / Article 21"}, "activity_events": [], "profile_version": "2.5", "statutory_matrix": [], "activity_clusters": [], "scenario_clusters": [], "scenario_keywords": [], "procedural_posture": {"remedy": "Dismissed", "disposition": "Dismissed"}}
673ff3ab-461a-4f3e-9eca-1a6c9df78e1f	NO. 22511 of 2026	SOHIL GULZARBHAI QURESHI v. STATE OF GUJARAT	High Court of Gujarat at Ahmedabad	2026	Hon'ble Mr. Justice Hasmukh D. Suthar	SOHIL GULZARBHAI QURESHI v. STATE OF GUJARAT	["Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita, 2023", "Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023", "the BNS"]	["Section 109(1) the BNS", "Section 115(2) the BNS", "Section 54 the BNS", "Section 61(2)(a) the BNS"]	["civil & constitutional law", "ghc", "disposed"]	Judgment in NO. 22511 of 2026 delivered by HONOURABLE MR. JUSTICE HASMUKH D. SUTHAR at High Court of Gujarat at Ahmedabad. The proceedings concern Civil & Constitutional Law with respect to Article 21.	Disposed	storage/cases/GHC_2026_NO_22511_of_2026_673ff3ab.pdf	0f182f418c01d9395f0d1223c72c64e5b0e8e27f7b889b5ff0ce2b75ce8104c4	\N	\N	\N	published	657396f3-5181-4922-8323-72d78b963be0	657396f3-5181-4922-8323-72d78b963be0	2026-10-25 14:51:54.158999+05:30	2026-10-25 14:51:54.159006+05:30	2026-10-26 10:38:09.542881+05:30	[1.0] RULE. Learned APP waives service of rule for the respondent-State. [2.0] The present application is filed under Section 483 of the Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita, 2023 (for short “BNSS”) for regular bail in connection with FIR being C.R. No. 11191010260214 of 2026 registered with Madhavpura Police Station, Ahmedabad, for the offences under Sections 109(1), 115(2), 54 and 61(2)(a) of the BNS. [3.0] Learned advocate appearing on behalf of the applicant submits that the applicant is innocent and has been falsely implicated in the offence. Nothing is required to be recovered or discovered. He therefore submits that, considering the nature of the offence, the applicant may be enlarged on regular bail by imposing suitable conditions. Page 1 of 5 R/CR.MA/22511/2026 ORDER DATED: 22/10/2026 (GJHC240729932026) [4.0] Learned APP appearing on behalf of the respondent-State has opposed the present application and requested to dismiss the present application for regular bail on the ground 	[]	Holding and principles affirmed in NO. 22511 of 2026 regarding Civil & Constitutional Law. The Court adjudicated upon Article 21.	[]	Disposed	[]	\N	unverified	Good Law (Binding Precedent)	R/CR.MA/22511/2026 ORDER DATED: 22/10/2026\n(GJHC240729932026)\nIN THE HIGH COURT OF GUJARAT AT AHMEDABAD\nR/CRIMINAL MISC.APPLICATION (FOR REGULAR BAIL - AFTER\nCHARGESHEET) NO. 22511 of 2026\n==========================================================\nSAMIR @ SOHIL GULZARBHAI QURESHI\nVersus\nSTATE OF GUJARAT\n==========================================================\nAppearance:\nMR BILAL M RADHANPURWALA(10978) for the Applicant(s) No. 1\nMR NISHIT H SHAH(10712) for the Applicant(s) No. 1\nMR YUVRAJ BRAHBHATT, APP for the Respondent(s) No. 1\n==========================================================\nCORAM:HONOURABLE MR. JUSTICE HASMUKH D. SUTHAR\nDate : 22/10/2026\nORDER\n[1.0] RULE. Learned APP waives service of rule for the\nrespondent-State.\n[2.0] The present application is filed under Section 483 of the\nBharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita, 2023 (for short “BNSS”) for\nregular bail in connection with FIR being C.R. No.\n11191010260214 of 2026 registered with Madhavpura Police\nStation, Ahmedabad, for the offences under Sections 109(1),\n115(2), 54 and 61(2)(a) of the BNS.\n[3.0] Learned advocate appearing on behalf of the applicant\nsubmits that the applicant is innocent and has been falsely\nimplicated in the offence. Nothing is required to be recovered or\ndiscovered. He therefore submits that, considering the nature of\nthe offence, the applicant may be enlarged on regular bail by\nimposing suitable conditions.\nPage 1 of 5\n\nR/CR.MA/22511/2026 ORDER DATED: 22/10/2026\n(GJHC240729932026)\n[4.0] Learned APP appearing on behalf of the respondent-State\nhas opposed the present application and requested to dismiss\nthe present application for regular bail on the ground that the\napplicant is very much involved in the present offence and\nconsidering the gravity of offence, no case is made out to\nentertain present bail application. Therefore, present application\ndoes not deserve consideration.\n[5.0] While granting bail, the Court has to consider the\ninvolvement of the accused in the alleged offence, the jurisdiction\nto grant bail has to be exercised on the basis of the well settled\nprinciples having regard to the facts and circumstances of each\ncase and the following factors are to be taken into consideration\nwhile considering an application for bail: (i) the nature of\naccusation and the severity of the punishment and the nature of\nthe materials relied upon by the prosecution; (ii) reasonable\napprehension of tampering with the witnesses and threat to the\ncomplainant or the witnesses; (iii) reasonable possibility of\nsecuring the presence of the accused at the time of trial or the\nlikelihood of his abscondence; (iv) character behaviour and\nstanding of the accused and the circumstances which are\npeculiar to the accused; (v) larger interest of the public or the\nState and similar other considerations are required to be\nconsidered.\n[6.0] I have heard the learned advocates appearing on behalf of\nthe respective parties and perused the investigation papers.\nFollowing aspects have been considered:\n(1) Investigation is over and charge-sheet is filed;\nPage 2 of 5\n\nR/CR.MA/22511/2026 ORDER DATED: 22/10/2026\n(GJHC240729932026)\n(2) Applicant is behind the bar since 26.05.2026;\n(3) There is nothing to be recovered or discovered from\nthe applicant;\n(4) It is alleged that the complainant was having an affair\nwith the applicant’s wife and that, due to this, the present\napplicant assaulted the complainant with a knife. However,\nthe complainant is out of danger and has been discharged\nfrom the hospital.\n(5) Though the applicant is having past antecedent, he is\npresumed to be innocent till proven guilty;.\n(6) Prosecution has failed to point out the circumstances\nto continue or prolong his incarceration;\n(7) Obviously commencement and conclusion of trial will\ntake its own time.\n[7.0] This Court has also taken into consideration the law laid\ndown by the Hon'ble Apex Court in the case of Sanjay Chandra\nvs. Central Bureau of Investigation reported in [2012]1 SCC\n40 as well as in the case of Gudikanti Narasimhulu And Ors\nvs. Public Prosecutor, High Court of Andhra Pradesh\nreported in (1978)1 SCC 240. Obviously, the conclusion of trial\nwill take time and keeping the accused behind the bars is\nnothing but amounts to pre-trial conviction and therefore,\nconsidering the celebrated principle of bail jurisprudence is that\n“bail is a rule and jail is exception” as well as the concept of\npersonal liberty guaranteed under Article 21 of the Constitution\nof India, present application deserves consideration.\n[8.0] In the facts and circumstances of the case and considering\nPage 3 of 5\n\nR/CR.MA/22511/2026 ORDER DATED: 22/10/2026\n(GJHC240729932026)\nthe nature of the allegations made against the applicant/s in the\nFIR, without discussing the evidence in detail, prima facie, this\nCourt is of the opinion that this is a fit case to exercise the\ndiscretion and enlarge the applicant/s on regular bail. Hence,\nthe present application is allowed. The applicant/s is/are\nordered to be released on regular bail in connection with FIR\nbeing C.R. No. 11191010260214 of 2026 registered with\nMadhavpura Police Station, Ahmedabad, on executing a\npersonal bond of Rs.25,000/- (Rupees Twenty-five Thousand\nonly) with one surety of the like amount to the satisfaction of the\ntrial Court and subject to the conditions that he/she/they shall;\n(a) not take undue advantage of liberty or misuse liberty;\n(b) not act in a manner injurious to the interest of the\nprosecution & shall not obstruct or hamper the police\ninvestigation and shall not to play mischief with the\nevidence collected or yet to be collected by the police;\n(c) surrender passport, if any, to the Trial Court within a\nweek;\n(d) not leave the State of Gujarat without prior permission\nof the Trial Court concerned;\n(e) mark presence before the concerned Police Station once\nin every month for a period of six months between 11.00\na.m. and 2.00 p.m.;\n(f) furnish the Aadhaar card, email ID/present address\nof his residence to the Investigating Officer and also to\nthe Court at the time of execution of the bond and shall\nnot change the residence/contact number without\nprior permission of Trial Court;\nPage 4 of 5\n\nR/CR.MA/22511/2026 ORDER DATED: 22/10/2026\n(GJHC240729932026)\n(g) not to indulge in any illegal activity failing which learned\ntrial Court shall issue warrant and cancel the bail of the\napplicant.\n[9.0] The authorities will release the applicant only if he/they\nis/are not required in connection with any other offence for the\ntime being. If breach of any of the above conditions is committed,\nthe Sessions Judge concerned will be free to issue warrant or\ntake appropriate action in the matter.\n[10.0] Bail bond to be executed before the lower Court having\njurisdiction to try the case. It will be open for the concerned\nCourt to delete, modify and/or relax any of the above conditions,\nin accordance with law.\n[11.0] At the trial, the trial Court shall not be influenced by the\nobservations of preliminary nature qua the evidence at this stage\nmade by this Court while enlarging the applicant/applicants on\nbail.\n[12.0] Rule is made absolute to the aforesaid extent. Direct\nservice is permitted.\n(HASMUKH D. SUTHAR,J)\nALI\nPage 5 of 5	5	t	GJHC240729932026	Judicial Precedent	2026-10-22	Single Bench	SOHIL GULZARBHAI QURESHI	STATE OF GUJARAT	\N	\N	Civil & Constitutional Law	In this matter, the High Court of Gujarat at Ahmedabad adjudicated issues between SAMIR @ SOHIL GULZARBHAI QURESHI and STATE OF GUJARAT. The Court rendered a decision disposing of the application under statutory provisions.	0	2026 LexGuard (GHC) 673FF3AB	{"court": "High Court of Gujarat at Ahmedabad", "title": "SAMIR @