nvolving offence\npunishable under Sections 115(2), 117(2), 126(2), 296, 3(5),\n324(4), 351(3) of B.N.S. in G.R. Case No.617 of 2026 in the Court\nof learned J.M.F.C. , Chilika arising out of Nachuni P.S. Case\nNo.397 of 2026.\n4. Learned counsel for the Petitioner at this juncture submitted\nthat the Petitioner does not wants to press this application and seeks\nliberty to surrender before the court below and move an application\nfor bail.\nPage 1 of 2.\n\n5. Considering such submissions, the Petitioner is permitted to\nsurrender before the learned court in seisin over the matter within a\nperiod of four weeks from today and move an application for bail.\nIn such eventuality, the learned court in seisin over the matter shall\ndo well to release the Petitioner on bail on such terms and\nconditions as the learned Magistrate may deem just and proper.\nViolation of any of the terms and conditions shall entail\ncancellation of the bail.\n6. It is further directed that the bail granted to the Petitioner\nshall be subject to depositing a cash security of Rs.2,000/- (Rupees\nTwo Thousand) before the learned Court in seisin over the matter,\nwhich shall be kept in any Nationalized bank in interest bearing\naccount initially for a period of one year which will be renewable\nfrom time to time till conclusion of trial and the same shall be abide\nby the final outcome of the trial of the case.\n7. It is further directed that the bail granted to the Petitioner\nshall be subject to the verification of his criminal antecedent and\nthe injury report. In the event, the Petitioner is having one criminal\nantecedent or the injured has sustained any grievous injury, then\nthis order shall stand automatically revoked.\n8. The ABLAPL is disposed of accordingly.\nUrgent certified copy of this order be granted as per rules.\n( A.K. Mohapatra)\nVacation Judge\nSisir\nPage 2 of 2.	2	t	ODHC010808992026	Judicial Precedent	2026-10-23	Single Bench	Chilika arising out of Nachuni P.S. Case	STATE OF ODISHA	\N	\N	Civil & Constitutional Law	In this matter, the High Court of Orissa at Cuttack adjudicated issues between Represented by Adv. - Jyotirmaya Sahoo and STATE OF ODISHA. The Court rendered a decision disposing of the application under statutory provisions.	0	2026 LexGuard (OHC) 7DC8FE6D	{"court": "High Court of Orissa at Cuttack", "title": "Represented by Adv. - Jyotirmaya Sahoo v. STATE OF ODISHA", "case_id": "7dc8fe6d-e242-444a-b08f-6c5f7aa2742f", "case_no": "NO. 12101 of 2026", "parties": "Represented by Adv. - Jyotirmaya Sahoo v. STATE OF ODISHA", "category": "BAIL_SUSPENSION", "petitioner": "Represented by Adv. - Jyotirmaya Sahoo", "respondent": "STATE OF ODISHA", "legal_domain": "Civil & Constitutional Law", "category_facts": {"category": "BAIL_SUSPENSION", "surety_count": null, "custody_period": null, "application_type": "Anticipatory Bail", "bail_bond_amount": null, "trial_court_fine": null, "reason_for_relief": null, "reporting_condition": null, "trial_court_sentence": null, "trial_court_fine_paid": false}, "activity_events": [], "profile_version": "2.5", "statutory_matrix": [], "activity_clusters": [], "scenario_clusters": [], "scenario_keywords": [], "procedural_posture": {"remedy": "Disposed", "disposition": "Disposed"}}
