dated 07.04.2011 made in W.P.No.23126 of 2008 and\npunish the respondents thereunder.\nFor Petitioner: Mr.A.Nishwer Jeelani\nFor Respondents: Mr.G.Anandakrishnan\nfor M/s.T.S.Gopalan And Co\n\\\nORDER\nThis contempt petition is filed alleging wilful disobedience and noncompliance with the order of this Court dated 07.04.2011 passed in\nW.P.No.23126 of 2008.\n__________\nPage1 of 3\n\nCONT P No. 3030 of 2016\n2. On this Court taking up the subject contempt petition for hearing, it was\nnoticed that the petitioner had already approached this Court at an earlier point\nof time by way of another contempt petition No.640 of 2012 alleging\ndisobedience and non-compliance with the order and the said contempt petition\nis pending consideration on the file of this Court.\n3. That being so, this Court is of the view that the petitioner cannot\nmaintain second contempt petition, having already filed contempt petition to\npunish the respondents for wilful disobedience of the order passed by this Court\nin W.P.No.23126 of 2008.\n4. In view of the above, the contempt petition is closed.\n09-10-2026\nIndex: Yes/No\nSpeaking/Non-speaking order\nNeutral Citation: Yes/No\nmsv\nTo\n1. Mr.Sasikumar\nChairman, Tamil Nadu Electricty Board,\nNo.144, Anna Salai, Chennai-600 002.\n2. Mr.Shantha Neelakumar\nAssistant Engineer, Rural / Cedc,\nTamil Nadu Electricity Board, Thirunindravur.\n__________\nPage2 of 3\n\nCONT P No. 3030 of 2016\nT.VINOD KUMAR, J.\nmsv\nCONT P No. 3030 of 2016\n09-10-2026\n__________\nPage3 of 3	3	t	HCMA010352822016	Writ Petition	2026-10-09	Single Bench	P.Dhamodharan	1. Mr.Sasikumar	Mr.A.Nishwer Jeelani	Mr.G.Anandakrishnan	Constitutional Law	In this judgment under Civil Law, the Court ruled on the dispute between 22 Cont-P-3030-2016 and the Respondent.	0	2026 LexGuard (Judg) 7EEC87	{"court": "Madras High Court (Principal Seat, Chennai)", "title": "CNR: {HCMA010352822016} v. 1. Mr.Sasikumar", "case_id": "7eec87a8-6b79-4d14-9b22-471dbee910fb", "case_no": "W.P.No.23126 of 2008", "parties": "22 Cont-P-3030-2016", "category": "GENERAL_CONSTITUTIONAL", "petitioner": "CNR: {HCMA010352822016}", "respondent": "1. Mr.Sasikumar", "legal_domain": "Constitutional Law", "category_facts": {"category": "GENERAL_CONSTITUTIONAL", "remedy_type": "Writ Petition / Criminal Appeal", "judicial_disposition": "Dismissed", "constitutional_article": "Article 226 / Article 21"}, "activity_events": [], "profile_version": "2.5", "statutory_matrix": [], "activity_clusters": [], "scenario_clusters": [], "scenario_keywords": [], "procedural_posture": {"remedy": "Allowed", "disposition": "Allowed"}}
80940c86-89b8-4c77-a7c3-6059480c02d0	NO. 1180 OF 2026	Ajinkya Arun Aghade .. Applicant v. The State of Maharashtra and Anr	High Court of Judicature	2026	Hon'ble MILIND N. JADHAV, J	Ajinkya Arun Aghade .. Applicant v. The State of Maharashtra and Anr	["Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023"]	[]	["civil & constitutional law", "hc", "allowed"]	Judgment in NO. 1180 OF 2026 delivered by Hon'ble MILIND N. JADHAV, J at High Court of Judicature. The proceedings concern Civil & Constitutional Law with respect to procedural compliance.	Disposed	storage/cases/HC_2026_NO_1180_OF_2026_80940c86.pdf	2b17c2ea604f55307d9c47cb33d99191ad2c0302d895e2b082a931b05f5f5b8b	\N	\N	\N	published	657396f3-5181-4922-8323-72d78b963be0	657396f3-5181-4922-8323-72d78b963be0	2026-10-25 14:51:55.775457+05:30	2026-10-25 14:51:55.775462+05:30	2026-10-26 10:38:09.554928+05:30	\N	[]	Holding and principles affirmed in NO. 1180 OF 2026 regarding Civil & Constitutional Law. The Court adjudicated upon applicable judicial standards.	[]	Disposed	[]	\N	unverified	Good Law (Binding Precedent)	50.BA.1180.2026.doc\nHARSHADA H. SAWANT\n(P.A.)\nIINN TTHHEE HHIIGGHH CCOOUURRTT OOFF JJUUDDIICCAATTUURREE AATT BBOOMMBBAAYY\nCCRRIIMMIINNAALL AAPPPPEELLLLAATTEE JJUURRIISSDDIICCTTIIOONN\nBAIL APPLICATION NO.1180 OF 2026\nAjinkya Arun Aghade .. Applicant\nVersus\nThe State of Maharashtra and Anr. .. Respondents\n....................\n Mr. Pushkar Durge a/w. Mr. Suyash Khose and Mr. Siddharth N.\nSutaria, Advocates for Applicant.\n Ms. Anuja S. Gotad, APP for Respondent No.1.\n Mr. Kuldeep Nikam, Advocate for Respondent No.2.\n Mohan Chavan, Khothrud Police Station, Pune.\n...................\nCORAM : MILIND N. JADHAV, J.\nDATE : OCTOBER 19, 2026\nP.C . :\n1. Heard Mr. Durge, learned Advocate for Applicant; Ms.\nGotad, learned APP for Respondent No.1 and Mr. Nikam, learned\nAdvocate for Respondent No.2.\n2. This is an Application under Section 483 of Bharatiya\nNagarik Suraksha Sanhita, 2023 seeking Bail in connection with C.R.\nNo.184 of 2025 registered with Kothrud Police Station for offences\npunishable under Sections 308(2), 308(3), 351(2), 111(3) read with\nSection 3(5) of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023.\n3. Accused No.2 is the Applicant before me who is incarcerated\nfor the past 13 months. He is a professional cyber expert whose\nservices were availed of by Accused No.3 and probably Accused No.1\n1 of 4\n\n50.BA.1180.2026.doc\nwho is the principal protagonist in the present case in a crime for\nextortion. In so far as the Complainant - First Informant duly\nrepresented by Mr. Nikam is concerned, there is an atrocities case filed\nby the Informant against the Accused No.3 and in retaliation to the\nsame and for settling the same the present offence was planned by\nAccused Nos.1 and 3.\n4. Role attributed to present Applicant is only to the extent of\nhe having attended the meeting with the other accused persons to the\nextent of removing the chats and having assisted them in retrieving the\nchats between Accused No.3 and the First Informant and in that way\nassisting the principal Accused No.1 to allegedly commit extortion in\nthe present crime.\n5. Considering the fact that case of prosecution against\nApplicant is solely based on electronic evidence, the investigation of\nwhich is completed, the same will undoubtedly be proved at trial qua\nthe complicity of the Applicant. The records have already been seized\nincluding the transcript certificate, the concerned mobile device has\nalso been seized and the cyber certificate which has been issued by the\nApplicant with regard to the said electronic evidence is also available\nwith the prosecution.\n6. It is prima facie seen that Applicant has also received his\nlegitimate professional fee with regard to the work done to the extent\n2 of 4\n\n50.BA.1180.2026.doc\nof which his services were availed by the Applicant. Hence, prima\nfacie case is made out for grant of bail.\n7. Considering the aforesaid, Applicant is released on bail\nsubject to following conditions:-\n(i) Applicant - Ajinkya Arun Aghade is directed to be\nimmediately released from prison in connection with\nCrime No. 184 of 2025;\n(ii) Applicant is directed to be released on bail on\nfurnishing P.R. Bond of Rs. 50,000/- (Rs. Fifty\nThousand only) with one or two surety / sureties of the\nlike amount;\n(iii) Applicant shall report to the Investigating Officer at\nKothrud Police Station, once every month on the first\nMonday of the month between 10:00 a.m. to 12:00\np.m.;\n(iv) Applicant shall co-operate with the conduct of trial and\nattend the Trial Court on all dates, unless specifically\nexempted and will not take any unnecessary\nadjournments, if he does so it will entitle the\nprosecution to apply for revocation of this order;\n(v) Applicant shall not leave the State of Maharashtra\nwithout prior permission of the Trial Court;\n3 of 4\n\n50.BA.1180.2026.doc\n(vi) Applicant shall not influence any of the witnesses or\ntamper with the evidence in any manner;\n(vii) Applicant shall keep the Investigating Officer informed\nof his current address and mobile contact number and /\nor change of residence or mobile details, if any, from\ntime to time, as applicable; and\n(viii)Any infraction of the conditions shall entail cancellation\nof bail granted to the Applicant.\n8. It is clarified that the observations made in this order are\nlimited for the purpose of granting Bail only and I have not made any\nobservations on merits of the case. The trial shall be adjudicated on\nthe strength of the evidence led and strictly on its own merits being\nuninfluenced with any of the prima facie observations made\nhereinabove in this order.\n9. Bail Application is allowed and disposed of in the above\nterms.\n[ MILIND N. JADHAV, J. ]\nH. H. SAWANT\nDigitally signed\nHARSHADA by HARSHADA\nHANUMANT H SA A W N A U N M T ANT\nSAWANT Date: 2026.10.19\n18:50:49 +0530\n4 of 4	4	t	HCMA010011802026	Judicial Precedent	2026-10-19	Single Bench	Ajinkya Arun Aghade .. Applicant	The State of Maharashtra and Anr	\N	No.1.  Mr. Kuldeep Nikam, Advocate for Respondent No.2.	Civil & Constitutional Law	In this matter, the High Court of Judicature adjudicated issues between CCRRIIMMIINNAALL AAPPPPEELLLLAATTEE JJUURRIISSDDIICCTTIIOONN Ajinkya Arun Aghade and The State of Maharashtra and Anr. The Court rendered a decision disposing of the application under statutory provisions.	0	2026 LexGuard (HC) 80940C86	{"court": "High Court of Judicature", "title": "CCRRIIMMIINNAALL AAPPPPEELLLLAATTEE JJUURRIISSDDIICCTTIIOONN Ajinkya Arun Aghade v. The State of Maharashtra and Anr", "case_id": "80940c86-89b8-4c77-a7c3-6059480c02d0", "case_no": "NO. 1180 OF 2026", "parties": "CCRRIIMMIINNAALL AAPPPPEELLLLAATTEE JJUURRIISSDDIICCTTIIOONN Ajinkya Arun Aghade v. The State of Maharashtra and Anr", "category": "BAIL_SUSPENSION", "petitioner": "CCRRIIMMIINNAALL AAPPPPEELLLLAATTEE JJUURRIISSDDIICCTTIIOONN Ajinkya Arun Aghade", "respondent": "The State of Maharashtra and Anr", "legal_domain": "Civil & Constitutional Law", "category_facts": {"category": "BAIL_SUSPENSION", "surety_count": null, "custody_period": null, "application_type": "Regular Bail", "bail_bond_amount": 50000.0, "trial_court_fine": null, "reason_for_relief": null, "reporting_condition": null, "trial_court_sentence": null, "trial_court_fine_paid": false}, "activity_events": [], "profile_version": "2.5", "statutory_matrix": [], "activity_clusters": [], "scenario_clusters": [], "scenario_keywords": [], "procedural_posture": {"remedy": "Allowed", "disposition": "Allowed"}}
