 Chennai\n... Respondent(s)\n\nSTATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:\nCentral Goods and Services Tax Act 2017, Tamil Nadu Goods and Services Tax Act 2017\n\nSECTIONS & PROVISIONS:\nCGST Act Section 16(2)(c), CGST Act Section 16(4), TNGST Act Section 16\n\nKEY TOPICS & ISSUES:\nGST Input Tax Credit, Bona Fide Purchaser, Supplier Default, GSTR-2A Matching, Tax Invoice\n\n================================================================================\n                                   JUDGMENT\n================================================================================\n\n1. FACTS OF THE CASE:\nRevenue reversed petitioner's Input Tax Credit on grounds that selling dealer failed to remit collected tax into government treasury.\n\n2. ISSUES FRAMED:\nCan genuine purchasing dealer who holds valid tax invoice and bank payment proofs be denied ITC for vendor's non-remittance?\n\n3. LEGAL RATIO & FINDINGS:\nWhere purchasing dealer proves bona fide purchase with invoice and banking channel proof, ITC cannot be denied without proceeding against defaulting supplier first.\n\n4. FINAL ORDER:\nWrit Petition Allowed; Input Tax Credit denial quashed; Purchasing dealer cannot be penalized for supplier default.\n\nOrdered and decreed accordingly.\n\nHon'ble Justice Mohammed Shaffiq\nMadras High Court (Principal Seat, Chennai)\n[LEXGUARD REPOSITORY CRYPTOGRAPHIC SEAL]\n	3	t	HCMA010223402026	Writ Petition	\N	Single Bench	M/s Precision Auto Components	Assistant Commissioner of State Tax	\N	\N	Constitutional Law	In this writ petition under Service & Employment Law, the Court ruled on the dispute between M/s Precision Auto Components and Assistant Commissioner of State Tax.	0	2026 LexGuard (Writ) 8E0B6D	{"court": "Madras High Court (Principal Seat, Chennai)", "title": "M/s Precision Auto Components v. Assistant Commissioner of State Tax", "case_id": "8e0b6d3f-dec2-4cca-ad97-6be6e5713cfa", "case_no": "W.P. No. 22340 of 2026", "parties": "M/s Precision Auto Components Private Limited", "category"