9eb72140-fa68-4803-8c50-067c6e9c4cf6	NO. 9031 of 2023	Anr. .. Petitioners v. Thane Municipal Corporation & Ors	High Court of Judicature at Bombay	2026	Hon'ble BHARATI DANGRE &	Anr. .. Petitioners v. Thane Municipal Corporation & Ors	[]	[]	["civil & constitutional law", "bhc", "disposed"]	Judgment in NO. 9031 of 2023 delivered by Hon'ble BHARATI DANGRE & at High Court of Judicature at Bombay. The proceedings concern Civil & Constitutional Law with respect to procedural compliance.	Disposed	storage/cases/BHC_2026_NO_9031_of_2023_9eb72140.pdf	bbf1bcce522380f1c88a6a06c8100153a48844305287ac4047f369c071c740ac	\N	\N	\N	published	657396f3-5181-4922-8323-72d78b963be0	657396f3-5181-4922-8323-72d78b963be0	2026-10-25 14:52:00.39385+05:30	2026-10-25 14:52:00.393858+05:30	2026-10-26 10:38:09.560158+05:30	\N	[]	Holding and principles affirmed in NO. 9031 of 2023 regarding Civil & Constitutional Law. The Court adjudicated upon applicable judicial standards.	[]	Disposed	[]	\N	unverified	Good Law (Binding Precedent)	1/7 909 CP-424-26.odt\nSalgaonkar\nIN THE HIGH COURT OF JUDICATURE AT BOMBAY\nM SA A L N G D A I O R N A K M A I R LIND DMD i aIg tLi e tI:Na 2 lDl 0 y 2Ss 6 iAg .L1 n 0Ge . dA2 O2 b Ny 1 3KM :A1 AR9 N :2 D 6 I R + A 0530\nCIVIL APPELLATE JURISDICTION\nCONTEMPT PETITION NO.424 OF 2026\nNamrata Nilesh Koli & Anr. .. Petitioners\nVersus\nThane Municipal Corporation & Ors. .. Respondents\n…\nMr.Pritesh Burad with Ms.Rama Somania and Mr.Akhilesh\nKumar Maurya i/b Pritesh Burad Associates for the Petitioner.\nMr.Rajesh Kanojia with Ms.Gargi Mandvikar i/b Res Juris for\nthe Respondent No.4.\nMr.M.M.Pabale, A.G.P. for the State/Respondent.\nCORAM: BHARATI DANGRE &\nASHISH S. CHAVAN, JJ.\nDATE : 19th OCTOBER, 2026\n...\nP.C:-\n1. The Contempt Petition is filed alleging disobedience of the\norder passed in Writ Petition No.9031 of 2023 on 28/02/2024.\nThe Petition being filed by the mother and daughter of one\nMohan Alaji Patil, an employee of Thane Municipal\nCorporation, since his death occurred during the Covid\npandemic and he being insured under the Pradhan Mantri\nGarib Kalyan Package :Insurance Scheme for Health Workers\nFighting Covid-19, they claimed the benefit of the scheme. It is\nworth to note that Mohan Alaji Patil demised while in service\non 29/10/2020 and the amount of compensation was\nsanctioned under the said scheme.\n\n2/7 909 CP-424-26.odt\nThe grievance of the petitioners before the Court was\nthat the Disbursing Authority has not disbursed the amount in\nthe wake of the inter se claim between the petitioners and the\nrespondent No.6 i.e. the son of Mohan Alaji Patil and,\ntherefore, the doors of the Court were knocked.\nIt is in this writ petition, the Division Bench passed the\nfollowing order.\n“2. The Petitioners have filed this Petition claiming that being the\ndaughter and mother of the deceased employee of the Respondent –\nThane Municipal Corporation are entitled to the insurance\ncompensation to be provided under the Pradhan Mantri Garib\nKalyan Package : Insurance Scheme for Health Workers Fighting\nCovid-19. It is their case that the deceased who was working with\nthe Respondent – Thane Municipal Corporation passed away while\nin service on 29 October 2020. Under the scheme the compensation\namount is sanctioned. The question has arisen as regard the claim\nof the Respondent No.6.\n3. There is no decision taken by the Disbursing Authority as to the\ninter se claim of the Petitioners and the Respondent No.6 and the\nPetitioners had called upon this Court at the first instance to decide\nthe issue. Therefore, we deem it appropriate that the Respondent\nNo.4 would examine the claim of the Petitioners and the\nRespondent No.6 and decide regarding the entitlement by passing a\nreasoned order.\n4. Since it is pointed out that the claim which is sanctioned has not\ndisbursed for almost four years, the Respondent No.4 upon giving\nopportunity to the Petitioners and the Respondent No.6 will take a\ndecision within a period of four weeks, after all record is made\navailable to it and communicate the same to the Petitioners and the\nRespondent No.6. All contentions of the parties are kept open.”\n2. Since this order was not complied with, when the\nContempt Petition appeared before us on 06/10/2026, we\npassed a detailed order, prima facie, noting that the Petitioners\nare waiting for more than five years for the amount and in fact,\nwhen the amount for disbursal under the scheme was already\ndetermined, the actual amount was not disbursed.\nDuring the course of hearing, learned counsel\nrepresenting the New India Assurance Company, one of the\n\n3/7 909 CP-424-26.odt\ncontemnors, invited our attention to the letter addressed by\nthe Deputy Secretary to the Govt. of India, Ministry of Health\n& Family Welfare to the Regional Manager of New India\nAssurance Co. Ltd. dated 29/04/2024, intimating that the\nMinistry has taken a decision that it would transfer the\namount of compensation directly to the aadhaar linked bank\naccount of the beneficiaries, as it is not desirous of incurring\nany additional expenditure on the commissions to be paid to\nthe Assurance Company for processing the pending claims. As\na result, the pending original claim documents pertaining to\nPradhan Mantri Garib Kalyan Package (PMGKP) were\ndirected to be forwarded to the Ministry.\n3. The Assurance Company, therefore, adopted a stand that\nnow it is not within its power to take any decision and it is in\nthis background, we observed thus :-\n“3. We are at pains to find that the heirs of a person who lost his life\nduring the COVID-19 pandemic are made to wait for the last six\nyears, and that is really unfortunate, according to us The\nPetitioners in the Writ Petition sought their respective share and,\ntherefore, the Court directed the Assurance Company, i.e.\nRespondent No. 4, only to take a decision about the inter-se claim of\nthe Petitioners and communicate the same to the Petitioners as well\nas Respondent No. 6, one of the claimants, but on the aforesaid\npretext, nothing has been done by the Assurance Company, and\nnow the excuse given is that all the documents have been\nforwarded. Though we could have initiated an action for flouting the\norders passed by us, since the learned counsel for the Assurance\nCompany earnestly submits that, if the learned counsel for the\nPetitioners furnishes the necessary documents and on the basis of\nwhich the order passed by this Court can be still complied with, it\nwill make a sincere endevour to do so. Upon its determination, how\nthe amount shall be disbursed and by whom will be taken care of by\nus on the next date of hearing.”\n4. In light of our aforesaid directions, the Assurance\nCompany has placed before us its report, and a copy of which is\naddressed to all the three claimants and it is in form of a order,\n\n4/7 909 CP-424-26.odt\nwhich refers to the proceedings taken by the parties to avail\nthe service benefits of the deceased and the report state that a\nsuccession certificate was granted on 21/10/2022, which was\nrestricted to gratuity, provident fund and other amounts\narising out of the employment benefits. However, there was no\nmention of the insurance amount.\nThe report mentions that the son of the deceased,\nnamely, Rakesh Mohan Patil, has also separately applied for\ngrant of succession certificate claiming that he is the only\nsuccessor of the said amount and at present, it is now pending\nbefore Raigad Alibag Court and this Miscellaneous Application\nNo.153 of 2021 for grant of succession certificate on being\ntransferred to the Court of Civil Judge, Senior Division, Alibag\nand renumbered as M.A.No.195 of 2023 is pending and\nsubjudice.\nThe report also makes a reference to a certificate that\nwas produced by Shri Rakesh Mohan Patil and the certificate\nissued by the District Magistrate in terms of the Insurance\nScheme for the Health Workers fighting Covid-2019, PMGKP,\nis in the name of Rakesh Mohan Patil i.e. son of Mohan Alaji\nPatil (the certificate wrongly mentions the nomenclature of\nthe deceased and the claimant) and on perusal of the\ncertificate, it appears that Rakesh Mohan Patil was only\nexclusively held entitled for the amount of insurance, in the\nwake of demise of Mohan Alaji Patil. In any case, the\nAssurance Company has not acted on it.\n5. The report of the New India Assurance Company is taken\non record and marked ‘X’ for identification. It is worth noting\nthat the copies of the same are already forwarded to the\n\n5/7 909 CP-424-26.odt\nPetitioners as well as to Rakesh Mohan Patil, Respondent No.6,\nwho has failed to mark his appearance.\n6. Although this is a Contempt Petition, but in order to do\ncomplete justice to the parties and in order to ensure\ncompliance of our order dated 06/10/2026, whereby the\nAssurance Company was directed to take a decision upon the\neligibility and entitlement of the claimants against the amount\nfor which the deceased was insured and since, it was clearly\nindicated that upon this being determined, how much shall be\nthe amount which shall be disbursed and how much shall be\npaid would be determined by us, with the Assurance Company\nfairly coming before us with all the relevant tax, we deem it\nappropriate to make an exception of issuing directions though\nin contempt proceedings we are not otherwise within our\njurisdiction to issue any positive directions and only to ensure\nwhether the directions issued by the Court are complied or\nnot. The Division Bench by its order dated 28/02/2024 itself\nhad indicated that the claim amount is already sanctioned, but\nnot disbursed for four years and by directing the Assurance\nCompany to take a decision, after giving an opportunity to the\npetitioners, namely, deceased’s mother and his own daughter\nand son, the petition was disposed of.\nIn our view, now the disbursement is not in the hands of\nthe Assurance Company, but will have to be done by the\nGovernment of India, Ministry of Health & Family Welfare in\nterms of the communication addressed to the New India\nAssurance Co. Ltd. on 29/04/2024 and since it was already\nindicated by the learned counsel for the Assurance Company\nthat all the papers are already forwarded to the Ministry of\n\n6/7 909 CP-424-26.odt\nHealth & Family Welfare, we direct him that the report that is\nplaced before us by the Assurance Company shall be\nimmediately forwarded to the Deputy Secretary to the\nGovernment of India, Ministry of Health & Family Welfare,\nNational ADIS Control Organisation in terms of the\ncommunication dated 29/04/2024. We also direct that the\nAssurance Company shall ensure that it is forwarded to the\nDeputy Secretary to the Government of India and though the\nGovernment of India is not a party, as it was not involved at\nthis stage, but in the wake of subsequent event that the\nGovernment of India deemed it appropriate to take up the\nwork of disbursement of compensation by itself, as much\nperiod has lapsed after the Covid pandemic and the\nGovernment did not deem it appropriate to issue commissions\nto the Assurance Company, which was earlier engaged for\nsettling the claim, we direct that the Government of India,\nMinistry of Health & Family Welfare shall immediately take a\ndecision upon the communication forwarded by the New India\nAssurance Co.Ltd.\nWe also declare that 2/3rd of the amount shall be\ndisbursed in favour of the two Petitioners before us. However,\nwe permit 1/3rd of the amount to be disbursed in favour of\nRakesh Mohan Patil in his account and we expect the\nPetitioners to furnish the account numbers of all the three\nclaimants to the learned counsel for the Assurance Company,\nso that in the forwarding letter, they shall be forwarded to the\nGovernment of India.\nUpon the communication being received, the only job\nwhich is required to be undertaken by the Government of India\n\n7/7 909 CP-424-26.odt\nshall be disbursement of the amount in each of the account\nholders, namely, Namrata Nilesh Koli alias Namrata Mohan\nPatil, Smt.Gangubai Alaji Patil and Rakesh Mohan Patil in\nequal proportion.\n7. With this, we dispose of the contempt proceedings by\nmaking out an exception and we also direct that the learned\ncounsel for the Petitioners shall forward a copy of our order to\nthe Government Advocate, who shall address a communication\nto the Government of India, Ministry of Health & Family\nWelfare, which shall act upon the said communication which\nshall be accompanied with the copy of our order within a\nperiod of eight (8) weeks from the date of its receipt.\n(ASHISH S. CHAVAN, J.) (BHARATI DANGRE, J.)	7	t	BHCB010090312026	Judicial Precedent	2026-10-23	Single Bench	Anr. .. Petitioners	Thane Municipal Corporation & Ors	\N	\N	Civil & Constitutional Law	In this matter, the High Court of Judicature at Bombay adjudicated issues between CONTEMPT PETITION NO.424 OF 2026 Namrata Nilesh Koli & Anr and Thane Municipal Corporation & Ors. The Court rendered a decision disposing of the application under statutory provisions.	0	2026 LexGuard (BHC) 9EB72140	{"court": "High Court of Judicature at Bombay", "title": "CONTEMPT PETITION NO.424 OF 2026 Namrata Nilesh Koli & Anr v. Thane Municipal Corporation & Ors", "case_id": "9eb72140-fa68-4803-8c50-067c6e9c4cf6", "case_no": "NO. 9031 of 2023", "parties": "CONTEMPT PETITION NO.424 OF 2026 Namrata Nilesh Koli & Anr v. Thane Municipal Corporation & Ors", "category": "GENERAL_CONSTITUTIONAL", "petitioner": "CONTEMPT PETITION NO.424 OF 2026 Namrata Nilesh Koli & Anr", "respondent": "Thane Municipal Corporation & Ors", "legal_domain": "Civil & Constitutional Law", "category_facts": {"category": "GENERAL_CONSTITUTIONAL", "remedy_type": "Writ Petition / Criminal Appeal", "judicial_disposition": "Dismissed", "constitutional_article": "Article 226 / Article 21"}, "activity_events": [], "profile_version": "2.5", "statutory_matrix": [], "activity_clusters": [], "scenario_clusters": [], "scenario_keywords": [], "procedural_posture": {"remedy": "Disposed", "disposition": "Disposed"}}
a24b34cb-7db9-4533-ad5b-7491b538b6d6	NO. 12126 of 2026	Represented by Adv. - Amlan Shakti Paul v. STATE OF ODISHA	High Court of Orissa at Cuttack	2026	Hon'ble MR. JUSTICE ADITYA KUMAR MOHAPATRA	Represented by Adv. - Amlan Shakti Paul v. STATE OF ODISHA	[]	["Section 482"]	["civil & constitutional law", "ohc", "disposed"]	Judgment in NO. 12126 of 2026 delivered by Hon'ble MR. JUSTICE ADITYA KUMAR MOHAPATRA at High Court of Orissa at Cuttack. The proceedings concern Civil & Constitutional Law with respect to Section 482.	Disposed	storage/cases/OHC_2026_NO_12126_of_2026_a24b34cb.pdf	a835e166bf616a37125805b44113b652372903f98be2f122becd9642040d7460	\N	\N	\N	published	657396f3-5181-4922-8323-72d78b963be0	657396f3-5181-4922-8323-72d78b963be0	2026-10-25 14:51:30.456559+05:30	2026-10-25 14:51:30.456563+05:30	2026-10-26 10:38:09.560529+05:30	23.10.2026 Order No. 01. 1. This matter is taken up through Hybrid Arrangement (Virtual /Physical Mode). 2. Heard learned counsel for the Petitioner and learned Additional Standing Counsel for the State. Perused the Anticipatory Bail Application as well as the F.I.R.	[]	Holding and principles affirmed in NO. 12126 of 2026 regarding Civil & Constitutional Law. The Court adjudicated upon Section 482.	[]	Disposed	[]	\N	unverified	Good Law (Binding Precedent)	IN THE HIGH COURT OF ORISSA AT CUTTACK\nABLAPL No.12126 of 2026\nCNR No. ODHC010809852026\nSiba @ Shiba Nayak ..... Petitioner\nRepresented by Adv. -\nAmlan Shakti Paul\n-versus-\nSTATE OF ODISHA ..... Opposite Party\nRepresented by Adv.\n– S.C. Pradhan, ASC\nCORAM:\nMR. JUSTICE ADITYA KUMAR MOHAPATRA\nORDER\n23.10.2026\nOrder No.\n01. 1. This matter is taken up through Hybrid Arrangement (Virtual\n/Physical Mode).\n2. Heard learned counsel for the Petitioner and learned\nAdditional Standing Counsel for the State. Perused the Anticipatory\nBail Application as well as the F.I.R.\n3. This is an application under Section 482 of the B.N.S.S.,\n2023 filed by the Petitioner for anticipatory bail, involving offence\npunishable under Section 309(6) of B.N.S. in C.T. Case No.2521 of\n2026 in the Court of learned J.M.F.C.-V, Bhubaneswar arising out\nof Bharatpur P.S. Case No.858 of 2026.\n4. Learned counsel for the Petitioner at this juncture submitted\nthat the Petitioner does not wants to press this application and seeks\nliberty to surrender before the court below and move an application\nfor bail.\nPage 1 of 2.\n\n5. Considering such submissions, the Petitioner is permitted to\nsurrender before the learned court in seisin over the matter within a\nperiod of three weeks from today and move an application for bail.\nIn such eventuality, the learned court in seisin over the matter shall\ndo well to release the Petitioner on bail on such terms and\nconditions as the learned Magistrate may deem just and proper.\nViolation of any of the terms and conditions shall entail\ncancellation of the bail.\n6. It is further directed that the bail granted to the Petitioner\nshall be subject to the verification of his criminal antecedent. In the\nevent, the Petitioner is having any similar criminal antecedent, then\nthis order shall stand automatically revoked.\n7. The ABLAPL is disposed of accordingly.\nUrgent certified copy of this order be granted as per rules.\n( A.K. Mohapatra)\nVacation Judge\nSisir\nPage 2 of 2.	2	t	ODHC010809852026	Judicial Precedent	2026-10-23	Single Bench	Represented by Adv. - Amlan Shakti Paul	STATE OF ODISHA	\N	\N	Civil & Constitutional Law	In this matter, the High Court of Orissa at Cuttack adjudicated issues between Represented by Adv. - Amlan Shakti Paul and STATE OF ODISHA. The Court rendered a decision disposing of the application under statutory provisions.	0	2026 LexGuard (OHC) A24B34CB	{"court": "High Court of Orissa at Cuttack", "title": "Represented by Adv. - Amlan Shakti Paul v. STATE OF ODISHA", "case_id": "a24b34cb-7db9-4533-ad5b-7491b538b6d6", "case_no": "NO. 12126 of 2026", "parties": "Represented by Adv. - Amlan Shakti Paul v. S