Kanagavel Murugan @ Kanagavel\n... Petitioner/\nAccused No.1\nVs\nThe State of Tamil Nadu rep by\nThe Inspector of Police,\nSipcot Police Station,\nThoothukudi District.\n(Crime No.683 of 2026)\n... Respondent/\nComplainant\nFor Petitioner : Mr.R.J.Karthick,\nAdvocate\nFor Respondent : Mr.T.Lenin Kumar,\nAdditional Public Prosecutor\nPETITION FOR BAIL Under Section 483 of B.N.S.S.\nPRAYER :-\nFor Bail in Crime No.683 of 2026 on the file of\nthe Respondent Police.\n1/6\nhttps://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis\nCRL OP(MD). No.23550 of 2026\nORDER : The Court made the following order :-\nThe petitioner / first accused, who was arrested\nand remanded to judicial custody on 27.09.2026 for\nthe offences punishable under Sections 296(b), 49,\n109(1), 115(2), 326(g) and 351(3) BNS, in Crime No.\n683 of 2026, on the file of the respondent police,\nseeks bail.\n2. The case of the prosecution is that the\ndefacto complainant and the second accused are\nhusband and wife and that the defacto complainant had\nbeen residing separately with his two children for\nthe past 1½ years. On 24.09.2026, at about 5.00 p.m.,\nthe second accused came to the house of the defacto\ncomplainant and asked her son to accompany her. When\nthey refused, she allegedly abused the defacto\ncomplainant in filthy language, assaulted the\nchildren and damaged the household articles.\nThereafter, she allegedly instigated the petitioner,\nwho is her brother, to commit the offence.\nAccordingly, on the same day, at about 11.45 p.m.,\nthe petitioner, along with two other persons, went to\n2/6\nhttps://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis\nCRL OP(MD). No.23550 of 2026\nthe house of the defacto complainant's parents and\nthrew a petrol bomb at the gate. When questioned\nabout the same, they allegedly abused his father in\nfilthy language, assaulted him and threatened him\nwith dire consequences. Hence, the complaint.\n3. The learned counsel appearing for the\npetitioner would submit that the petitioner is an\ninnocent and he has not committed any offence as\nalleged by the prosecution. He would further submit\nthat the petitioner is in judicial custody from\n27.09.2026.\n4. The learned Additional Public Prosecutor\nappearing for the respondent police would submit that\nthere are totally 4 accused and the petitioner is\narrayed as first accused, that the petitioner had\nalso attacked the injured, that the injured was\nalready discharged from the hospital, that the second\naccused was granted anticipatory bail by the\nPrincipal Sessions Court on 05.10.2026 and that the\npetitioner is not having any previous cases.\n3/6\nhttps://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis\nCRL OP(MD). No.23550 of 2026\n5. Considering the above facts and circumstances\nand also the facts that there existed matrimonial\ndispute between the defacto complainant and the\nsecond accused, that the injured was already\ndischarged from the hospital and that the petitioner\nis not having any bad antecedents, this Court is\ninclined to grant bail to the petitioner subject to\nthe following conditions:\n6. Accordingly, the petitioner is ordered to be\nreleased on bail on his executing a bond for a sum of\nRs.25,000/- (Rupees Twenty Five Thousand only) with\ntwo sureties each for a like sum to the satisfaction\nof the learned Judicial Magistrate No.III,\nThoothukudi, and on further conditions that:\n(i)the sureties shall affix their photographs\nand left thumb impression in the surety bond and the\nMagistrate / concerned court may obtain a copy of\ntheir Aadhar card or Bank Pass Book to ensure their\nidentity;\n(ii)the petitioner shall report before the\nrespondent police daily at 10.30 a.m., for a period\nof one month and thereafter, as and when required for\n4/6\nhttps://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis\nCRL OP(MD). No.23550 of 2026\ninterrogation;\n(iii)the petitioner shall not tamper with the\nevidence or witness either during investigation or\ntrial;\n(iv)the petitioner shall not abscond either\nduring investigation or trial;\n(v)On breach of any of the aforesaid conditions,\nthe learned Magistrate / Trial Court is entitled to\ntake appropriate action against the petitioner in\naccordance with law as if the conditions have been\nimposed and the petitioner is released on bail by the\nlearned Magistrate / Trial Court himself as laid down\nby the Hon'ble Supreme Court in P.K.Shaji vs. State\nof Kerala [(2005)AIR SCW 5560];\n(vi)If the accused thereafter abscond, a fresh\nFIR can be registered under Section 269 BNS, 2023.\n(K M S J)\n15.10.2026\nCSM\nTO\n1. The Judicial Magistrate No.III,\nThoothukudi.\n5/6\nhttps://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis\nCRL OP(MD). No.23550 of 2026\nK.MURALI SHANKAR,J\nCSM\n2. Do through\nThe Chief Judicial Magistrate,\nThoothukudi.\n3. The Superintendent,\nDistrict Jail,\nPerurani, Thoothukudi District.\n4. The Inspector of Police,\nSipcot Police Station,\nThoothukudi District.\n5. The Additional Public Prosecutor,\nMadurai Bench of Madras High Court,\nMadurai.\nORDER\nIN\nCRL OP(MD) No.23550 of 2026\nDate : 15.10.2026\n6/6\nhttps://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis	6	t	HCMD011474992026	Criminal Original Petition (Bail)	\N	Single Bench	Case QR Kanagavel Murugan @ Kanagavel	.	Mr.R.J.Karthick,	Mr.T.Lenin Kumar, Additional Public Prosecutor	Civil Law	In this criminal original petition under Criminal Law, the Court ruled on the dispute between Case QR Kanagavel Murugan @ Kanagavel and ..	0	2026 LexGuard (Crim) B04E5D	{"court": "Madras High Court (Madurai Bench)", "title": "Case QR Kanagavel Murugan @ Kanagavel v. .", "case_id": "b04e5d61-b58c-48af-bb57-f0e978af6342", "case_no": "CRL OP(MD). No.23550 of 2026", "parties": "Case QR Kanagavel Murugan @ Kanagavel v. .", "category": "BAIL_SUSPENSION", "petitioner": "Case QR Kanagavel Murugan @ Kanagavel", "respondent": ".", "legal_domain": "Civil Law", "category_facts": {"category": "BAIL_SUSPENSION", "surety_count": 2, "custody_period": null, "application_type": "Anticipatory Bail", "bail_bond_amount": 25000.0, "trial_court_fine": null, "reason_for_relief": null, "reporting_condition": null, "trial_court_sentence": null, "trial_court_fine_paid": false}, "activity_events": [], "profile_version": "2.5", "statutory_matrix": [], "activity_clusters": [], "scenario_clusters": ["pre_trial_custody"], "scenario_keywords": ["remand"], "procedural_posture": {"remedy": "Disposed of with directions.", "disposition": "Disposed of with directions."}}
cee620c2-4ecd-4e1d-a5c3-9879f038f95a	NO. 193 of 2026	Ors. v. Shakuntala Pipes Pvt. Ltd & Ors. .. for the	High Court at Calcutta	2026	Hon'ble Bench	Ors. v. Shakuntala Pipes Pvt. Ltd & Ors. .. for the	["Constitution of India"]	["Article 227"]	["civil & constitutional law", "chc", "disposed"]	Judgment in NO. 193 of 2026 delivered by Hon'ble Bench at High Court at Calcutta. The proceedings concern Civil & Constitutional Law with respect to Article 227.	Disposed	storage/cases/CHC_2026_NO_193_of_2026_cee620c2.pdf	c915a82a821ccd8bbc24c95640d8347da8b2efa493e00152fb134ed9fb54a7e8	\N	\N	\N	published	657396f3-5181-4922-8323-72d78b963be0	657396f3-5181-4922-8323-72d78b963be0	2026-10-25 14:52:01.981183+05:30	2026-10-25 14:52:01.981187+05:30	2026-10-26 10:38:09.564635+05:30	\N	[]	Holding and principles affirmed in NO. 193 of 2026 regarding Civil & Constitutional Law. The Court adjudicated upon Article 227.	[]	Disposed	[]	\N	unverified	Good Law (Binding Precedent)	23.10.2026\nCt. no. 7\nJPD.48\n(Vacation Bench)\nSD/PM\nCalcutta High Court\nIn the Circuit Bench at Jalpaiguri\n(From Principal Bench)\nCO 191 of 2026\nSanjay Mittal Agarwal & Ors.\nVS\nShakuntala Pipes Pvt. Ltd & Ors.\nMr. Piyush Chaturvedi, Ld. Sr. Adv.,\nMr. Dibanath Dey,\nMr. Tarun Kumar Das\n.. for the Petitioners\n1. By filing the instant revisional application under\nArticle 227 of the Constitution of India the\nplaintiff/revisionist prays for an appropriate order upon\nthe Trial Court directing him to dispose of the injunction\napplication as filed by the plaintiff within a specified\nperiod.\n2. At the time of hearing Mr. Chaturvedi, learned\nSenior Advocate appearing for the petitioner at the very\noutset draws attention of this Court to the server copy of\nthe Order No. 2 dated 14.08.2026 and Order No. 3 dated\n09.9.2026 as passed by the learned Trial Court in Title\nSuit No. 193 of 2026. It is submitted by Mr. Chaturvedi, on\nperusal of the said two orders as passed by the Trial Court,\nit would reveal that the learned advocate for the defendant\nno(s) 1 to 10 appeared and the plaintiff was directed to\nserve copy of the plaint and injunction application upon\nthe said learned Advocate for the defendant no(s).1 to 10.\n\n2\n3. Mr. Chaturvedi, upon instruction submits before\nthis Court that the Advocate on Record for the plaintiff has\nalready served the copy of the plaint and injunction\napplication of Title Suit No. 193 of 2026 upon the learned\nAdvocate for the contesting defendant no(s) 1 to 10 and\ndespite that by order no. 4 dated 15.12.2026 (which should\nbe read as “15.9.2026”) the learned Trial Court has fixed\nthe next date that is 21.11.2026 for S.R.\n4. Mr. Chaturvedi, submits that when all the\ncontesting respondents appeared before the learned Trial\nCourt there cannot be any difficulty to fix a date for\nhearing of the injunction application by the learned Trial\nCourt.\n5. On careful perusal of the entire materials as\nplaced before this Court, it appears that the instant\nrevisional application can be disposed of without passing a\ndirection for service of notice, since sufficient materials\nhave been placed before this Court, that despite\nappearance of all the defendants the learned Trial Court\nhas wrongly fixed 21.11.2026 for S.R.\n6. Such being the position this Court while disposing\nof the instant revisional application directs the learned\nTrial Court to fix the date of hearing of the injunction\napplication on December 1, 2026, with a liberty to the\ndefendants of the said suit to file their written objection\npositively on or before November 26, 2026 with a further\nliberty to the present revisionist/plaintiff to file affidavit-\nin-reply on or before November 30, 2026.\n\n3\n7. The time limits as fixed by this Court are\nperemptory and mandatory. The learned Trial Court is\ndirected to hear out the injunction application positively\non the day as fixed by this Court and in the event of the\nnon-availability of the regular Presiding Officer of the said\nTrial Court, the Judge-in-Charge of the said Court will\nhear out the injunction application and shall pass a\njudicial order on such injunction application positively by\nDecember 15, 2026.\n8. Since this order is passed in absence of the\ndefendants/opposite parties, the learned Advocate on\nRecord for the revisionst is hereby requested to\ncommunicate the server copy of the order upon all the\nopposite parties as well as upon the learned advocate for\nthe defendants in Title Suit No. 193 of 2026 by speed post\nand to file proof of service to the learned Trial Court.\n9. With the above observation CO 191 of 2026\nstands disposed of.\n10. Parties shall act on the server copy of this order.\n(Partha Sarathi Sen, J.)	3	t	HCMA010001932026	Judicial Precedent	2026-10-23	Single Bench	Ors.	Shakuntala Pipes Pvt. Ltd & Ors. .. for the	\N	\N	Civil & Constitutional Law	In this matter, the High Court at Calcutta adjudicated issues between CO 191 of 2026 Sanjay Mittal Agarwal & Ors and Shakuntala Pipes Pvt. Ltd & Ors. .. for the. The Court rendered a decision disposing of the application under statutory provisions.	0	2026 LexGuard (CHC) CEE620C2	{"court": "High Court at Calcutta", "title": "CO 191 of 2026 Sanjay Mittal Agarwal & Ors v. Shakuntala Pipes Pvt. Ltd & Ors. .. for the", "case_id": "cee620c2-4ecd-4e1d-a5c3-9879f038f95a", "case_no": "NO. 193 of 2026", "parties": "CO 191 of 2026 Sanjay Mittal Agarwal & Ors v. Shakuntala Pipes Pvt. Ltd & Ors. .. for the", "category": "GENERAL_CONSTITUTIONAL", "petitioner": "CO 191 of 2026 Sanjay Mittal Agarwal & Ors", "respondent": "Shakuntala Pipes Pvt. Ltd & Ors. .. for the", "legal_domain": "Civil & Constitutional Law", "category_facts": {"category": "GENERAL_CONSTITUTIONAL", "remedy_type": "Writ Petition / Criminal Appeal", "judicial_disposition": "Dismissed", "constitutional_article": "Article 226 / Article 21"}, "activity_events": [], "profile_version": "2.5", "statutory_matrix": [{"act": "CONSTITUTION", "section": "227", "canonical": "Section 227 CONSTITUTION", "equivalents": []}], "activity_clusters": [], "scenario_clusters": [], "scenario_keywords": [], "procedural_posture": {"remedy": "Disposed", "disposition": "Disposed"}}
d2ae5ce1-a53d-4cc6-a6d5-e8a336b1c3a4	NO. 14150 OF 2026	Jumma Masjid Trust, Dahanu Gaon through its Chairman Mustakim Harun Patel v. The State of Maharashtra through Collector and Others	High Court of Judicature at Bombay	2026	Hon'ble R. I. CHAGLA AND	Jumma Masjid Trust, Dahanu Gaon through its Chairman Mustakim Harun Patel v. The State of Maharashtra through Collector and Others	["Maharashtra Town Planning Act"]	["Section 53 Maharashtra Town Planning Act"]	["civil & constitutional law", "bhc", "disposed"]	Judgment in NO. 14150 OF 2026 delivered by Hon'ble R. I. CHAGLA AND at High Court of Judicature at Bombay. The proceedings concern Civil & Constitutional Law with respect to procedural compliance.	Disposed	storage/cases/BHC_2026_NO_14150_OF_2026_d2ae5ce1.pdf	b742ec08f4c801f30020d41ebb19b557d0de061fd3783e26222165b18adddd57	\N	\N	\N	published	657396f3-5181-4922-8323-72d78b963be0	657396f3-5181-4922-8323-72d78b963be0	2026-10-25 14:51:29.235752+05:30	2026-10-25 14:51:29.235755+05:30	2026-10-26 10:38:09.565381+05:30	\N	[]	Holding and principles affirmed in NO. 14150 OF 2026 regarding Civil & Constitutional Law. The Court adjudicated upon applicable judicial standards.	[]	Disposed	[]	\N	unverified	Good Law (Binding Precedent)	1 904-wp-14150-\n2026.doc\nIN THE HIGH COURT OF JUDICATURE AT BOMBAY\nCIVIL APPELLATE JURISDICTION\nWRIT PETITION NO. 14150 OF 2026\nJumma Masjid Trust, Dahanu Gaon through\nits Chairman Mustakim Harun Patel ...Petitioner\nVs.\nThe State of Maharashtra through\nCollector and Others ...Respondents\n-----------------\nDr. Uday Warunjikar a/w. Mr. Sumit Kate a/w. Ms. Gargi Warunjikar, for the\nPetitioner.\nMs. Reena A. Salunkhe, AGP, for the Respondent / State.\nMr. Kiran Bapat, Senior Counsel i/b. Mr. Mahendra V. Shingade a/w. Mr.\nPrabhat R. Salunkhe and Mr. Jenish Kansara, for Respondent No.2.\n-----------------\nM AM AM AR TA\nDsMAK i\nMA\nigA g\nL\nnMA ite\nER\nadT l l Abyy\nKALE D21+ 01 a 0 2: t 51 e6 39 :. 0 1:008.23\nCORAM : R. I. CHAGLA AND\nFIRDOSH P. POONIWALLA, JJ.\nDATED : 22nd OCTOBER, 2026\nP.C.:-\n1. The parties have arrived at a workable arrangement in the\npresent Writ Petition. Accordingly, the following order is passed by consent\nof the parties.\nORDER\na) The impugned Notice dated 7th October 2026 issued by\nMamta Kale 1/3\n\n2 904-wp-14150-\n2026.doc\nRespondent No.2, under Section 53 of the Maharashtra Town\nPlanning Act, 1966, is recalled by Respondent No.2.\nb) A fresh Show Cause Notice shall be issued by Respondent\nNo.2 within a period of one week from today, i.e., on or before\n29th October 2026, providing all relevant documents which the\nfresh Show Cause Notice relies upon, to the Petitioner.\nc) The Petitioner shall reply to the Show Cause Notice\nwithin a period of two weeks from issuance of Show Cause\nNotice viz., on or before 16th November 2026.\nd) Respondent No.2 shall fix a hearing on 17th November\n2026, at 11:00 a.m., wherein the Petitioner shall remain\npresent along with any documents which the Petitioner intends\nto rely upon.\ne) Respondent No.2 shall pass a reasoned speaking Order\nafter hearing the Petitioner on or before 25th November 2026\nand it shall be served on the Petitioner within a period of one\nweek from the date of passing of the Order.\nf) In the event the decision of Respondent No.2 is adverse\nto the Petitioner, liberty is granted to the Petitioner to adopt\nappropriate proceedings, and for which the decision shall be\nnot acted upon for a period of one week from service on the\nPetitioner.\nMamta Kale 2/3\n\n3 904-wp-14150-\n2026.doc\ng) The rights and contentions of the parties are expressly\nkept open.\n2. The Writ Petition is disposed of in the above terms. There shall\nbe no order as to costs.\n[FIRDOSH P. POONIWALLA, J.] [R.I. CHAGLA, J.]\nMamta Kale 3/3	3	t	BHCB010141502026	Judicial Precedent	2026-10-23	Single Bench	Jumma Masjid Trust, Dahanu Gaon through its Chairman Mustakim Harun Patel	The State of Maharashtra through Collector and Others	\N	N