Bench	B. S. CASTELINO ... APPLICANT	STATE OF GOA, THROUGH THE CHIEF SECRETARY AND 4 ORS	\N	nos. 1 to 3.	Civil & Constitutional Law	In this matter, the High Court of Judicature adjudicated issues between RONIE MENEZES ALIAS RONEY MENEZES REP. BY P.O.A, B. S. CASTELINO and STATE OF GOA, THROUGH THE CHIEF SECRETARY AND 4 ORS. The Court rendered a decision disposing of the application under statutory provisions.	0	2026 LexGuard (HC) D2B2EAA8	{"court": "High Court of Judicature", "title": "RONIE MENEZES ALIAS RONEY MENEZES REP. BY P.O.A, B. S. CASTELINO v. STATE OF GOA, THROUGH THE CHIEF SECRETARY AND 4 ORS", "case_id": "d2b2eaa8-83e9-4447-b33d-491dea098587", "case_no": "NO. 30 OF 2025", "parties": "RONIE MENEZES ALIAS RONEY MENEZES REP. BY P.O.A, B. S. CASTELINO v. STATE OF GOA, THROUGH THE CHIEF SECRETARY AND 4 ORS", "category": "GENERAL_CONSTITUTIONAL", "petitioner": "RONIE MENEZES ALIAS RONEY MENEZES REP. BY P.O.A, B. S. CASTELINO", "respondent": "STATE OF GOA, THROUGH THE CHIEF SECRETARY AND 4 ORS", "legal_domain": "Civil & Constitutional Law", "category_facts": {"category": "GENERAL_CONSTITUTIONAL", "remedy_type": "Writ Petition / Criminal Appeal", "judicial_disposition": "Allowed", "constitutional_article": "Article 226 / Article 21"}, "activity_events": [], "profile_version": "2.5", "statutory_matrix": [], "activity_clusters": [], "scenario_clusters": [], "scenario_keywords": [], "procedural_posture": {"remedy": "Allowed", "disposition": "Allowed"}}
d6f56647-206f-4ac0-8544-a44d0ff52ba8	NO. 2937 OF 2026	Applicant v. The State of Maharashtra	High Court of Judicature at Bombay	2026	Hon'ble MADHAV J. JAMDAR, J	Applicant v. The State of Maharashtra	["Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023", "Food Safety and Standards Act", "Indian Penal Code, 1860", "of BNS", "of IPC"]	["Section 123 of BNS", "Section 26(2)(i) Food Safety and Standards Act", "Section 26(2)(iv) Food Safety and Standards Act", "Section 328 of IPC", "Section 59 Food Safety and Standards Act"]	["civil & constitutional law", "bhc", "disposed"]	Judgment in NO. 2937 OF 2026 delivered by Hon'ble MADHAV J. JAMDAR, J at High Court of Judicature at Bombay. The proceedings concern Civil & Constitutional Law with respect to procedural compliance.	Disposed	storage/cases/BHC_2026_NO_2937_OF_2026_d6f56647.pdf	9e1c25a32a1b9ea924574c8ceb8cda2ef8154fc9252ee3d23d041921fd966dab	\N	\N	\N	published	657396f3-5181-4922-8323-72d78b963be0	657396f3-5181-4922-8323-72d78b963be0	2026-10-25 14:51:46.652032+05:30	2026-10-25 14:51:46.652042+05:30	2026-10-26 10:38:09.56673+05:30	\N	[]	Holding and principles affirmed in NO. 2937 OF 2026 regarding Civil & Constitutional Law. The Court adjudicated upon applicable judicial standards.	[]	Disposed	[]	\N	unverified	Good Law (Binding Precedent)	914 ABA-2937-2026.DOC\nskt\nIN THE HIGH COURT OF JUDICATURE AT BOMBAY\nCRIMINAL APPELLATE JURISDICTION\nANTICIPATORY BAIL APPLICATION NO. 2937 OF 2026\nSagar Fulchand Luniya …Applicant\nVersus\nThe State of Maharashtra …Respondent\nMr. Piyush R Toshnival a/w. Yash R. Sonawale, for the Applicant.\nMrs. M.R. Tidke, APP, for the Respondent-State.\nCORAM: MADHAV J. JAMDAR, J.\nDATE : 22nd OCTOBER 2026\nPC:-\n1. Heard Mr. Toshnival, learned Counsel appearing for the\nApplicant and Mrs. Tidke, learned APP, for the Respondent-State of\nMaharashtra.\n2. By the present Anticipatory Bail Application, the Applicant is\nseeking pre-arrest bail in connection with C.R. No.688 of 2026\nregistered on 4th September 2026 with Kondhwa Police Station,\nDistrict Pune, for the offences punishable under Sections 123, 223,\n274 and 275 read with Section 3(5) of the Bharatiya Nyaya\nSanhita, 2023 (“BNS”) and Sections 26(2)(i), 26(2)(iv) and 59 of\nthe Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 and Sections 7(2), 20(2)\nof the Cigarettes and Other Tobacco Products (Prohibition of\nPage 1/ 6\n22nd October 2026\n\n914 ABA-2937-2026.DOC\nskt\nAdvertisement and Regulation of Trade and Commerce,\nProduction, Supply and Distribution) Act, 2003 (“COTPA Act”).\n3. As per the prosecution case, the Applicant was procuring\ncontraband material which is unsafe and dangerous for the health\nof people.\n4. It is the submission of Mr. Toshnival, learned Counsel, that\nexcept the offence under Section 123 of BNS, all other offences are\nbailable offences. He submits that as far as Section 123 of BNS is\nconcerned, the Supreme Court is considering the applicability of\nSection 123 (i.e. Section 328 of IPC) to the similar cases. He\ntherefore, states that the anticipatory bail be granted.\n5. On the other hand, Mrs. Tidke, learned APP, strongly opposes\nthe Anticipatory Bail Application. He submits that the offence is\nvery serious and, therefore, the Anticipatory Bail Application be\nrejected. On instructions, learned APP submits that there is one\nantecedent against the Applicant.\n6. Learned APP submits that if this Court is inclined to grant\nanticipatory bail then the Applicant be directed to give undertaking\nPage 2/ 6\n22nd October 2026\n\n914 ABA-2937-2026.DOC\nskt\nin terms of Order of the Supreme Court in the case of Abhijit\nJitendra Lolage v. State of Maharashtra 1 and more particularly\nrelies on following condition imposed by the Supreme Court in\ncase of similar offences:\n“It is deemed appropriate to impose the\ncondition – “I, Abhijeet Jitendra Lolage do\nundertake to not deal with Gutkha, that is, Pan\nMasala with Tobacco”. In case, the appellant –\nAbhijeet Jitendra Lolage violates the terms and\nconditions of bail, including the undertaking\nimposed, it would be open to the prosecution to\nseek cancellation of bail.”\n(Emphasis added)\nMr. Toshnival, learned Counsel appearing for the Applicant, after\ntaking instructions, submits that the Applicant will give the\nundertaking.\n7. The Supreme Court in the said order has imposed the above\ncondition in case of similar offence.\n8. Perusal of the record shows that except the offence under\nSection 123 of BNS the other offences are bailable offences. The\nissue whether Section 123 of BNS will apply to similar cases is\npending before the Supreme Court. As the Applicant is ready to\n1 SLP (Crl.) Diary No.2806/2023\nPage 3/ 6\n22nd October 2026\n\n914 ABA-2937-2026.DOC\nskt\ngive the undertaking that he will not deal with Gutkha and\nTobacco products in any manner whatsoever, the case is made out\nfor grant of anticipatory bail.\n9. In view thereof, the following order is passed:\nO R D E R\n(a) In the event of arrest of the Applicant-Sagar Fulchand\nLuniya in connection with C.R. No.688 of 2026\nregistered with Kondhwa Police Station, District Pune,\nthe Applicant is directed to be released on bail on his\nfurnishing PR Bond in the sum of Rs.1,00,000/- with\none or two solvent sureties in the like amount.\n(b) The Applicant shall attend the concerned Police\nStation once in a month, i.e., first Sunday of each\nmonth, till filing of the charge-sheet and shall\ncooperate with the investigation.\n(c) The Applicant to furnish an undertaking that he will\nnot deal with banned products i.e. Gutkha, Pan\nMasala with Tobacco products, etc., in any manner\nwhatsoever. Such undertaking is to be filed in this\nCourt within a period of two weeks from today. The\nPage 4/ 6\n22nd October 2026\n\n914 ABA-2937-2026.DOC\nskt\nApplicant to strictly comply with the said undertaking.\n(d) The Applicant shall furnish his cell phone number and\nresidential address to the Investigating Officer and\nshall keep the same updated, in case of any change\nthereto.\n(e) The Applicant shall not directly or indirectly make any\ninducement, threat, or promise to any person\nacquainted with the facts of the case so as to dissuade\nsuch a person from disclosing the facts to the Court or\nto any Police personnel.\n(f) The Applicant shall not tamper with the prosecution\nevidence and shall not contact or influence the\nComplainant or any witness in any manner.\n(g) The Applicant shall not leave India without prior\npermission of the Court.\n(h) In case, the Applicant violates the terms and\nconditions of bail, including the undertaking, it would\nbe open to the prosecution to seek cancellation of bail.\nPage 5/ 6\n22nd October 2026\n\n914 ABA-2937-2026.DOC\nskt\n10. The Anticipatory Bail Application is disposed of accordingly.\n[MADHAV J. JAMDAR, J.]\nPage 6/ 6\n22nd October 2026	6	t	BHCB010029372026	Judicial Precedent	2026-10-23	Single Bench	Applicant	The State of Maharashtra	\N	\N	Civil & Constitutional Law	In this matter, the High Court of Judicature at Bombay adjudicated issues between skt Sagar Fulchand Luniya and The State of Maharashtra. The Court rendered a decision disposing of the application under statutory provisions.	0	2026 LexGuard (BHC) D6F56647	{"court": "High Court of Judicature at Bombay", "title": "skt Sagar Fulchand Luniya v. The State of Maharashtra", "case_id": "d6f56647-206f-4ac0-8544-a44d0ff52ba8", "case_no": "NO. 2937 OF 2026", "parties": "skt Sagar Fulchand Luniya v. The State of Maharashtra", "category": "NDPS", "petitioner": "skt Sagar Fulchand Luniya", "respondent": "The State of Maharashtra", "legal_domain": "Civil & Constitutional Law", "category_facts": {"category": "NDPS", "custody_period": null, "contraband_type": "Contraband / Narcotics", "seized_quantity": null, "statutory_issue": "Bail / Pre-trial Release under NDPS Act", "quantity_category": "Intermediate Quantity", "section_37_embargo": false, "search_compliance_sec_50": "Search procedure evaluated"}, "activity_events": [], "profile_version": "2.5", "statutory_matrix": [], "activity_clusters": [], "scenario_clusters": [], "scenario_keywords": [], "procedural_posture": {"remedy": "Disposed", "disposition": "Disposed"}}
d9cbd3d9-857e-4557-823c-426728f8f230	NO. 30869 of 2026	Crl.O.P.No.30869 of 2026 A.Palanisamy v. The State Rep. by, The Inspector of Police Gobi All Women Police Station.	Madras High Court (Principal Seat, Chennai)	2026	Hon'ble Mr. Justice N.Ramesh	Crl.O.P.No.30869 of 2026 A.Palanisamy v. The State Rep. by, The Inspector of Police Gobi All Women Police Station.	["Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita, 2023", "Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023", "Protection of Children from Sexual Offences Act, 2012", "of BNSS"]	["Section 183 of BNSS"]	["civil & constitutional law", "mhc", "disposed"]	Judgment in NO. 30869 of 2026 delivered by Hon'ble THE HON'BLE MR. JUSTICE N.RAMESH at Madras High Court (Principal Seat, Chennai). The proceedings concern Civil & Constitutional Law with respect to procedural compliance.	Bail Granted	storage/cases/MHC_2026_NO_30869_of_2026_d9cbd3d9.pdf	bd6eb4ff0a417e81a8eac14a31857ea70512150edc248ca36c091b4da5813faf	\N	\N	\N	published	657396f3-5181-4922-8323-72d78b963be0	657396f3-5181-4922-8323-72d78b963be0	2026-10-25 14:51:56.626473+05:30	2026-10-25 14:51:56.62648+05:30	2026-10-26 10:38:09.567834+05:30	2. The case of the prosecution is that the petitioner, who is the father of the victim girl aged about 14 years, had committed repeated sexual assault on his own daughter in a drunken state. Consequently, the present case was registered against the petitioner. 3.	[]	Regular bail granted in NO. 30869 of 2026 under applicable statutory provisions, considering the duration of incarceration and absence of flight risk, subject to executing bond and standard reporting conditions.	[]	Allowed	["ble Supreme Court in P.K.Shaji vs. State of Kerala [(2005)13 SCC 283]"]	\N	unverified	Good Law (Binding Precedent)	Crl.O.P.No.30869 of 2026\nIN THE HIGH COURT OF JUDICATURE AT MADRAS\nDATED: 23-10-2026\nCORAM\nTHE HON'BLE MR. JUSTICE N.RAMESH\nCrl.O.P.No.30869 of 2026\nCNR: {HCMA012560772026}\nA.Palanisamy ..Petitioner(s)\nVs\nThe State Rep. by,\nThe Inspector of Police\nGobi All Women Police Station.\nCrime No.21 of 2026.\n..Respondent(s)\nPRAYER: Criminal Original Petition is filed petition under Section 483 of\nBharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita, 2023, to enlarge the Petitioner on bail in\nSpl.SC.No.136 of 2026 pending trial on the file of Learned Sessions Judge,\nMagalir Neethi Mandram (Fast Track Mahila Court), Erode.\nFor Petitioner(s) : Mr. J.Ranjithkumar\nFor Respondent(s) : Mrs.R.S.Indira\nAdditional Public Prosecutor\nORDER\nThe petitioner, who was arrested and remanded to judicial custody on\n10.06.2026 for the alleged offences punishable under Sections 7 & 8 of the\nProtection of Children from Sexual Offences (POCSO) Act, 2012, in\nSpl.SC.No.136 of 2026 pending trial on the file of Learned Sessions Judge,\nMagalir Neethi Mandram (Fast Track Mahila Court), Erode, in connection with\nCrime No.21 of 2026, on the file of the respondent police, seeks regular bail.\nPage 1 of 6\nhttps://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis\n\nCrl.O.P.No.30869 of 2026\n2. The case of the prosecution is that the petitioner, who is the father\nof the victim girl aged about 14 years, had committed repeated sexual assault on\nhis own daughter in a drunken state. Consequently, the present case was\nregistered against the petitioner.\n3. Learned counsel appearing for the petitioner submits that the\npetitioner is innocent and has been falsely implicated in the present case. He\nfurther undertakes that the petitioner will strictly abide by any stringent\nconditions imposed by this Court and will co-operate in the investigation. He\nfurther submits that the petitioner has been incarcerated in judicial custody since\n10.06.2026. Hence, he prays that the petitioner may be granted bail.\n4. On the other hand, the learned Additional Public Prosecutor\nappearing for the respondent strongly opposes the grant of bail to the petitioner\nand produced the statement of the victim girl recorded under Section 183 of\nBNSS. She further submits that it is the case where the petitioner/accused had\ntouched inappropriately his own daughter/victim girl. He also submits the\ncharge sheet in this case has been filed and the same has also been taken on the\nfile of the Magalir Neethi Mandram (Fast Track Mahila Court), Erode, in\nSpl.S.C.No.136 of 2026. She also submits that the case now stands posted on\n28.10.2026 for framing of charges.\nPage 2 of 6\nhttps://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis\n\nCrl.O.P.No.30869 of 2026\n5. I have gone through the statement of the victim child. Considering\nthe fact that the investigation in this case has been completed and the case has\nbeen posted for framing of charges and taking note of the period of\nincarceration undergone by the petitioner, this Court is inclined to grant regular\nbail to the petitioner, subject to strict conditions to ensure his presence during\nthe trial.\n6. Accordingly, the petitioner is ordered to be released on bail on his\nexecuting a bond for a sum of Rs.25,000/- (Rupees Twenty Five Thousand\nonly) with two sureties, each for a like sum to the satisfaction of the learned\nSessions Judge, Magalir Neethi Mandram (Fast Track Mahila Court),\nErode District, and on further conditions that:\n[a] The sureties shall affix his photographs and Left Thumb\nImpression in the Application for Surety ship [Judicial Form No.46\nannexed to 'The Criminal Rules of Practice, 2019']. The learned\nMagistrate shall obtain a copy of any one of the identity proofs to\nensure his identity;\n[b] The petitioner shall appear before the trial Court daily at\n10.30 a.m. until further orders;\n[c] The petitioner shall not, in any way, meet her\ndaughter/victim, nor shall he attempt to influence the witnesses;\n[d] The petitioner shall not abscond during trial;\nPage 3 of 6\nhttps://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis\n\nCrl.O.P.No.30869 of 2026\n[e] The petitioner shall not tamper with the evidence or\nwitness during trial;\n[f] On breach of any of the aforementioned conditions, the\nlearned Magistrate/Trial Court is entitled to pass appropriate orders\nagainst the petitioner in accordance with law as if the\naforementioned conditions have been imposed and the petitioner\nreleased on bail by the learned Magistrate/Trial Court himself as\nlaid down by the Hon'ble Supreme Court in P.K.Shaji vs. State of\nKerala [(2005)13 SCC 283]; and\n[g] If the accused thereafter absconds, a fresh FIR can be\nregistered under Section 269 of B.N.S.\n23-10-2026\nNeutral Citation: Yes/No\nham\nNote:\n1. Registry is directed to forthwith upload this\norder on the Official Website of this Court.\n2. All concerned to act on this order being\nuploaded on Official Website of this Court\nwithout insisting on certified hard copies. To\nbe noted, this order, when uploaded on the\nofficial website of this Court, will be\nwatermarked and will also have a QR code.\nPage 4 of 6\nhttps://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis\n\nCrl.O.P.No.30869 of 2026\nTo\n1. The Sessions Judge,\nMagalir Neethi Mandram (Fast Track Mahila Court),\nErode.\n2. The Inspector of Police,\nGobi All Women Police Station.\n3. The Superintendent,\nDistrict Jail, Gopichettipalayam.\n4. The Public Prosecutor,\nHigh Court of Madras.\nPage 5 of 6\nhttps://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis\n\nCrl.O.P.No.30869 of 2026\nN.RAMESH, J.\nham\nCrl.O.P.No.30869 of 2026\n23-10-2026\nPage 6 of 6\nhttps://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis	6	t	HCMA012560772026	Judicial Precedent	2026-10-23	Single Bench	Crl.O.P.No.30869 of 2026 A.Palanisamy	The State Rep. by, The Inspector of Police Gobi All Women Police Station.	Mr. J.Ranjithkumar	Mrs.R.S.Indira Additional Public Prosecutor	Civil & Constitutional Law	In this matter, the Madras High Court (Principal Seat, Chennai) adjudicated issues between Crl.O.P.No.30869 of 2026 A.Palanisamy and The State Rep. by, The Inspector of Police. The Court rendered a decision disposing of the application under statutory provisions.	0	2026 LexGuard (MHC) D9CBD3D9	{"court": "Madras High Court (Principal Seat, Chennai)", "title": "Crl.O.P.No.30869 of 2026 A.Palanisamy v. The State Rep. by, The Inspector of Police", "case_id": "d9cbd3d9-857e-4557-823c-426728f8f230", "case_no": "NO. 30869 of 2026", "parties": "Crl.O.P.No.30869 of 2026 A.Palanisamy v. The State Rep. by, The Inspector of Police", "category": "BAIL_SUSPENSION", "petitioner": "Crl.O.P.No.30869 of 2026 A.Palanisamy", "respondent": "The State Rep. by, The Inspector of Police", "legal_domain": "Civil & Constitutional Law", "category_facts": {"category": "BAIL_SUSPENSION", "surety_count": 2, "custody_period": null, "application_type": "Regular Bail", "bail_bond_amount": 25000.0, "trial_court_fine": null, "reason_for_relief": null, "reporting_condition": "appear before the trial Court daily at", "trial_court_sentence": null, "trial_court_fine_paid": false}, "activity_events": [], "profile_version": "2.5", "statutory_matrix": [], "activity_clusters": [], "scenario_clusters": [], "scenario_keywords": [], "procedural_posture": {"remedy": "Disposed", "disposition": "Disposed"}}
dc3d190e-67b3-4975-8d49-9eeb6b8ee6c4	NO. 7854 OF 2023	Petitioner v. Respondent / State	High Court of Judicature at Bombay (Nagpur Bench)	2026	Hon'ble ANIL L. PANSARE & NIVEDITA P. MEHTA, JJ	Petitioner v. Respondent / State	[]	[]	["civil & constitutional law", "bhc", "disposed"]	Judgment in NO. 7854 OF 2023 delivered by Hon'ble ANIL L. PANSARE & NIVEDITA P. MEHTA, JJ at High Court of Judicature at Bombay (Nagpur Bench). The proceedings concern Civil & Constitutional Law with respect to procedural compliance.	Disposed	storage/cases/BHC_2026_NO_7854_OF_2023_dc3d190e.pdf	b8a3d52cc2b4c916482b4d684ff76cbc5931821e16f9644b47e17a494f0d3433	\N	\N	\N	published	657396f3-5181-4922-8323-72d78b963be0	657396f3-5181-4922-8323-72d78b963be0	2026-10-25 14:51:52.467018+05:30	2026-10-25 14:51:52.467023+05:30	2026-10-26 10:38:09.569087+05:30	\N	[]	Holding and principles affirmed in NO. 7854 OF 2023 regarding Civil & Constitutional Law. The Court adjudicated upon applicable judicial standards.	[]	Disposed	[]	\N	unverified	Good Law (Binding Precedent)	2026:BHC-NAG:14209-DB\n1\nwp 7854.23\nIN THE HIGH COURT OF JUDICATURE AT BOMBAY,\nNAGPUR BENCH, AT NAGPUR.\nWRIT PETITION NO. 7854 OF 2023\n( Madhorao s/o Vithoba Sukhdeve ..vs.. State of Maharashtra, through its Secretary, School Education\nand Sports Department, Mumbai and others )\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\nOffice Notes, Office Memoranda of Coram, Court's or Judge's orders\nappearances, Court's orders of directions\nand Registrar's orders\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\nMr. Bhushan Dafle, Counsel for the petitioner,\nMr. S.A. Ashirgade, Addl.G.P. for respondent Nos. 1 to 3.\nCORAM : ANIL L. PANSARE & NIVEDITA P. MEHTA, JJ.\nDATED : 22 nd OCTOBER, 2026\nThe petitioner has filed the present petition seeking a direction to\nrespondent No. 1 to decide the proposal dated 23-05-2018. The learned\nAdditional Government Pleader was requested to obtain instructions as to\nwhether the proposal dated 23-05-2018 has been decided and taken to its\nlogical conclusion. In response, the learned Additional Government\nPleader submits that the proposal dated 23-05-2018 was decided by\nrespondent No. 1 on 28-10-2020.\n2. In view of the aforesaid statement, the learned Counsel for the\npetitioner submits that the relief sought in the petition has been redressed\nand, therefore, seeks permission to withdraw the petition.\n3. Permission, as sought, is granted.\n4. The petition stands disposed of as withdrawn.\n(Nivedita P. Mehta, J.) (Anil L. Pansare, J.)\nadgokar	1	t	BHCB010078542026	Judicial Precedent	2026-10-23	Single Bench	Petitioner	Respondent / State	\N	Nos. 1 to 3.	Civil & Constitutional Law	In this matter, the High Court of Judicature at Bombay (Nagpur Bench) adjudicated issues between Petitioner and Respondent / State. The Court rendered a decision disposing of the application under statutory provisions.	0	2026 LexGuard (BHC) DC3D190E	{"court": "High Court of Judicature at Bombay (Nagpur Bench)", "title": "Petitioner v. Respondent / State", "case_id": "dc3d190e-67b3-4975-8d49-9eeb6b8ee6c4", "case_no": "NO. 7854 OF 2023", "parties": "Petitioner v. Respondent / State", "category": "GENERAL_CONSTITUTIONAL", "petitioner": "Petitioner", "respondent": "Respondent / State", "legal_domain": "Civil & Constitutional Law", "category_facts": {"category": "GENERAL_CONSTITUTIONAL", "remedy_type": "Writ Petition / Criminal Appeal", "judicial_disposition": "Dismissed", "constitutional_article": "Article 226 / Article 21"}, "activity_events": [], "profile_version": "2.5", "statutory_matrix": [], "activity_clusters": [], "scenario_clusters": [], "scenario_keywords": [], "procedural_posture": {"remedy": "Disposed", "disposition": "Disposed"}}
