eby and\nwhereunder the prescribed Authority has fixed the\ndate of meeting on motion for removal of Pradhan\non 29.09.2026.\n3. At the time of hearing, it is submitted at the bar\nthat pursuant to the said notice of motion, the\nremoval of Pradhan has been effected.\n4. The learned Advocate appearing on behalf of the\nwrit petitioner submits before this Court that\nsimilar such notice was issued on 05.10.2026\n\n2\nwhere the proposed meeting was scheduled to be\nheld on 13.10.2026, the date of which has already\nbeen expired.\n5. In view of such, this Court finds that with the\npassage of time, the instant writ petition has\nbecome infructuous and nothing remains to be\ndecided in respect of the impugned notice.\n6. With the aforesaid observation, the instant writ\npetition is disposed of.\n(Partha Sarathi Sen, J.)	2	t	HCMA010278672026	Writ Petition	\N	Single Bench	Tafijul Hoque	State of West Bengal & Ors.	\N	\N	Civil Law	In this writ petition under Constitutional Law, the Court ruled on the dispute between Tafijul Hoque and State of West Bengal & Ors..	0	2026 LexGuard (Writ) E673E4	{"court": "High Court at Calcutta (Appellate Side)", "title": "Tafijul Hoque v. State of West Bengal & Ors.", "case_id": "e673e489-69cf-481b-b029-4a542c1b5e6b", "case_no": "WPA 27867 of 2026", "parties": "Tafijul Hoque v. State of West Bengal & Ors.", "category": "GENERAL_CONSTITUTIONAL", "petitioner": "Tafijul Hoque", "respondent": "State of West Bengal & Ors.", "legal_domain": "Civil Law", "category_facts": {"category": "GENERAL_CONSTITUTIONAL", "remedy_type": "Writ Petition / Criminal Appeal", "judicial_disposition": "Dismissed", "constitutional_article": "Article 226 / Article 21"}, "activity_events": [], "profile_version": "2.5", "statutory_matrix": [{"act": "CONSTITUTION", "section": "226", "canonical": "Section 226 CONSTITUTION", "equivalents": []}], "activity_clusters": [], "scenario_clusters": ["constitutional_fundamental"], "scenario_keywords": ["writ of mandamus", "article 226"], "procedural_posture": {"remedy": "Disposed", "disposition": "Disposed"}}
e9631da8-860d-4602-8252-d73bfcd7893f	NO. 12099 of 2026	Represented by Adv. - Sujit Kumar Pattnaik v. State Of Odisha	High Court of Orissa at Cuttack	2026	Hon'ble THE HON’BLE MR. JUSTICE ADITYA KUMAR	Represented by Adv. - Sujit Kumar Pattnaik v. State Of Odisha	["Orissa Prevention of Gambling Act"]	["Section 3 Orissa Prevention of Gambling Act"]	["civil & constitutional law", "ohc", "disposed"]	Judgment in NO. 12099 of 2026 delivered by Hon'ble THE HON’BLE MR. JUSTICE ADITYA KUMAR at High Court of Orissa at Cuttack. The proceedings concern Civil & Constitutional Law with respect to Section 482.	Disposed	storage/cases/OHC_2026_NO_12099_of_2026_e9631da8.pdf	fd63e869d7d91a18d7b29eb8e242ebb6ecf4e81b5768a6f80f6abeea47b8d623	\N	\N	\N	published	657396f3-5181-4922-8323-72d78b963be0	657396f3-5181-4922-8323-72d78b963be0	2026-10-25 14:51:58.546637+05:30	2026-10-25 14:51:58.546645+05:30	2026-10-26 10:38:09.574014+05:30	23.10.2026 Order No. 01. 1. This matter is taken up through Virtual Mode. 2. Heard learned counsel for the Petitioner and learned Counsel for the State. Perused the Anticipatory Bail Application as well as the F.I.R.	[]	Holding and principles affirmed in NO. 12099 of 2026 regarding Civil & Constitutional Law. The Court adjudicated upon Section 482.	[]	Disposed	[]	\N	unverified	Good Law (Binding Precedent)	IN THE HIGH COURT OF ORISSA AT CUTTACK\nABLAPL No.12099 of 2026\nCNR No. ODHC010808702026\nRaja Swain ..... Petitioner\nRepresented by Adv. -\nSujit Kumar Pattnaik\n-versus-\nState Of Odisha ..... Opposite Party\nRepresented by Adv. -\nP.Satpathy, A.S.C.\nCORAM:\nTHE HON’BLE MR. JUSTICE ADITYA KUMAR\nMOHAPATRA\nORDER\n23.10.2026\nOrder No.\n01. 1. This matter is taken up through Virtual Mode.\n2. Heard learned counsel for the Petitioner and learned Counsel\nfor the State. Perused the Anticipatory Bail Application as well as\nthe F.I.R.\n3. This is an application under Section 482 of the B.N.S.S.,\n2023 filed by the Petitioner for anticipatory bail, involving offence\npunishable under Sections 109/ 112(2)/ 121 / 132/296 of B.N.S,\n2023 read with Section 3 of Orissa Prevention of Gambling Act,\n1954, in G.R. Case No.1946 of 2026 in the Court of learned\nJ.M.F.C.(R) (Cog.), Berhampur arising out of Berhampur Sadar\nP.S. Case No.616 of 2026.\n4. Learned counsel for the Petitioner, at the outset, submitted\nPage 1 of 3.\n\nthat the Petitioner does not want to press this bail application and\nseek liberty to surrender before the court below and move an\napplication for bail.\n5. Considering such submissions, the Petitioner is permitted to\nsurrender before the learned court in seisin over the matter within a\nperiod of three weeks from today and move an application for bail.\nIn such eventuality, learned court in seisin over the matter shall\nrelease the Petitioner on bail subject to such terms and conditions\nas the learned Magistrate may deem just and proper. While\nimposing condition, learned court below shall impose a condition\nthat the Petitioner shall appear before the jurisdictional Police\nStation once in a month, preferably, on ‘Sunday’ in between 10.00\nA.M. to 1 P.M., for a period four months, thereafter, once in a\nmonth for a period of three months. Violation of any of the terms\nand conditions shall entail cancellation of the bail.\n6. It is further directed that the bail granted to the Petitioner\nshall be subject to the verification of his criminal antecedent and\nthe injury report of the injured. In the event, the Petitioner is\nhaving more than two criminal antecedents and the injured person\nhas sustained any grievous injury, then this order shall stand\nautomatically revoked.\n7. It is further directed that the bail granted to the Petitioner\nshall be subject to depositing a cash security of Rs.3,000/- (Rupees\nThree Thousand) before the learned Court in seisin over the matter,\nwhich shall be kept in any Nationalized bank in interest bearing\naccount initially for a period of one year which will be renewable\nfrom time to time till conclusion of trial and the same shall be\nabide by the final outcome of the trial of the case.\nPage 2 of 3.\n\n8. The ABLAPL is disposed of accordingly.\nUrgent certified copy of this order be granted as per rules.\n.\n( A.K. Mohapatra)\nVacation Judge\nAnil\nPage 3 of 3.	3	t	ODHC010808702026	Judicial Precedent	2026-10-23	Single Bench	Represented by Adv. - Sujit Kumar Pattnaik	State Of Odisha	\N	\N	Civil & Constitutional Law	In this matter, the High Court of Orissa at Cuttack adjudicated issues between Represented by Adv. - Sujit Kumar Pattnaik and State Of Odisha. The Court rendered a decision disposing of the application under statutory provisions.	0	2026 LexGuard (OHC) E9631DA8	{"court": "High Court of Orissa at Cuttack", "title": "Represented by Adv. - Sujit Kumar Pattnaik v. State Of Odisha", "case_id": "e9631da8-860d-4602-8252-d73bfcd7893f", "case_no": "NO. 12099 of 2026", "parties": "Represented by Adv. - Sujit Kumar Pattnaik v. State Of Odisha", "category": "BAIL_SUSPENSION", "petitioner": "Represented by Adv. - Sujit Kumar Pattnaik", "respondent": "State Of Odisha", "legal_domain": "Civil & Constitutional Law", "category_facts": {"category": "BAIL_SUSPENSION", "surety_count": null, "custody_period": null, "application_type": "Anticipatory Bail", "bail_bond_amount": null, "trial_court_fine": null, "reason_for_relief": null, "reporting_condition": "appear before the jurisdictional Police", "trial_court_sentence": null, "trial_court_fine_paid": false}, "activity_events": [], "profile_version": "2.5", "statutory_matrix": [], "activity_clusters": [], "scenario_clusters": [], "scenario_keywords": [], "procedural_posture": {"remedy": "Disposed", "disposition": "Disposed"}}
