rabhakaran\nFor Respondent: Mr.A.R.Balaji\nGovernment Advocate\nORDER\nToday, on this Court taking up the contempt petition for hearing, it is\nbrought to the notice of this Court that the Division Bench vide order dated\n01.10.2026 in CMP.NO.13407 of 2024 in W.A.Sr.No.78914 of 2024 while\ncondoning the delay has kept in abeyance the contempt proceedings.\n__________\nPage1 of 3\n\nCONT P No. 228 of 2026\n2. By submitting as above, learned Government Advocate appearing for\nthe respondents has placed before this Court, a copy of the order passed by the\nHon’ble Division Bench.\n3. Since, the order which is the subject matter of the present contempt\npetition, is a subject matter of the writ appeal and the Division Bench of this\nCourt having kept in abeyance the contempt proceedings, this Court is of the\nview that by keeping the contempt proceedings pending till adjudication of writ\nappeal, no useful purpose would be served.\n4. Accordingly, the contempt petition is closed. However, liberty is\ngranted to the petitioner to revive the contempt petition after disposal of the writ\nappeal if cause continues.\n09-10-2026\nIndex: Yes/No\nSpeaking/Non-speaking order\nNeutral Citation: Yes/No\nMSV\nTo\nS.Elanselvi\nJoint Registrar of the Cooperative Society,\nThe Cuddalore District Central\nCooperative Bank Ltd,\nNo.1, Beach Road,\nCuddalore - 607 001\n__________\nPage2 of 3\n\nCONT P No. 228 of 2026\nT.VINOD KUMAR, J.\nMSV\nCONT P No. 228 of 2026\n09-10-2026\n__________\nPage3 of 3	3	t	HCMA013126442025	Writ Petition	2026-10-09	Single Bench	E.Sivagamasundari	S.Elanselvi	Mr.R. Prabhakaran	Mr.A.R.Balaji Government Advocate	Constitutional Law	In this judgment under Civil Law, the Court ruled on the dispute between 04 Cont-P-228-2026 and the Respondent.	0	2026 LexGuard (Judg) EAAF80	{"court": "Madras High Court (Principal Seat, Chennai)", "title": "E.Sivagamasundari v. S.Elanselvi", "case_id": "eaaf80d4-bd27-4116-8289-f8c7bba6c1af", "case_no": "WP.No.15163 of 2020", "parties