)\n\nSTATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:\nConstitution of India, Territorial Waters, Continental Shelf, Exclusive Economic Zone and other Maritime Zones Act 1976\n\nSECTIONS & PROVISIONS:\nArticle 21, Maritime Zones Act Section 6\n\nKEY TOPICS & ISSUES:\nTraditional Fishing Rights, Palk Strait, Maritime Boundary, Livelihood Protection, Diplomatic Retrieval\n\n================================================================================\n                                   JUDGMENT\n================================================================================\n\n1. FACTS OF THE CASE:\nArtisanal fishermen from Rameswaram had 68 mechanized trawlers impounded across International Maritime Boundary Line.\n\n2. ISSUES FRAMED:\nDoes continuous deprivation of means of maritime livelihood trigger State's constitutional obligation to protect citizens abroad?\n\n3. LEGAL RATIO & FINDINGS:\nRight to livelihood under Article 21 imposes affirmative obligation on the Union to protect citizens' occupational survival through diplomatic channels.\n\n4. FINAL ORDER:\nWrit Petition Allowed; Central Government directed to expedite diplomatic retrieval of seized mechanized fishing trawlers.\n\nOrdered and decreed accordingly.\n\nHon'ble Justice M.S. Ramesh & Justice M. Nirmal Kumar\nMadras High Court (Madurai Bench)\n[LEXGUARD REPOSITORY CRYPTOGRAPHIC SEAL]\n	3	t	HCMD010081902026	Writ Petition	\N	Single Bench	Rameswaram Traditional Fishermen Association	Union of India & 3 Ors.	\N	\N	Constitutional Law	In this writ petition under Constitutional Law, the Court ruled on the dispute between Rameswaram Traditional Fishermen Association and Union of India & 3 Ors..	0	2026 LexGuard (Writ) C1F8E9	{"court": "Madras High Court (Madurai Bench)", "title": "Rameswaram Traditional Fishermen Association v. Union of India & 3 Ors.", "case_id": "c1f8e9ff-abf4-4962-b048-7fc0bd4c6287", "case_no": "W.P.(MD) No. 8190 of 2026", "parties": "Rameswaram Traditional Fishermen Welfare Association", "category": "GENERAL