ca51bebc-acd7-4a31-8854-ebb79e358363	NO. 11962 of 2026	Represented by Adv. – Mr. Pradeep Kumar Das v. State of Odisha	High Court of Orissa at Cuttack	2026	Hon'ble MR. JUSTICE ADITYA KUMAR MOHAPATRA	Represented by Adv. – Mr. Pradeep Kumar Das v. State of Odisha	["Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023", "of BNS"]	["Section 310(4) of BNS", "Section 310(5) of BNS"]	["civil & constitutional law", "ohc", "disposed"]	Judgment in NO. 11962 of 2026 delivered by Hon'ble MR. JUSTICE ADITYA KUMAR MOHAPATRA at High Court of Orissa at Cuttack. The proceedings concern Civil & Constitutional Law with respect to Section 482.	Disposed	storage/cases/OHC_2026_NO_11962_of_2026_ca51bebc.pdf	e73edc1cb30cc09ed6ddc0b32d2220cb6a62f0329364c12908669f7e046396f8	\N	\N	\N	published	657396f3-5181-4922-8323-72d78b963be0	657396f3-5181-4922-8323-72d78b963be0	2026-10-25 14:51:30.604863+05:30	2026-10-25 14:51:30.604866+05:30	2026-10-26 10:38:09.82954+05:30	23.10.2026 Order No. 01. 1. This matter is taken up through Hybrid mode. 2. Heard learned counsel for the Petitioner as well as learned Additional Standing Counsel appearing for the State-Opposite Party. Perused the Anticipatory Bail Application as well as the F.I.R.	[]	Holding and principles affirmed in NO. 11962 of 2026 regarding Civil & Constitutional Law. The Court adjudicated upon Section 482.	[]	Disposed	[]	\N	unverified	Good Law (Binding Precedent)	IN THE HIGH COURT OF ORISSA AT CUTTACK\nABLAPL No.11962 of 2026\nCNR No. ODHC010796332026\nSk. Niyaz Quadri @ Sk. Muna ..... Petitioner\nRepresented by Adv. –\nMr. Pradeep Kumar Das\n-versus-\nState of Odisha ..... Opposite Party\nRepresented by Adv. –\nMr. Aurobinda Mohanty,\nASC\nCORAM:\nMR. JUSTICE ADITYA KUMAR MOHAPATRA\nORDER\n23.10.2026\nOrder No.\n01. 1. This matter is taken up through Hybrid mode.\n2. Heard learned counsel for the Petitioner as well as learned\nAdditional Standing Counsel appearing for the State-Opposite\nParty. Perused the Anticipatory Bail Application as well as the\nF.I.R.\n3. The present application has been filed under Section 482\nof B.N.S.S., 2023 by the Petitioner seeking pre-arrest bail in\nconnection with Puruna Bazar P.S. Case No.49 of 2026,\ncorresponding to G.R. Case No.69 of 2026, pending in the court\nof the learned Sub-Divisional Judicial Magistrate, Bhadrak,\nregistered for alleged commission of offences punishable under\nSections 310(4)/310(5) of BNS, 2023.\nPage 1 of 1.\n\n4. Learned counsel for the Petitioner, at the outset, submitted\nthat the Petitioner does not want to press this bail application\nand seeks liberty to surrender before the court below and move\nan application for bail.\n5. Considering such submissions, the Petitioner is permitted\nto surrender before the court in seisin over the matter within a\nperiod of four weeks from today and move an application for\nbail. In such eventuality, the court in seisin over the matter\nshall release the Petitioner on bail on such terms and conditions\nas it may deem just and proper in the facts and circumstances of\nthe case, but subject to verification of criminal antecedent of the\nPetitioner. In the event it is found by the court below that the\nPetitioner is having more than one criminal antecedent, then this\norder shall automatically stand revoked.\n6. Accordingly, the ABLAPL is disposed of.\nUrgent certified copy of this order be granted on proper\napplication.\n( Aditya Kumar Mohapatra )\nVacation Judge\nDebasis\nPage 2 of 2.	2	t	ODHC010796332026	Judicial Precedent	2026-10-23	Single Bench	Represented by Adv. – Mr. Pradeep Kumar Das	State of Odisha	\N	\N	Civil & Constitutional Law	In this matter, the High Court of Orissa at Cuttack adjudicated issues between Represented by Adv. – Mr. Pradeep Kumar Das and State of Odisha. The Court rendered a decision disposing of the application under statutory provisions.	0	2026 LexGuard (OHC) CA51BEBC	{"court": "High Court of Orissa at Cuttack", "title": "Represented by Adv. – Mr. Pradeep Kumar Das v. State of Odisha", "case_id":