otection of Tanks and Eviction of Encroachment Act 2007, Constitution of India\n\nSECTIONS & PROVISIONS:\nTN Act 8 of 2007 Section 7, Article 21, Article 48A, Article 51A(g)\n\nKEY TOPICS & ISSUES:\nWater Body Protection, Encroachment Removal, Public Trust Doctrine, Ecological Balance, Wetlands\n\n================================================================================\n                                   JUDGMENT\n================================================================================\n\n1. FACTS OF THE CASE:\nLake catchment area measuring 45 acres was reclassified and encroached by commercial logistics park.\n\n2. ISSUES FRAMED:\nCan government authorities regularize or reclassify water spread areas for industrial or commercial layouts?\n\n3. LEGAL RATIO & FINDINGS:\nState holds all water bodies in public trust; no government authority has jurisdiction to reclassify water bodies or regularize catchment encroachments.\n\n4. FINAL ORDER:\nWrit Petition Allowed; Encroachments in lake water-spread area ordered removed within 60 days.\n\nOrdered and decreed accordingly.\n\nHon'ble Acting Chief Justice & Justice D. Bharatha Chakravarthy\nMadras High Court (Principal Seat, Chennai)\n[LEXGUARD REPOSITORY CRYPTOGRAPHIC SEAL]\n	3	t	HCMA010245102026	Writ Petition	\N	Single Bench	Citizens Waterbody Protection Forum	District Collector & 4 Ors.	\N	\N	Constitutional Law	In this writ petition under Constitutional Law, the Court ruled on the dispute between Citizens Waterbody Protection Forum and District Collector & 4 Ors..	0	2026 LexGuard (Writ) E003B5	{"court": "Madras High Court (Principal Seat, Chennai)", "title": "Citizens Waterbody Protection Forum v. District Collector & 4 Ors.", "case_id": "e003b57d-f087-4139-aa7e-b1c8622e771d", "case_no": "W.P. No. 24510 of 2026", "parties": "Citizens Waterbody Protection Forum", "category": "GENERAL_CONSTITUTIONAL", "petitioner": "Citizens Waterbody Protection Forum", "respondent": "District Collector & 4 Ors.", "legal_d