ndent No. 4 to undertake and complete the demarcation of his land\nmeasuring 10 Kanals falling under survey Nos. 476, 490 and 489, situated\nat Gurah Brahamana, Jammu.\n2. Learned counsel for the petitioner submits that despite the petitioner has\nfiled number of representations for carrying out the demarcation of land in\nquestion but respondents had failed to perform their statutory duties.\n3. The learned counsel for the petitioner submits that he will be satisfied in\ncase the respondents are directed to demarcate the land in question in\naccordance with law.\n4. At this stage, Ms. Sagira Jaffar, Advocate appearing vice Mrs. Monika\nKohli, Sr. AAG entered appearance on behalf of the respondents, who is\nnot averse to the prayer made by the learned counsel for the petitioner.\n5. In view of the submissions made, the writ petition is taken on board and is\ndisposed of with a direction to the respondents, particularly, respondent\n\n2 WP (C) No. 3369/2026\nNo. 4 to carry out the demarcation of the land measuring 10 Kanals falling\nunder survey Nos. 476, 490 and 489, situated at Gurah Brahamana,\nJammu, strictly in accordance with Chapter-IX of the Land Revenue Act.\nLet this exercise be completed within a period of six weeks from the date\na copy of this order is made available to the respondents.\n6. Disposed of, alongwith connected application.\n(Shahzad Azeem)\nJudge\nJammu\n23.10.2026\nMahavir	2	t	JKHC010000072026	Matter	2026-10-23	Single Bench	Advocate	UT of J&K and others	\N	\N	Civil & Constitutional Law	In this matter, the High Court of Jammu & Kashmir and Ladakh adjudicated issues between Chander Rekha Through: Mr. Aman Bhagotra, Advocate and UT of J&K and others. The Court rendered a decision disposing of the application under statutory provisions.	0	2026 LexGuard (JKHC) E1183602	{"court": "High Court of Jammu & Kashmir and Ladakh", "title": "Chander Rekha Through: Mr. Aman Bhagotra, Advocate v. UT of J&K and others", "case_id": "e1183602-cf19-4eae-85b8-4c