NS & ACTS REFERRED:\nIndian Penal Code, Code of Criminal Procedure 1973, Constitution of India\n\nSECTIONS & CLAUSES UNDER CONSIDERATION:\nIPC Section 302, CrPC Section 354(3), Article 21\n\nKEY LEGAL DOMAINS & TOPICS:\nDeath Penalty, Rarest of Rare, Commutation, Mitigating Circumstances, Reformation\n\n================================================================================\n                                   JUDGMENT\n================================================================================\n\n1. FACTUAL MATRIX:\nConvict was sentenced to death for multiple murders. High Court confirmed death sentence. Supreme Court examined psychiatric evaluation and jail conduct records.\n\n2. ISSUES FRAMED FOR ADJUDICATION:\n1. Whether possibility of reformation was adequately ruled out before imposing capital punishment?\n\n3. STATUTORY FRAMEWORK & PRECEDENTS:\nManoj v. State of M.P. mandates comprehensive psychological assessment and socioeconomic report of convict before capital sentencing.\n\n4. RATIO DECIDENDI:\nDeath sentence cannot be confirmed unless prosecution conclusively proves by cogent material that convict is incapable of reformation.\n\n5. FINAL DISPOSITION & ORDER:\nCriminal Appeal Partly Allowed; Death sentence commuted to 25 years imprisonment without remission.\n\nDecreed and ordered accordingly.\n\nHon'ble Chief Justice of India & Justice B.R. Gavai & Justice Surya Kant\nSupreme Court of India\n[LEXGUARD CRYPTOGRAPHIC VERIFIED REPOSITORY RECORD]\n	3	t	SCIN010001022026	Criminal Appeal	\N	Single Bench	Vikas Yadav	State of Uttar Pradesh	\N	\N	Civil Law	In this criminal appeal under Criminal Law, the Court ruled on the dispute between Vikas Yadav and State of Uttar Pradesh.	0	2026 LexGuard (Crim) E63402	{"court": "Supreme Court of India", "title": "Vikas Yadav v. State of Uttar Pradesh", "case_id": "e634027c-520f-4994-a3c3-b8ebf9aad412", "case_no": "Crl.A. No. 102 of 2026", "parties": "Vikas Yadav", "category": "GENERAL_CONSTITUTIONAL", "petitione