 Section 3, Employee's Compensation Act Section 4\n\nKEY TOPICS & ISSUES:\nWorkmen Compensation, Functional Disability, Total Incapacity, Employment Injury, Occupational Hazard\n\n================================================================================\n                                   JUDGMENT\n================================================================================\n\n1. FACTS OF THE CASE:\nQuarry blaster suffered right arm amputation. Insurance company argued medical board assessed physical disability at only 65%.\n\n2. ISSUES FRAMED:\nShould compensation be assessed on medical physical disability or functional loss of earning capacity?\n\n3. LEGAL RATIO & FINDINGS:\nFunctional disability must be assessed based on the specific vocational work performed by the workman; 65% physical disability equals 100% functional loss.\n\n4. FINAL ORDER:\nCivil Miscellaneous Appeal Dismissed; 100% loss of earning capacity upheld for quarry blaster suffering limb amputation.\n\nOrdered and decreed accordingly.\n\nHon'ble Justice R. Vijayakumar\nMadras High Court (Madurai Bench)\n[LEXGUARD REPOSITORY CRYPTOGRAPHIC SEAL]\n	3	t	HCMD010014502026	Civil Miscellaneous Appeal	\N	Single Bench	The Divisional Manager, New India Assurance	Veluchamy	\N	\N	Civil Law	In this civil miscellaneous appeal under Civil Law, the Court ruled on the dispute between The Divisional Manager, New India Assurance and Veluchamy.	0	2026 LexGuard (Civi) F233EE	{"court": "Madras High Court (Madurai Bench)", "title": "The Divisional Manager, New India Assurance v. Veluchamy", "case_id": "f233ee4d-85ce-4d6c-a497-038225e4630a", "case_no": "C.M.A.(MD) No. 1450 of 2026", "parties": "The Divisional Manager, New India Assurance Co. Ltd.", "category": "GENERAL_CONSTITUTIONAL", "petitioner": "The Divisional Manager, New India Assurance", "respondent": "Veluchamy", "legal_domain": "Civil Law", "category_facts": {"category": "GENERAL_CONSTITUTIONAL", "remedy_type": "Writ Petition / Criminal Appeal", "judi