eddy, I.F.S.,\nThe Principal Chief Conservator of Forests,\n(Head of Forest Force),\nPanagal Buildings, Saidapet,\nChennai - 600 015.\nNow at Velachery Main Road,\nGuindy, Chennai – 32.\n3.Thiru.M.G.Ganesan, I.F.S.,\nThe Deputy Director,\nMudumalai Tiger Reserve Forest,\nNilgiris.\n..Contemnor(s)\nPrayer: Contempt Petition is filed under Section 11 of Contempt of Court Act,\n1971, to punish the respondents for their willfull disobedience in not complying\nwith the order dated 10.11.2025 passed by this Court in W.P.No.2939 of 2019.\nFor Petitioner(s): Mr.S.Mani\n__________\nPage1 of 4\n\nCONT P No. 3254 of 2026\nFor Contemnor(s): Mr.S.Seenuvsan\nGovernment Advocate\nORDER\nWhen the contempt petition is taken up for hearing, the learned\nGovernment Advocate appearing for the respondents submits that the\nrespondents have complied with the order of this Court in W.P.No.2939 of 2019\ndated 10.11.2025, by issuing G.O.2(D).No.153 Environment, Climate Change\nand Forests (FR.2(ii)) Department, dated 07.10.2026, granting permission to\ninclude the name of the petitioner in the State-wise seniority list for promotion\nto the post of Plot Watchers/Social Forestry Workers based on his initial\nappointment and also to appoint him as Forest Watcher as per the Rules,\neligibility and seniority, subject to the outcome of the writ appeal.\n2. By submitting as above, the learned Government Advocate has placed\nbefore this Court a copy of the aforesaid G.O. The same is taken on record.\n3. In view of the above submission and the facts as noted herein above,\nthe Government having issued the Government Order granting seniority to the\npetitioner and also directing for the appointment of the petitioner to the post of\nPlot Watcher, the respondents have substantially complied with the order of this\nCourt and thus, there is no necessity to proceed further with the present\n__________\nPage2 of 4\n\nCONT P No. 3254 of 2026\ncontempt petition.\nAccordingly, this Contempt Petition is closed. No order as to costs.\n09-10-2026\nIndex: Yes/No\nSpeaking/Non-speaking order\nNeutral Citation: Yes/No\ndh\nTo\n1. Tmt. Supriya Sahu, IAS.,\nSecretary to Government,\nEnvironment and Forest Department,\nFort St.George, Chennai - 600 009.\n2. Thiru.Srinivas R.Reddy, I.F.S.,\nThe Principal Chief Conservator of Forests,\n(Head of Forest Force),\nPanagal Buildings, Saidapet,\nChennai - 600 015.\nNow at Velachery Main Road,\nGuindy, Chennai – 32.\n3. Thiru.M.G.Ganesan, I.F.S.,\nThe Deputy Director,\nMudumalai Tiger Reserve Forest,\nNilgiris.\n__________\nPage3 of 4\n\nCONT P No. 3254 of 2026\nT.VINOD KUMAR, J.\ndh\nCONT.P No. 3254 of 2026\n09-10-2026\n__________\nPage4 of 4	4	t	HCMA011880622026	Writ Petition	2026-10-09	Single Bench	M.Vishnu	1.Tmt. Supriya Sahu, IAS.,	Mr.S.Mani	\N	Constitutional Law	In this judgment under Civil Law, the Court ruled on the dispute between 07 Cont-P-3254-2026 and the Respondent.	0	2026 LexGuard (Judg) F7DD3C	{"court": "Madras High Court (Principal Seat, Chennai)", "title": "M.Vishnu v. 1.Tmt. Supriya Sahu, IAS.,", "case_id": "f7dd3c3f-4427-4f6d-84c9-6555add85cd4", "case_no": "W.P.No.2939 of 2019", "parties": "07 Cont-P-3254-2026", "category": "GENERAL_CONSTITUTIONAL", "petitioner": "M.Vishnu", "respondent": "1.Tmt. Supriya Sahu, IAS.,", "legal_domain": "Constitutional Law", "category_facts": {"category": "GENERAL_CONSTITUTIONAL", "remedy_type": "Writ Petition / Criminal Appeal", "judicial_disposition": "Dismissed", "constitutional_article": "Article 226 / Article 21"}, "activity_events": [], "profile_version": "2.5", "statutory_matrix": [], "activity_clusters": [], "scenario_clusters": [], "scenario_keywords": [], "procedural_posture": {"remedy": "Allowed", "disposition": "Allowed"}}
