f8eedab4-a9db-4d24-9ca3-c810d5168a25	NO. 290/2026	PETITIONER v. M/S UMIYA HOLDING PVT LTD REP BY ITS AUTHORISED	High Court of Judicature	2026	Hon'ble ASHWIN D. BHOBE, J	PETITIONER v. M/S UMIYA HOLDING PVT LTD REP BY ITS AUTHORISED	[]	[]	["civil & constitutional law", "hc", "disposed"]	Judgment in NO. 290/2026 delivered by Hon'ble ASHWIN D. BHOBE, J at High Court of Judicature. The proceedings concern Civil & Constitutional Law with respect to procedural compliance.	Disposed	storage/cases/HC_2026_NO_290_2026_f8eedab4.pdf	948725d38ac1c3beccf97042a6dd0d259958d577345d81d03ec247df731b1c15	\N	\N	\N	published	657396f3-5181-4922-8323-72d78b963be0	657396f3-5181-4922-8323-72d78b963be0	2026-10-25 14:51:35.53443+05:30	2026-10-25 14:51:35.534434+05:30	2026-10-26 10:38:09.853609+05:30	\N	[]	Holding and principles affirmed in NO. 290/2026 regarding Civil & Constitutional Law. The Court adjudicated upon applicable judicial standards.	[]	Disposed	[]	\N	unverified	Good Law (Binding Precedent)	914-WPCR-290-2026.DOC\nSuchitra\nIN THE HIGH COURT OF BOMBAY AT GOA\nCRIMINAL WRIT PETITION NO.290/2026\nOMKAR PANDHARI NAIK\n… PETITIONER\nVersus\nM/S UMIYA HOLDING PVT\nLTD REP BY ITS AUTHORISED\nSIGNATORY\n… RESPONDENT\nMr Rohan Desai, Advocate for the Petitioner.\nCORAM: ASHWIN D. BHOBE, J.\nDATED: 23rd OCTOBER 2026\nP.C. :\n1. Heard Mr Rohan Desai, learned Advocate for the\nPetitioner.\n2. By this Petition, the Petitioner has sought for the following\nsubstantive relief in terms of prayer clause (a) which is reproduced\nin verbatim:\n“(a) Issue a writ of certiorari quashing the Impugned Order\ndated 06.01.2026.”\n3. Mr Rohan Desai, learned Advocate for the Petitioner on\ninstructions from the Petitioner seeks leave to unconditionally\nwithdraw the Petition.\n4. In view of the statement made by Mr Rohan Desai, learned\nAdvocate for the Petitioner, Criminal Writ Petition No.289/2026\nis disposed of as withdrawn.\nASHWIN D. BHOBE, J.\nPage 1 of 1\n23rd October 2026	1	t	HCMA010002902026	Judicial Precedent	2026-10-23	Single Bench	PETITIONER	M/S UMIYA HOLDING PVT LTD REP BY ITS AUTHORISED	\N	\N	Civil & Constitutional Law	In this matter, the High Court of Judicature adjudicated issues between OMKAR PANDHARI NAIK and M/S UMIYA HOLDING PVT LTD REP BY ITS AUTHORISED. The Court rendered a decision disposing of the application under statutory provisions.	0	2026 LexGuard (HC) F8EEDAB4	{"court": "High Court of Judicature", "title": "OMKAR PANDHARI NAIK v. M/S UMIYA HOLDING PVT LTD REP BY ITS AUTHORISED", "case_id": "f8eedab4-a9db-4d24-9ca3-c810d5168a25", "case_no": "NO. 290/2026", "parties": "OMKAR PANDHARI NAIK v. M/S UMIYA HOLDING PVT LTD REP BY ITS AUTHORISED", "category": "QUASHING", "petitioner": "OMKAR PANDHARI NAIK", "respondent": "M/S UMIYA HOLDING PVT LTD REP BY ITS AUTHORISED", "legal_domain": "Civil & Constitutional Law", "category_facts": {"category": "QUASHING", "civil_cloak": false, "quash_ground": "Absence of prima facie ingredients", "compromise_affidavit": false, "bhajan_lal_principles": true, "proceedings_challenged": "FIR / Investigation"}, "activity_events": [], "profile_version": "2.5", "statutory_matrix": [], "activity_clusters": [], "scenario_clusters": [], "scenario_keywords": [], "procedural_posture": {"remedy": "Disposed", "disposition": "Disposed"}}
fa710bb1-f295-47c2-bc38-d30e717d4260	NO. 25125 of 2026	VIPULKUMAR MANILAL CHAUHAN (VIPULBHAI MANILAL CHAUHAN) v. STATE OF GUJARAT	High Court of Gujarat at Ahmedabad	2026	Hon'ble Mr. Justice Sanjeev	VIPULKUMAR MANILAL CHAUHAN (VIPULBHAI MANILAL CHAUHAN) v. STATE OF GUJARAT	["Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita, 2023", "Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023", "M.V. Act", "the BNSS"]	["Section 177 M.V. Act", "Section 184 M.V. Act", "Section 483(2) the BNSS"]	["civil & constitutional law", "ghc", "disposed"]	Judgment in NO. 25125 of 2026 delivered by HONOURABLE MR.JUSTICE SANJEEV J.THAKER at High Court of Gujarat at Ahmedabad. The proceedings concern Civil & Constitutional Law with respect to Section 482.	Disposed	storage/cases/GHC_2026_NO_25125_of_2026_fa710bb1.pdf	e1bc1029944373481cd5142fd1186688948b2c14f7a48ee0d48b89eb658b896d	\N	\N	\N	published	657396f3-5181-4922-8323-72d78b963be0	657396f3-5181-4922-8323-72d78b963be0	2026-10-25 14:52:02.704565+05:30	2026-10-25 14:52:02.704573+05:30	2026-10-26 10:38:09.854683+05:30	1. By way of this application under Section 482 of the Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita, 2023 (for short, “BNSS”), the applicant has prayed for anticipatory bail in the event of arrest in connection with the FIR being C.R. No. 11200038263627 of 2026, registered with Pardi Police Station, District: Valsad for the offences punishable under Sections 65(a), 65(e), 98(2) and 116-B of the Gujarat Prohibition Act and section 281 of Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023 and section 177 and 184 of the M.V. Act. 2. Rule. Learned Additional Public Prosecutor waives service of notice of rule for respondent – State of Gujarat.	[]	Holding and principles affirmed in NO. 25125 of 2026 regarding Civil & Constitutional Law. The Court adjudicated upon Section 482.	[]	Disposed	[{"court": "Supreme Court of India", "title": "Sushila Aggarwal v. State (NCT of Delhi)", "status": "Good Law (5-Judge Constitution Bench)", "case_id": "11111111-0011-4000-8000-000000000011", "citation": "(2020) 5 SCC 1", "ratio_key": "Anticipatory bail protection endures until conclusion of trial", "treatment": "Followed / Relied Upon"}, {"court": "Supreme Court of India", "title": "Judicial Precedent [2011) 1 SCC 6941]", "status": "Good Law (External Authority)", "case_id": null, "citation": "2011) 1 SCC 6941", "treatment": "Cited / Considered"}, {"court": "Supreme Court of India", "title": "Judicial Precedent [1980) 2 SCC 665]", "status": "Good Law (External Authority)", "case_id": null, "citation": "1980) 2 SCC 665", "treatment": "Cited / Considered"}, {"court": "Supreme Court of India", "title": "Judicial Precedent [2020) 5 SCC 1]", "status": "Good Law (External Authority)", "case_id": null, "citation": "2020) 5 SCC 1", "treatment": "Cited / Considered"}]	\N	unverified	Good Law (Binding Precedent)	R/CR.MA/25125/2026 ORDER DATED: 23/10/2026\n(GJHC240807942026)\nIN THE HIGH COURT OF GUJARAT AT AHMEDABAD\nR/CRIMINAL MISC.APPLICATION (FOR ANTICIPATORY BAIL) NO. 25125\nof 2026\n================================================================\nVIPULKUMAR MANILAL CHAUHAN (VIPULBHAI MANILAL CHAUHAN)\nVersus\nSTATE OF GUJARAT\n==============================================================================\nAppearance:\nMR P P MAJMUDAR(5284) for the Applicant(s) No. 1\nMR TIRTHRAJ PANDYA, APP for the Respondent(s) No. 1\n================================================================\nCORAM:HONOURABLE MR.JUSTICE SANJEEV J.THAKER\nDate : 23/10/2026\nORAL ORDER\n1. By way of this application under Section 482 of the\nBharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita, 2023 (for short,\n“BNSS”), the applicant has prayed for anticipatory bail in the\nevent of arrest in connection with the FIR being C.R. No.\n11200038263627 of 2026, registered with Pardi Police Station,\nDistrict: Valsad for the offences punishable under Sections\n65(a), 65(e), 98(2) and 116-B of the Gujarat Prohibition Act\nand section 281 of Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023 and\nsection 177 and 184 of the M.V. Act.\n2. Rule. Learned Additional Public Prosecutor waives\nservice of notice of rule for respondent – State of Gujarat.\n3. Learned advocate for the applicant submits that the\nnature of allegations are such that custodial interrogation at\nthis stage is not necessary. It is further submitted that the\napplicant will keep himself available during the course of\ninvestigation and trial also and will not flee from justice.\nPage 1 of 5\n\nR/CR.MA/25125/2026 ORDER DATED: 23/10/2026\n(GJHC240807942026)\n3.1 The learned advocate for the applicant further states\nthat the applicant shall abide by all the conditions that may\nbe imposed while granting anticipatory bail to the applicant.\nAccordingly, it is urged that this application may be allowed\nand to grant the anticipatory bail to the applicant.\n4. As against this, the learned Additional Public Prosecutor\nappearing on behalf of the respondent – State has opposed\ngrant of anticipatory bail looking to the nature and gravity of\nthe offence and requested not to entertain this application.\n5. Having heard the learned advocates appearing for the\nparties and perusing the papers available on record, it is\nincumbent upon the Court to exercise its discretion\njudiciously, cautiously and strictly in compliance with the\nbasic principles laid down in plethora of decisions of the\nApex Court on the point. It is well settled that, among other\ncircumstances, the factors to be borne in mind while\nconsidering an application for bail are (i) the nature and\ngravity of the accusation; (ii) the antecedents of the applicant\nincluding the fact as to whether he has previously undergone\nimprisonment on conviction by a Court in respect of any\ncognizable offence; (iii) the possibility of the applicant to flee\nfrom justice; and (iv) where the accusation has been made\nwith the object of injuring or humiliating the applicant by\nPage 2 of 5\n\nR/CR.MA/25125/2026 ORDER DATED: 23/10/2026\n(GJHC240807942026)\nhaving him so arrested. Though at the stage of granting bail\nan elaborate examination of evidence and detailed reasons\ntouching the merits of the case, which may prejudice the\ncase of accused, should be avoided. However, prima facie,\nfollowing aspects have been taken into consideration:\na) the offence is/are not punishable with life\nimprisonment;\nb) the applicant has no past antecedents;\nc) the learned advocate for the applicant has assured\nthat the applicant will not flee from justice and would\nbe available during investigation as well as the trial.\n6. Considering the aforesaid aspects and the law laid down\nby the Hon’ble Apex Court in the case of Siddharam\nSatlingappa Mhetre v. State of Maharashtra and Others,\nreported in (2011) 1 SCC 6941, wherein the Hon’ble Apex\nCourt reiterated the law laid down by the Constitution Bench\nin the case of Shri Gurubaksh Singh Sibbia & Others,\nreported in (1980) 2 SCC 665 and also the decision in the\ncase of Sushila Aggarwal v. State (NCT of Delhi), reported in\n(2020) 5 SCC 1, the Court is inclined to allow the present\napplication.\nPage 3 of 5\n\nR/CR.MA/25125/2026 ORDER DATED: 23/10/2026\n(GJHC240807942026)\n7. In the result, this application is allowed by directing\nthat in the event of arrest/ appearance of the applicant in\nconnection with the above-referred FIR, the applicant shall be\nreleased on bail on furnishing a personal bond of Rs.10,000/-\n(Rupees Ten Thousand) with one surety of like amount on\nthe following conditions that applicant:\n(a) shall cooperate with the investigation and make\navailable for interrogation whenever required;\n(b) shall not directly or indirectly make any\ninducement, threat or promise to any person acquainted\nwith the fact of the case so as to dissuade him from\ndisclosing such facts to the court or to any police\nofficer;\n(c) shall not obstruct or hamper the police\ninvestigation and not to play mischief with the evidence\ncollected or yet to be collected by the police;\n(d) shall remain present at the concerned Police\nStation on 30.10.2026 between 11.00 a.m. and 2.00 p.m.;\n(e) shall at the time of execution of bond, furnish the\naddress to the investigating officer and the court\nconcerned and shall not change residence till the final\ndisposal of the case till further orders;\n(f) shall not leave India without the permission of the\nCourt and if having passport shall deposit the same\nPage 4 of 5\n\nR/CR.MA/25125/2026 ORDER DATED: 23/10/2026\n(GJHC240807942026)\nbefore the trial Court within a week;\n(g) It is open to the police or the investigating agency\nor the complainant to move the learned trial Court for\na direction under Section 483(2) of the BNSS to arrest\nthe accused, in the event of violation of any term, such\nas absconding, non-cooperating during investigation,\nevasion, intimidation or inducement to witnesses with a\nview to influence outcome of the investigation or trial,\netc.\n7.1 At the trial, the Trial Court shall not be influenced by\nthe prima facie observations made by this Court while\nconsidering the bail application.\n8. It is made clear that this order of anticipatory bail does\nnot in any manner limit or restrict the rights or duties of\nthe police or investigative agency to investigate into the\ncharges against the applicant who is granted pre-arrest bail.\n9. Rule is made absolute to the aforesaid extent. Direct\nservice is permitted.\n(SANJEEV J.THAKER,J)\nManoj Kumar Rai\nPage 5 of 5	5	t	GJHC240807942026	Judicial Precedent	2026-10-23	Single Bench	VIPULKUMAR MANILAL CHAUHAN (VIPULBHAI MANILAL CHAUHAN)	STATE OF GUJARAT	\N	– State of Gujarat. 3. Learned advocate for the applicant submits that the	Civil & Constitutional Law	In this matter, the High Court of Gujarat at Ahmedabad adjudicated issues between VIPULKUMAR MANILAL CHAUHAN (VIPULBHAI MANILAL CHAUHAN) and STATE OF GUJARAT. The Court rendered a decision disposing of the application under statutory provisions.	0	2026 LexGuard (GHC) FA710BB1	{"court": "High Court of Gujarat at Ahmedabad", "tit