\nPrevention of Corruption, Demand and Acceptance, Trap Witness, Circumstantial Proof, Shadow Witness\n\n================================================================================\n                                   JUDGMENT\n================================================================================\n\n1. FACTS OF THE CASE:\nClarification sought on whether demand and acceptance in bribery cases can be inferred purely on shadow witness testimony without complainant.\n\n2. ISSUES FRAMED:\nWhat standard of circumstantial evidence suffices to prove demand and acceptance when primary complainant is hostile or deceased?\n\n3. LEGAL RATIO & FINDINGS:\nDemand and acceptance of illegal gratification can be proved by circumstantial evidence, but evidence must lead to sole inference of guilt.\n\n4. FINAL ORDER:\nReview Clarified; Corroboration of demand and acceptance through circumstantial evidence must satisfy chain of proof.\n\nOrdered and decreed accordingly.\n\nHon'ble Constitution Bench (5 Judges)\nSupreme Court of India\n[LEXGUARD REPOSITORY CRYPTOGRAPHIC SEAL]\n	3	t	SCIN010007102026	Criminal Appeal	\N	Single Bench	Neeraj Dutta (Review)	State (Govt. of NCT of Delhi)	\N	\N	Civil Law	In this criminal appeal under Civil Law, the Court ruled on the dispute between Neeraj Dutta (Review) and State (Govt. of NCT of Delhi).	0	2026 LexGuard (Crim) FDCC77	{"court": "Supreme Court of India", "title": "Neeraj Dutta (Review) v. State (Govt. of NCT of Delhi)", "case_id": "fdcc77b7-8838-496c-98a6-a1602cb09388", "case_no": "Crl.A. No. 710 of 2026", "parties": "Neeraj Dutta", "category": "GENERAL_CONSTITUTIONAL", "petitioner": "Neeraj Dutta (Review)", "respondent": "State (Govt. of NCT of Delhi)", "legal_domain": "Civil Law", "category_facts": {"category": "GENERAL_CONSTITUTIONAL", "remedy_type": "Criminal Appeal Against Conviction", "judicial_disposition": "Dismissed", "constitutional_article": "Article 226 / Article 21"}, "activity_events": [], "profile_version": "2.5", "s